 : markdown\nhas_design : True\nnotes : New design (no needs-revision). No sibling designs existed; conventions established here for Python/FastAPI+Uvicorn, SQLite WAL at /app/data/huddle.sqlite, Redis pub/sub-only on :6379, node_id↔port map. Keep label backend for implementer routing after architect approval removes architect.\ncreated_at : 2026-08-22T22:16:49.780466332Z\nupdated_at : 2026-08-22T22:23:05.621229081Z\ncreated_by : marathon-harness\ndescription : Create /app/start.sh that stays in the foreground and keeps the cluster serving while alive. Launch three HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000, :8001, :8002 and a local redis-server on 127.0.0.1:6379. Self-contained (no remote services, no DinD). Respawning: if an HTTP node is SIGKILLed it must come back within 60s without external action; if Redis is SIGKILLed, start.sh must respawn it. Stub GET / on each node and GET /api/health returning 200 {status:ok, node_id} with node_id 0/1/2 matching ports 8000\ndependents : list\n","stderr":"","executionTime":106,"interleavedOutput":"Add a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n\nUsage:\n  loom data comment <issue-id> <text> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --author string   Comment author (defaults to server-side session user)\n  -h, --help            help for comment\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n  -o, --output string       Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string       Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\nid : MARATHON-2\ntitle : Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis\nstatus : in_progress\npriority : 0\nissue_type : task\nassignee : backend-dev-1\nowner : marathon-harness\nlabels : list\nsource_repo : app\nparent : MARATHON-1\ndesign_f