{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-142aa07a-289d-4349-a168-b9ace95e2425-10\nfc_6ad3dc34-c7c1-9075-ba6f-369a5b543036_4","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-3 --output json 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json,re\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d['design']\n# extract schema / migration / data model sections\nfor m in re.finditer(r'## .+?\\n', design):\n  print(m.group().strip())\nprint('---SCHEMA SECTION---')\nidx=design.find('Data Model')\nprint(design[idx:idx+4000] if idx>=0 else 'no Data Model')\nprint('---IMPL---')\nidx=design.find('Implementation')\nprint(design[idx:idx+3500] if idx>=0 else 'no Implementation')\n\"","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-142aa07a-289d-4349-a168-b9ace95e2425-10\nfc_6ad3dc34-c7c1-9075-ba6f-369a5b543036_4","simpleCommands":["loom","python3"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-3"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-3 --output json"},{"name":"python3","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"string","value":"\"\nimport sys,json,re\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d['design']\n# extract schema / migration / data model sections\nfor m in re.finditer(r'## .+?\\n', design):\n  print(m.group().strip())\nprint('---SCHEMA SECTION---')\nidx=design.find('Data Model')\nprint(design[idx:idx+4000] if idx>=0 else 'no Data Model')\nprint('---IMPL---')\nidx=design.find('Implementation')\nprint(design[idx:idx+3500] if idx>=0 else 'no Implementation')\n\""}],"fullText":"python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json,re\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d['design']\n# extract schema / migration / data model sections\nfor m in re.finditer(r'## .+?\\n', design):\n  print(m.group().strip())\nprint('---SCHEMA SECTION---')\nidx=design.find('Data Model')\nprint(design[idx:idx+4000] if idx>=0 else 'no Data Model')\nprint('---IMPL---')\nidx=design.find('Implementation')\nprint(design[idx:idx+3500] if idx>=0 else 'no Implementation')\n\""}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Extract design schema and impl sections","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"3eccf520-9b37-480c-8b6e-626d40d089c1","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-3 --output json 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json,re\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d['design']\n# extract schema / migration / data model sections\nfor m in re.finditer(r'## .+?\\n', design):\n  print(m.group().strip())\nprint('---SCHEMA SECTION---')\nidx=design.find('Data Model')\nprint(design[idx:idx+4000] if idx>=0 else 'no Data Model')\nprint('---IMPL---')\nidx=design.find('Implementation')\nprint(design[idx:idx+3500] if idx>=0 else 'no Implementation')\n\"","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"## Summary\n## Technical Approach\n## Decision\n## Why\n## Alternatives considered\n## Trade-off accepted\n## Conventions inherited from MARATHON-2 (must not diverge)\n## Interface Contracts\n## Shared types (frontend ↔ backend)\n## `UserObj`\n## Error envelope (all Auth errors; convention for later REST)\n## Username validation (server owns; client should mirror for UX)\n## Password validation (server owns)\n## Bearer header\n## `POST /api/auth/register`\n## `POST /api/auth/login`\n## `GET /api/auth/me`\n## Seam: Auth dependency for sibling tasks\n## Seam: Cluster identity\n## Data Model\n## Migration version 1\n## Table `users`\n## Table `auth_tokens`\n## Password hash string format (normative for implementers)\n## Token generation\n## Schema change summary\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n## Create\n## Modify\n## Do not touch\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n## Build order (single implementer)\n## Downstream seams this task owns\n## Upstream dependency\n## Must land before\n## Suggested follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n## Acceptance Criteria\n## Testing Strategy\n## Automated (implementer)\n## Manual / cluster verification\n## Human checks\n---SCHEMA SECTION---\nData Model\n\n### Migration version 1\n\nApplied via `schema_migrations` after version 0 bootstrap from MARATHON-2. **Backward compatible** with empty product schema (additive). On existing DBs with only version 0, migrate forward once.\n\n#### Table `users`\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | PK, UUID4 string |\n| `username` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UNIQUE |\n| `password_hash` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Encoded scrypt parameters + salt + hash (single string; document format in module docstring) |\n| `display_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| `timezone` | TEXT | NULL | |\n| `avatar_url` | TEXT | NULL | |\n| `status_text` | TEXT | NULL | |\n| `status_emoji` | TEXT | NULL | |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UTC ISO-8601 with `Z` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) |\n| `updated_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Same format; set on create |\n\nIndexes: `UNIQUE(username)`.\n\n#### Table `auth_tokens`\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `token_hash` | TEXT | NOT NULL | PK; hex SHA-256 of raw token |\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → `users.id` ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UTC `Z` |\n\nIndex: `user_id` (for future revoke-all).\n\n**No Redis keys** for auth. **No email column.**\n\n### Password hash string format (normative for implementers)\n\nStore one TEXT value, e.g. `scrypt$N=2^14$r=8$p=1$<salt_b64>$<hash_b64>` (exact parameter tuning may vary but must be stable and verified on login). Salt ≥ 16 bytes from `secrets`.\n\n### Token generation\n\n- Raw token: `secrets.token_urlsafe(32)` (always length ≥ 16).\n- Persist only `hashlib.sha256(raw_token.encode(\"ascii\")).hexdigest()`.\n- Compare presented token by hashing then PK lookup (constant-time compare optional once looked up by hash).\n\n### Schema change summary\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| Add `users`, `auth_tokens`; insert migration version 1 | Yes — additive on greenfield / version 0 DBs |\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/__init__.py` | Package marker; optionally re-export router + `get_current_user`. |\n| `server/auth/passwords.py` | Hash / verify helpers (`scrypt`). |\n| `server/auth/tokens.py` | Mint raw token; hash; insert row; resolve hash → `user_id`. |\n| `server/auth/users.py` | Create user; fetch by id/username; map row → `UserObj` dict. |\n| `server/auth/deps.py` | `get_current_user` FastAPI dependency; 401 envelope helper. |\n| `server/auth/routes.py` | `APIRouter` with register / login / me. |\n| `server/errors.py` | Small helper to build `JSONResponse` error envelopes (shared). |\n| `tests/test_auth.py` | Contract tests: register 201, duplicate 409, validation 400, login 200/401, me 200/401, cross-DB identity (same sqlite path / TestClient). |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/db.py` | Add `migrate(conn)` / `ensure_schema(sqlite_path)` applying version 1 DDL; keep existing bootstrap. Prefer a list of `(version, sql_callable)` migrations. Expose `connect(sqlite_path) -> Connection` used by auth (WAL pragmas every time). |\n| `server/app.py` | Call full schema ensure on lifespan (not only bootstrap); `include_router` auth routes; leave `/api/health` and stub `GET /` unchanged. |\n| `requirements.txt` | **No new dependencies required** if using stdlib crypto + uuid. Do not add Redis usage for auth. |\n| `tests/test_health.py` | Only if lifespan/migration changes break bootstrap assertions — keep health unauthenticated; do not weaken existing checks. |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `start.sh` | Supervisor already shares `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`; no auth-specific change |\n| `server/settings.py` | Already exposes sqlite path |\n| `timer.sh`, `loom-prompts/**` | Harness |\n| SPA / `GET /` HTML | MARATHON-16 |\n| Profile PATCH routes | MARATHON-4 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order (single implementer)\n\n1. `server/errors.py` + `db.py` migration v1.\n2. `passwords.py` / `tokens.\n---IMPL---\nno Implementation\n","stderr":"","executionTime":116,"interleavedOutput":"## Summary\n## Technical Approach\n## Decision\n## Why\n## Alternatives considered\n## Trade-off accepted\n## Conventions inherited from MARATHON-2 (must not diverge)\n## Interface Contracts\n## Shared types (frontend ↔ backend)\n## `UserObj`\n## Error envelope (all Auth errors; convention for later REST)\n## Username validation (server owns; client should mirror for UX)\n## Password validation (server owns)\n## Bearer header\n## `POST /api/auth/register`\n## `POST /api/auth/login`\n## `GET /api/auth/me`\n## Seam: Auth dependency for sibling tasks\n## Seam: Cluster identity\n## Data Model\n## Migration version 1\n## Table `users`\n## Table `auth_tokens`\n## Password hash string format (normative for implementers)\n## Token generation\n## Schema change summary\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n## Create\n## Modify\n## Do not touch\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n## Build order (single implementer)\n## Downstream seams this task owns\n## Upstream dependency\n## Must land before\n## Suggested follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n## Acceptance Criteria\n## Testing Strategy\n## Automated (implementer)\n## Manual / cluster verification\n## Human checks\n-