{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-36e90b36-47ae-4ba4-b45b-7d18e8e1a54c-13\nfc_4ced65ff-b22f-94a1-9d4a-079de7bd4ec5_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/marathon-4-design.md","offset":200,"limit":200},"result":{"success":{"content":"| `status_emoji` | TEXT | NULL | PATCH |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Untouched |\n| `updated_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Set to `utc_now_z()` on any successful mutating PATCH |\n\nBackward compatible: additive behavior only; existing Auth rows remain valid.\n\n### Update SQL pattern\n\n- Build dynamic `SET` only for fields present in the validated patch dict.\n- Always set `updated_at = ?` when at least one profile column changes.\n- Single transaction; return `row_to_user_obj` of the updated row.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/users/__init__.py` | Package marker; export router. |\n| `server/users/routes.py` | `GET /{id}` and `PATCH /me` under prefix `/api/users`; `Depends(get_current_user)`. |\n| `server/events.py` | `publish_user_updated(user: dict[str, Any]) -> None` no-op (+ docstring stating MARATHON-13/14 ownership of fan-out). |\n| `tests/test_profiles.py` | Contract tests for GET/PATCH, auth, 404, validation lengths/timezone, UserObj key set, no-op PATCH, ignore immutable keys. |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/users.py` | Add profile validators + `update_user_profile(conn, user_id, patch) -> dict` (or equivalent) that UPDATEs columns and returns `UserObj`. Reuse `normalize_display_name` semantics for PATCH resets. |\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` users router; leave health, stub `/`, auth router unchanged. |\n| `server/errors.py` | Broaden validation handler to `/api/*` except `/api/health` (no-op if MARATHON-5 already did). |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/db.py` | No schema change |\n| `server/auth/routes.py`, `tokens.py`, `passwords.py`, `deps.py` | Auth complete; only consume `get_current_user` |\n| `start.sh`, `server/settings.py` | No new env |\n| `tests/test_auth.py` | Keep green; do not weaken Auth contracts (optional: one assert that PATCH’d fields appear on `/api/auth/me` can live in `test_profiles.py`) |\n| SPA / `GET /` HTML | MARATHON-16 / settings UI MARATHON-18 |\n| Redis / WebSocket server | MARATHON-13/14 |\n| File upload storage | MARATHON-10 (`avatar_url` is a string only here) |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order (single implementer)\n\n1. `server/auth/users.py` update + validators.\n2. `server/events.py` hook.\n3. `server/users/routes.py` + wire `app.py`.\n4. Broaden `errors.py` if needed.\n5. `tests/test_profiles.py`.\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Event stub and validators can proceed in parallel; routes depend on both.\n- Safe to implement **in parallel with MARATHON-5** (different routers/tables). Only shared file risk: `server/errors.py` and `server/app.py` — apply the agreed envelope rule and mount independently.\n\n### Downstream seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumed by |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `GET /api/users/{id}` → `{user}` | MARATHON-6/9/12/16/17 (member displays, DMs, mentions UI) |\n| `PATCH /api/users/me` → `{user}` | MARATHON-16/18 settings/profile forms |\n| Profile length + IANA rules | SPA client-side hints (optional); graders |\n| `user.updated` payload shape (no channel seq) | MARATHON-13 (subscribe/dispatch), MARATHON-14 (cross-node fan-out) |\n| `publish_user_updated` hook | MARATHON-13/14 replace no-op |\n\n### Upstream\n\n- **MARATHON-3** (closed): `users` table, `UserObj`, bearer, envelope — required and present.\n- **MARATHON-2** (closed): app factory / shared DB.\n\n### Must land before\n\n- Profile UI in SPA settings (MARATHON-16/18) and any feature that assumes GET-by-id directory.\n\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- Actual WebSocket/Redis broadcast of `user.updated` → MARATHON-13/14.\n- Avatar file upload + serving → MARATHON-10 (then clients may PATCH `avatar_url` to the file URL).\n- Username change / account delete → new task if ever required.\n- Presence (“active”/“away”) beyond `status_text`/`status_emoji` → out of epic wording for this task.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| WS subscribe/resume + event delivery | future WS routes | MARATHON-13 |\n| Cross-node Redis fan-out / outage path | Redis pub/sub | MARATHON-14 |\n| SPA profile/settings forms + `data-testid` | frontend | MARATHON-16/18 |\n| File upload for avatars | files API | MARATHON-10 |\n| Workspace membership-gated user visibility | workspaces/members | Not required; directory is cluster-global here |\n| `GET /api/users` list/search | — | Search is MARATHON-11; no list endpoint in this task |\n| Changing `/api/auth/me` behavior | `server/auth/routes.py` | Remains session read; PATCH is `/api/users/me` |\n| Migration v2 workspaces schema | `server/db.py` | MARATHON-5 |\n| IRC nick metadata sync | IRC gateway | MARATHON-15 |\n| Logout/token revoke | auth_tokens | Still out of scope per MARATHON-3 |\n\nNeighborhood scan disposition:\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `server/auth/users.py` — `UserObj` map, create, get_by_id | **In scope** — add update/validators; do not change register defaults |\n| `server/auth/routes.py` — `/api/auth/*` | Out of scope (read-only `/me` stays) |\n| `server/auth/deps.py` — bearer → UserObj | **Consume only** |\n| `server/errors.py` — auth-only validation envelope | **In scope** — broaden per MARATHON-5 rule |\n| `server/app.py` — routers | **In scope** — mount users router |\n| `server/db.py` — v1 users columns | Out of scope for DDL; columns already sufficient |\n| `tests/test_auth.py` — UserObj null profile fields | Keep green; profiles tests are a new file |\n| Grep `avatar_url`/`status_text`/`timezone` | Only Auth create/mapping today — Profiles owns mutation |\n| No existing `server/users/` package | **Create** |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| GET unknown UUID | **404** `not_found` |\n| GET without bearer | **401** `unauthorized` |\n| PATCH without bearer | **401** |\n| PATCH `{}` | **200** same user; **do not** call `publish_user_updated`; **do not** bump `updated_at` |\n| PATCH only unknown keys | Same as `{}` (no-op) |\n| PATCH `timezone: \"Not/AZone\"` | **400** `validation_error` |\n| PATCH `timezone: \"UTC\"` | **200** (valid IANA / ZoneInfo) |\n| PATCH `timezone: null` | Clear to JSON `null` |\n| PATCH `display_name: \"   \"` or `null` | Store `username`; return that string |\n| PATCH `display_name` length 81 | **400** |\n| PATCH `status_text` length 101 | **400** |\n| PATCH `status_emoji` length 65 | **400** |\n| PATCH `avatar_url` length 2049 | **400** |\n| PATCH `avatar_url: \"\"` | Clear to `null` |\n| PATCH includes `username: \"other\"` | Ignore; username unchanged |\n| PATCH includes `id` of another user | Ignore; still updates **caller** only |\n| Values identical to current | Treat as success **200**; prefer **skip** publish and **skip** `updated_at` bump if nothing changed |\n| Concurrent PATCHs from two tokens same user | Last writer wins per SQLite; both 200; both may publish |\n| PATCH then GET `/api/auth/me` | Returns updated fields (same DB row) |\n| PATCH on node :8000 then GET user on :8002 | Sees update (shared SQLite) |\n| Invalid JSON body | **400** envelope (after errors.py broaden) |\n| Extra nested objects | Ignore unknown; do not 500 |\n| `ZoneInfo` / tzdata missing on platform | Fail closed: invalid timezone → 400; do not silently accept (image has zoneinfo data) |\n| SQLite busy | Wait `busy_timeout`; on failure → 500; do not return partial success |\n| publish hook raises (future) | Must not fail the HTTP response after commit — catch/log inside publisher when wired; no-op today cannot raise |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET /api/users/{id}` with valid bearer and existing id → **200** `{ \"user\": UserObj }` with exact key set and no `email`.\n2. `GET /api/users/{id}` for missing id → **404** `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"not_found\", ... } }`.\n3. `GET` / `PATCH` without/invalid bearer → **401** `unauthorized`.\n4. `PATCH /api/users/me` with a valid subset (e.g. `{ \"display_name\": \"Ada\", \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\" }`) → **200** full `user` reflecting changes.\n5. Invalid timezone string → **400** `validation_error`; DB row unchanged.\n6. Over-max `display_name` / `status_text` / `status_emoji` / `avatar_url` → **400**; DB unchanged.\n7. Clearing nullable fields with `null` (or `\"\"`) → stored/returned as JSON `null`.\n8. After PATCH, `GET /api/auth/me` and `GET /api/users/{own_id}` return the same updated profile fields.\n9. **Negative:** PATCH must **not** change `username` or `id` even if those keys are sent.\n10. **Negative:** responses must **not** include `password`, `password_hash`, or `email`.\n11. **Negative:** successful profile events prepared for later WS must **not** require `channel_id` or `seq` (hook payload documents their absence).\n12. **Cluster:** PATCH on `:8000` visible via GET on `:8001`/`:8002` while `./start.sh` runs.\n13. `publish_user_updated` exists and is invoked on mutating PATCH (may be no-op).\n14. `/api/health` remains unenveloped and unauthenticated.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (implementer)\n\n`tests/test_profiles.py` with `TestClient(create_app(Settings(...)))` and per-test `tmp_path` sqlite:\n\n- Register via Auth helpers → GET self by id → 200 key set.\n- GET random UUID → 404 envelope.\n- GET/PATCH missing Authorization → 401.\n- PATCH display_name + timezone happy path; assert `/api/auth/me` matches.\n- PATCH invalid timezone → 400; re-GET shows prior values.\n- Parametrize over-length fields → 400.\n- PATCH null clears nullable fields; display_name null resets to username.\n- PATCH `{}` and PATCH with only `username` → unchanged profile.\n- Assert `USER_OBJ_KEYS` / no email.\n- Optional: monkeypatch/spy that `publish_user_updated` called once on mutating PATCH and not on no-op.\n\nKeep `tests/test_auth.py` fully green (no regressions).\n\n### Manual (human / cluster)\n\n1. `./start.sh` up; register on `:8000`.\n2. `PATCH /api/users/me` with timezone + status; confirm 200.\n3. `GET /api/users/{id}` on `:8001` returns new fields.\n4. Invalid timezone → 400 JSON envelope.\n5. Confirm `/api/health` still plain `{status,node_id}`.\n\n### Out of test scope here\n\n- Actual WS client receipt of `user.updated` (MARATHON-13).\n- SPA form selectors (MARATHON-16/18).\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":391,"fileSize":21329,"path":"/tmp/marathon-4-design.md","readRange":{"startLine":200,"endLine":391},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-36e90b36-47ae-4ba4-b45b-7d18e8e1a54c-13\nfc_4ced65ff-b22f-94a1-9d4a-079de7bd4ec5_0","startedAtMs":"1787439258290","completedAtMs":"1787439258550"},"model_call_id":"a0dfa0ee-aa77-4354-aa4c-699fe2d7eb30-3-gahq","session_id":"3a13baf3-8b3d-4288-b33c-5b5a6719fc16","timestamp_ms":1787439258577}
