{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-566537d1-85ad-4117-85f6-9042dd0f577e-16\nfc_755aafd6-33ac-9cce-ba9d-874496717a7f_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/marathon-4-design.md","offset":140,"limit":60},"result":{"success":{"content":"**Field validation** (any failure → 400 `validation_error`; first failure message may be returned):\n\n| Field | Rules |\n|-------|--------|\n| `display_name` | Must be `string` if present (JSON `null` allowed → treat as reset). Strip leading/trailing whitespace. If empty after strip **or** JSON `null` → persist `username` (never store NULL; `UserObj.display_name` stays a string). Max length **80** Unicode code points after strip (reject longer). |\n| `timezone` | JSON `null` or `\"\"` → store SQL `NULL`. Non-empty string: must be a valid IANA key (`zoneinfo.ZoneInfo(value)` succeeds). Max length **64** code points before ZoneInfo check. Do **not** rewrite aliases (store the client string as given if valid). |\n| `avatar_url` | JSON `null` or `\"\"` → SQL `NULL`. Otherwise must be `string` with length **1..2048** code points. No fetch; no required scheme. |\n| `status_text` | JSON `null` or `\"\"` → SQL `NULL`. Otherwise string length **1..100** code points. |\n| `status_emoji` | JSON `null` or `\"\"` → SQL `NULL`. Otherwise string length **1..64** code points (emoji or shortcode text). |\n\nWrong JSON types (e.g. `timezone: 1`, `status_text: true`) → 400 `validation_error` (via Pydantic handler or explicit `ApiError`).\n\n**Response 200:**\n\n```json\n{ \"user\": { /* full UserObj after update */ } }\n```\n\nAlways return the **complete** user object (not a sparse patch echo).\n\n**Errors:** 401; 400 validation. **No 404** on PATCH `/me` (auth user always exists; if token’s user row vanished → 401 via dependency, same as Auth).\n\n### Seam: `user.updated` event (backend internal → future WS)\n\nContract owned here; **transport not implemented** in this task.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"user.updated\",\n  \"user\": { /* UserObj */ }\n}\n```\n\n| Rule | Detail |\n|------|--------|\n| Present | `type`, `user` |\n| Absent | **`channel_id`**, **`seq`**, workspace ids — profile events are not channel-sequenced |\n| When to call | After successful COMMIT of a PATCH that changed at least one column (including clearing to NULL). Skip if no-op `{}` or values equal to previous |\n| Hook API | `server/events.py::publish_user_updated(user: dict) -> None` — **no-op body** for now (may log at debug). MARATHON-13/14 replace/extend to Redis pub/sub + WS clients |\n| Multi-node | Durability is SQLite UPDATE; other nodes see new values on next GET. Live push across nodes is MARATHON-14 |\n\n### Validation envelope scope (`server/errors.py`)\n\n`RequestValidationError` → 400 envelope for any path starting with `/api/` **except** exact `/api/health`. Identical to MARATHON-5. If Workspaces already landed this change, Profiles implementer makes **no further edit** (verify with a PATCH type-error test).\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Schema\n\n**No migration.** Uses existing v1 `users` columns:\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Profiles behavior |\n|--------|------|------|-------------------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | Read-only |\n| `username` | TEXT UNIQUE | NOT NULL | Read-only |\n| `password_hash` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Never exposed / never patched |\n| `display_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | PATCH; never NULL |\n| `timezone` | TEXT | NULL | PATCH |\n| `avatar_url` | TEXT | NULL | PATCH |\n| `status_text` | TEXT | NULL | PATCH |","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":391,"fileSize":21329,"path":"/tmp/marathon-4-design.md","readRange":{"startLine":140,"endLine":199},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-566537d1-85ad-4117-85f6-9042dd0f577e-16\nfc_755aafd6-33ac-9cce-ba9d-874496717a7f_0","startedAtMs":"1787439264005","completedAtMs":"1787439265586"},"model_call_id":"a0dfa0ee-aa77-4354-aa4c-699fe2d7eb30-4-c84v","session_id