{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-ca616d98-c1ca-4f5f-a62f-42d5b8cab5ba-17\nfc_9a00ff78-66ac-9451-9624-156cd6c34a7b_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/marathon-5-design.md","offset":300},"result":{"success":{"content":"| `topic` | TEXT | NOT NULL | default `''` |\n| `is_archived` | INTEGER | NOT NULL | 0/1 default 0 |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UTC Z |\n| `updated_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UTC Z |\n| UNIQUE | (`workspace_id`,`name`) | | |\n\n#### `channel_members`\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `channel_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → `channels.id` ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → `users.id` ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| PRIMARY KEY | (`channel_id`,`user_id`) | | |\n\n#### `channel_read_state`\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `channel_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → `channels.id` ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → `users.id` ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `last_read_seq` | INTEGER | NOT NULL | DEFAULT 0; never decreases (enforced in MARATHON-11) |\n| `unread_count` | INTEGER | NOT NULL | DEFAULT 0; JSON field of same name |\n| `mention_count` | INTEGER | NOT NULL | DEFAULT 0; JSON field of same name |\n| `updated_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| PRIMARY KEY | (`channel_id`,`user_id`) | | |\n\n**No Redis keys.** Booleans in JSON are real booleans; SQLite stores 0/1. This task **does not** insert `channel_read_state` rows on workspace create (detail returns `[]`).\n\n### Schema change summary\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| Add migration v2 tables above | Yes — additive on v1 DBs |\n\n### Create transaction (single BEGIN/COMMIT)\n\n1. INSERT `workspaces` (`join_mode='open'`, `owner_id=creator`).\n2. INSERT `workspace_members` (`role='owner'`).\n3. INSERT `channels` (`name='general'`, `is_private=0`, `is_dm=0`, `topic=''`, `is_archived=0`).\n4. INSERT `channel_members` (creator ↔ general).\n5. Commit; map rows → response objects.\n\nOn any failure: rollback; map UNIQUE(slug) → 409; unexpected → 500 (log).\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/workspaces/__init__.py` | Package marker; export router. |\n| `server/workspaces/store.py` | Slug/name validation; insert workspace; list for user; get by slug; membership check; row→`WorkspaceObj`. |\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` | `POST \"\"`, `GET \"\"`, `GET \"/{slug}\"` under prefix `/api/workspaces`; Depend `get_current_user`; parse `include_archived` (`1` \\| case-insensitive `true`). |\n| `server/channels/__init__.py` | Package marker. |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | `ChannelObj` mapping; `create_general_channel`; `list_channels_for_workspace_user` (private + archive filters); `list_read_state_for_channels` → full `ReadStateEntry` dicts. |\n| `tests/test_workspaces.py` | Contract tests for create/list/detail, authz, slug conflict, archive query (`1` and `true`), full `read_state` keys, envelope errors. |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/db.py` | Add `_migrate_v2` / reverse; append `(2, _migrate_v2)` to `MIGRATIONS`. |\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` workspaces router; leave health + stub `/` + auth router unchanged. |\n| `server/errors.py` | Broaden validation handler to `/api/*` except `/api/health`. |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/**` | Auth complete (MARATHON-3); only consume `get_current_user` |\n| `start.sh`, `server/settings.py` | No workspace-specific env |\n| `timer.sh`, `loom-prompts/**` | Harness |\n| SPA / replace `GET /` | MARATHON-16 |\n| Member list/PATCH/transfer routes | MARATHON-6 |\n| Channel create/join/leave/archive/pins routes | MARATHON-7 |\n| Read POST/GET routes, search, slash | MARATHON-11 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order (single implementer)\n\n1. `db.py` migration v2 (+ reverse for tests if pattern continues).\n2. `server/channels/store.py` + `server/workspaces/store.py`.\n3. `server/workspaces/routes.py` + wire `app.py`.\n4. Broaden `errors.py` validation paths.\n5. `tests/test_workspaces.py`.\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Channel store vs workspace store can proceed in parallel after migration DDL is known.\n- Tests after routes.\n\n### Downstream seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumed by |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `WorkspaceObj` + `/api/workspaces` create/list/detail | MARATHON-6, 7, 12, 16, 18 |\n| `ChannelObj` JSON + `channels` / `channel_members` tables | MARATHON-7, 8, 9, 11, 13, 17 |\n| Auto `#general` with `name=\"general\"` | SPA default channel; IRC/bridge later |\n| `join_mode` column default `open` | MARATHON-6 PATCH; MARATHON-7 join rules |\n| `workspace_members.role` including `owner` | MARATHON-6 |\n| Embedded `read_state[]` **full** `ReadStateEntry` shape | MARATHON-11 (writes + `GET/POST .../read`); MARATHON-16 (badges) |\n| `include_archived` ∈ {`1`,`true`} | SPA / channel settings UI |\n| 404-for-non-members detail policy | SPA routing |\n\n### Upstream\n\n- **MARATHON-3** (closed): users, bearer, envelope — required.\n- **MARATHON-2** (closed): shared DB / app factory.\n\n### Must land before\n\n- MARATHON-6, 7, 16 (declared blockers/dependents).\n\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- Members list, role PATCH, ownership transfer → MARATHON-6.\n- Extra channels, join/leave, archive, pins → MARATHON-7.\n- Populating/updating `channel_read_state` and computing unread/mention → MARATHON-11.\n- SPA forms/selectors → MARATHON-16.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| `GET/PATCH` members, transfer ownership | future `/api/workspaces/{slug}/members` | MARATHON-6 |\n| `PATCH` workspace `name`/`join_mode` | — | MARATHON-6 |\n| `POST .../channels`, join/leave, topic, archive, pins | — | MARATHON-7 |\n| Open-workspace auto-onboard of non-members | join rules in MARATHON-7 | Non-members get 404 on detail until they become members via later APIs |\n| Invitations / user groups | — | MARATHON-12 |\n| Messages / seq assignment | — | MARATHON-8/13 |\n| `POST/GET /api/channels/{id}/read` | — | MARATHON-11 (embeds **same** shape here; does not implement those routes) |\n| Computing live unread/mention from messages | — | MARATHON-11; this task only maps stored columns / returns `[]` |\n| SPA workspace shell / `workspace-create-form` | stub `GET /` | MARATHON-16 |\n| Profiles PATCH | `server/users/**` (MARATHON-4) | Profiles task |\n| Changing auth token semantics | `server/auth/**` | MARATHON-3 closed |\n| Health envelope/auth | `GET /api/health` | MARATHON-2 |\n| Cluster boot/respawn tests | `tests/test_cluster_*.py` | MARATHON-19/20 closed |\n\n**Neighborhood scan** (current tree after MARATHON-3; Profiles may add `server/users/**` in parallel):\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `server/app.py` — routers, health, stub `/` | **In scope** — mount workspaces router only |\n| `server/db.py` — migrations v0/v1 | **In scope** — add v2 |\n| `server/errors.py` — auth-only validation envelope | **In scope** — broaden to `/api/*` |\n| `server/auth/**` — register/login/me, deps | **Out of scope** — consume dependency only |\n| `tests/test_auth.py`, `tests/test_health.py`, `tests/test_cluster_*.py` | Keep green; new tests in `test_workspaces.py` |\n| `start.sh`, `settings.py`, `requirements.txt` | No change required |\n| Grep `workspace`/`channel`/`read_state`/`general` / `include_archived` | **No matches** in application code — greenfield modules |\n| MARATHON-4 Profiles (`/api/users`) | **Out of scope** — parallel sibling; shared envelope rule only |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Unauthenticated POST/GET | **401** `unauthorized` |\n| Slug `AB` / `a` / `ab_cd` / empty | **400** `validation_error` |\n| Slug `ab` / `a-b` / 32-char kebab | Accepted if regex matches |\n| Duplicate slug | **409** `conflict` |\n| Concurrent duplicate slug inserts | IntegrityError → **409** (no 500) |\n| Name `\"  \"` / missing name | **400** |\n| Name with internal spaces / Unicode | Allowed after strip |\n| Extra body fields | Ignore |\n| Create success | Creator is `owner_id` and sole `workspace_members` row with `role=owner`; `#general` exists exactly once; no `channel_read_state` rows yet |\n| Second create by same user different slug | Allowed (multi-workspace) |\n| List with no memberships | **200** `{workspaces:[]}` |\n| Detail unknown slug | **404** |\n| Detail existing slug, non-member | **404** (same body as unknown) |\n| Detail as owner/member | **200**; `channels` includes `general`; `read_state` is `[]` until rows exist |\n| Private channel (future data) without membership | Omitted from `channels` and from `read_state` |\n| Archived channel, no query flag | Omitted |\n| `?include_archived=1` | Archived included (if visible re: private) |\n| `?include_archived=true` (any ASCII case) | **Same as `1`** — archived included |\n| `?include_archived=0` / `false` / `yes` / `on` | Treat as off |\n| Fixture `channel_read_state` row for visible channel | Detail includes entry with all four keys; counts from columns (default 0) |\n| Fixture row for omitted private/archived channel | Must **not** appear in `read_state` |\n| `#general` accidentally archived in DB | Obeys archive filter like any channel |\n| SQLite busy | Wait `busy_timeout`; still fail closed with 500/503 only after timeout; create remains transactional |\n| Validation 422 from FastAPI on workspaces | Normalized to **400** envelope |\n| Cross-node create on :8000, list on :8001 | Sees workspace (shared DB) |\n| `join_mode` column somehow not `open`/`invite_only` | Prevented by CHECK; API never emits other values |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `POST /api/workspaces` with valid Bearer + `{slug,name}` → **201** with `workspace` (`WorkspaceObj` keys exactly) and `general_channel` (`ChannelObj` keys exactly); `workspace.join_mode==\"open\"`; `workspace.owner_id` equals caller; `general_channel.name==\"general\"`; `is_private/is_dm/is_archived` are JSON `false`; `topic==\"\"`.\n2. Duplicate `slug` → **409** envelope `code=conflict`.\n3. Invalid slug (fails `^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`) or empty/whitespace name → **400** `validation_error`.\n4. Missing/invalid Bearer on any of the three routes → **401**.\n5. After create, `GET /api/workspaces` includes that workspace for the creator and does **not** require a second join call.\n6. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as member → **200** with `workspace`, `channels` containing `#general`, and `read_state` (array; may be empty). When non-empty, **every** entry has exactly the keys `channel_id`, `last_read_seq`, `unread_count`, `mention_count` (integers ≥ 0 for the three numeric fields).\n7. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as different user with no membership → **404** (must **not** return 200).\n8. With only `#general` present, `channels` length is 1 and name is `general`.\n9. When an archived channel exists visible to the user: default detail omits it; `?include_archived=1` **and** `?include_archived=true` both include it.\n10. When a private channel exists without `channel_members` for the caller: detail omits it even with `include_archived=1` or `true`.\n11. **Cluster:** workspace created via `:8000` is listed/detailed via `:8001`/`:8002` with the same token.\n12. **Negative:** must **not** create workspace without `#general`; must **not** store workspace SoT in Redis; must **not** add member-list or channel-CRUD routes; must **not** change `/api/health` shape/auth; must **not** include `email` or password fields anywhere; must **not** emit truncated `read_state` entries missing `unread_count` or `mention_count`.\n13. Migration v2 applied idempotently; fresh and v1-upgraded DBs both serve the routes; `channel_read_state` includes `unread_count` and `mention_count` columns.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (`tests/test_workspaces.py`)\n\nUse `TestClient(create_app(Settings(data_dir=tmp_path,...)))`; register via `/api/auth/register` to obtain token.\n\n- Create happy path → 201 shape + DB rows (workspace, member owner, channel general, channel member).\n- Duplicate slug → 409.\n- Bad slug / blank name → 400 envelope.\n- Unauthenticated → 401.\n- List empty then list after create.\n- Detail as member vs other user → 200 vs 404.\n- Insert archived + private channels via SQL fixtures; assert omit/include for `include_archived=1` **and** `include_archived=true`; assert `0`/`false`/`yes` leave archived omitted.\n- Fresh detail: `read_state == []`.\n- After SQL insert of a `channel_read_state` row (with counts), detail returns matching `ReadStateEntry` including `unread_count` and `mention_count` for visible channels only; assert key set equality.\n- Optional: two apps sharing `data_dir` — create on A, get on B.\n\n### Manual / cluster\n\n```bash\ncd /app && ./start.sh &\n# register on :8000, create workspace, then:\ncurl -sS http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/workspaces -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"\ncurl -sS http://127.0.0.1:8002/api/workspaces/acme -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"\ncurl -sS 'http://127.0.0.1:8002/api/workspaces/acme?include_archived=true' -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"\n```\n\n### Human checks\n\n1. Create workspace → response includes usable `general_channel.id`.\n2. Second account cannot open the slug (404).\n3. Confirm sqlite tables exist; `#general` row `name=general` without `#`; `channel_read_state` has count columns.\n4. Kill one HTTP node; after respawn, list still works with same token.\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":533,"fileSize":28825,"path":"/tmp/marathon-5-design.md","readRange":{"startLine":300,"endLine":533},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-ca616d98-c1ca-4f5f-a62f-42d5b8cab5ba-17\nfc_9a00ff78-66ac-9451-9624-156cd6c34a7b_0","startedAtMs":"1787439628735","completedAtMs":"1787439629725"},"model_call_id":"b1fcab4f-0d7b-4634-a885-5d667e8467f0-4-0qbf","session_id":"ffd1d970-ba7b-4639-af17-a540128dd1ae","timestamp_ms":1787439629750}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-ca616d98-c1ca-4f5f-a62f-42d5b8cab5ba-18\nfc_9a00ff78-66ac-9451-9624-156cd6c34a7b_1","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"git log --oneline -5 -- server/db.py server/app.py server/errors.py && ls -la server/ && head -n 5 tests/test_*.py; which marathon-freeports marathon-portlock 2>/dev/null; ls start.sh 2>/dev/null; cat server/settings.py","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-ca616d98-c1ca-4f5f-a62f-42d5b8cab5ba-18\nfc_9a00ff78-66ac-9451-9624-156cd6c34a7b_1","simpleCommands":["git","ls","head","which","ls","cat"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"log"},{"type":"word","value":"--oneline"},{"type":"number","value":"-5"},{"type":"word","value":"--"},{"type":"word","value":"server/db.py"},{"type":"word","value":"server/app.py"},{"type":"word","value":"server/errors.py"}],"fullText":"git log --oneline -5 -- server/db.py server/app.py server/errors.py"},{"name":"ls","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-la"},{"type":"word","value":"server/"}],"fullText":"ls -la server/"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-n"},{"type":"number","value":"5"},{"type":"word","value":"tests/test_*.py"}],"fullText":"head -n 5 tests/test_*.py"},{"name":"which","args":[{"type":"word","value":"marathon-freeports"},{"type":"word","value":"marathon-portlock"}],"fullText":"which marathon-freeports marathon-portlock"},{"name":"ls","args":[{"type":"word","value":"start.sh"}],"fullText":"ls start.sh"},{"name":"cat","args":[{"type":"word","value":"server/settings.py"}],"fullText":"cat server/settings.py"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresh