{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-9d8c7914-0bf9-48ec-b9b2-153bdc99f7f2-1\nfc_7c6147e8-c784-9e1a-a719-f4a9069dfa9c_1","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-7 --output json","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-9d8c7914-0bf9-48ec-b9b2-153bdc99f7f2-1\nfc_7c6147e8-c784-9e1a-a719-f4a9069dfa9c_1","simpleCommands":["loom"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-7"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-7 --output json"}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Show MARATHON-7 task details","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"86bf3402-21e8-4aa3-94a1-667e1b9066f8","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-7 --output json","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-7\",\n  \"title\": \"Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"priority\": 0,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"assignee\": \"backend-dev-1\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"backend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-7 — Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task completes channel lifecycle for Huddle on top of the workspace tenancy shipped in MARATHON-5/6: authenticated callers can create public/private channels under a workspace slug, join and leave channels (with open-workspace auto-onboard and invite_only/guest/private gates), list channel members as `UserObj`, patch topic, archive/unarchive (owner-only), and pin/unpin messages. It also implements the SPA-locked workspace join seam (`POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join`) that MARATHON-16 already calls. It locks the `/api/channels/*` and pin REST contracts, introduces migration **v3** (`messages` minimal + `channel_pins`), and exports a shared **archived-write guard** (`423`) that MARATHON-8/11 must reuse.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite SoT; **migration version 3** additive: minimal `messages` + `channel_pins` (pins need message rows; same “schema-ahead” pattern as M5 channels-before-CRUD) |\\n| Route layout | (1) Extend `server/workspaces/routes.py`: `POST /{slug}/join`, `POST /{slug}/channels`. (2) New `server/channels/routes.py` prefix `/api/channels`: join, leave, PATCH, members, archive, unarchive, pins. (3) New `server/messages/routes.py` (or pin routes mounted under `/api/messages`) for `POST/DELETE /{id}/pin` |\\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all new endpoints require Bearer |\\n| `ChannelObj` | **Unchanged** key set from MARATHON-5 (`CHANNEL_OBJ_KEYS`); this task owns create/mutate behavior |\\n| Workspace join vs channel join | **Both**: SPA uses workspace join (M16); product grader uses channel join with open auto-onboard. Same membership insert helper |\\n| Private “invite” | No private-invite table yet (MARATHON-12). “Without invite” ≡ caller lacks `channel_members` row → **403** on join. Creator is auto-member on create; tests may SQL-seed members until add-member API exists |\\n| Pins without full Message API | Minimal `messages` table + thin `MessageObj` mapper (empty `files`/`reactions`/`mentions`, `reply_count=0`) so pin list/embed works; MARATHON-8 owns message CRUD and enriches the same object |\\n| Archived writes | Shared helper `assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived`; used by topic PATCH + pin mutate now; documented for M8 message/reaction writes |\\n| Events / Redis | No pub/sub (MARATHON-13/14); optional no-op hooks OK but not required |\\n| Timestamps | Reuse `utc_now_z()` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) consistent with M3–M6 |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- Product contract is explicit on paths, envelopes, role matrix, 423, and pin shapes; inventing alternate routes would fail the grader and diverge from SPA settings (MARATHON-17/18).\\n- Workspace join is already wired in `static/js/shell.js`; omitting it leaves onboarding broken despite channel-join auto-onboard.\\n- Introducing a minimal `messages` table for pins mirrors M5 shipping `channels` early — one migration, stable FKs, no pin→message soft-orphan mess.\\n- Centralizing the archived guard prevents M8 from inventing a second 423 code/message.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| Only channel-join auto-onboard; skip workspace join | Breaks MARATHON-16 SPA contract already shipped |\\n| Defer pins entirely to MARATHON-8 | Task + product contract require pin routes in this task |\\n| Pin table without messages; return message stubs | Violates `{pins:[{message,...}]}` and FK integrity |\\n| Allow members to create private channels | Product: member → **403** on `is_private:true` |\\n| Soft 200 on guest join | Product: guest → **403** |\\n| Use `MemberObj` for channel members list | Product: `UserObj[]` under `members` |\\n| 404 for archived writes | Product: **423** |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\nMinimal `messages` lands before message CRUD. Implementers must not invent message POST here; tests for pins SQL-insert message rows (or a tiny test helper). MARATHON-8 must **extend** v3 `messages` (additive columns/tables), not replace the table or diverge `MessageObj` keys listed below.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: UUID4 string ids; `ApiError` + `{error:{code,message}}`; ignore unknown JSON body fields; `400` `validation_error`; `401` `unauthorized`; `409` `conflict` on uniqueness.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: `UserObj` exact keys via `row_to_user_obj`.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-5**: `ChannelObj` exact keys; `WorkspaceObj`; workspace slug resolution; non-member workspace routes → **404** (do not leak); `include_archived` semantics unchanged; `#general` name without `#`.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-6**: roles `owner|admin|member|guest`; **403** `forbidden` when member lacks privilege; `join_mode` ∈ {`open`,`invite_only`}; dual ownership invariant.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-16**: `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` body `{}`; **200** `{workspace}` (+ optional `channels`/`read_state`); open → member; invite_only → 403; unknown → 404; idempotent if already member.\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Shared types\\n\\n#### `ChannelObj` (unchanged)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"workspace_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"eng\\\",\\n  \\\"is_private\\\": false,\\n  \\\"is_dm\\\": false,\\n  \\\"topic\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"is_archived\\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\nExact keys: `id`, `workspace_id`, `name`, `is_private`, `is_dm`, `topic`, `is_archived`.\\n\\n#### `UserObj` (channel members list — MARATHON-4)\\n\\nExact keys: `id`, `username`, `display_name`, `timezone`, `avatar_url`, `status_text`, `status_emoji`.\\n\\n#### Minimal `MessageObj` (for pin embed; MARATHON-8 owns enrichment)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"author_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": { /* UserObj */ },\\n  \\\"body\\\": \\\"hello\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_id\\\": null,\\n  \\\"reply_count\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-08-22T23:00:00Z\\\",\\n  \\\"edited_at\\\": null,\\n  \\\"files\\\": [],\\n  \\\"reactions\\\": [],\\n  \\\"mentions\\\": []\\n}\\n```\\n\\nUntil M8 lands, pin responses use this shape with empty lists / zero reply_count / `edited_at` null when unset. **Do not** omit keys.\\n\\n#### `PinObj` (POST pin response nested under `pin`)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"message_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"pinned_by\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"pinned_at\\\": \\\"2026-08-22T23:00:00Z\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n#### Pin list entry\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"message\\\": { /* MessageObj */ },\\n  \\\"pinned_by\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"pinned_at\\\": \\\"…\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n#### Error codes (this task)\\n\\n| `code` | HTTP | When |\\n|--------|------|------|\\n| `validation_error` | 400 | Bad name/topic; topic \\u003e 250; null where disallowed |\\n| `unauthorized` | 401 | Missing/invalid bearer |\\n| `forbidden` | 403 | Guest create/join; member create private; invite_only non-member join; private join without membership; private pin list/mutate for non-members; archive by non-owner |\\n| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown workspace slug (create/join workspace); unknown channel/message id; non-member on workspace-scoped create (same as M5/6) |\\n| `conflict` | 409 | Duplicate channel name in workspace |\\n| `archived` | 423 | Mutating write against `is_archived=1` channel (topic, pin, and future message writes) |\\n\\n### Role / join capability matrix (normative)\\n\\n| Action | owner | admin | member | guest | non-member (open ws) | non-member (invite_only) |\\n|--------|-------|-------|--------|-------|----------------------|---------------------------|\\n| `POST .../workspaces/{slug}/join` | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | **200** add as `member` | **403** |\\n| `POST .../workspaces/{slug}/channels` public | yes | yes | yes | **403** | **404** | **404** |\\n| `POST .../channels` private (`is_private:true`) | yes | yes | **403** | **403** | **404** | **404** |\\n| `POST /channels/{id}/join` public | yes | yes | yes | **403** | **200** + auto workspace `member` | **403** |\\n| `POST /channels/{id}/join` private, not channel member | **403** | **403** | **403** | **403** | **403** (open) / **403** (invite_only) | **403** |\\n| `POST /channels/{id}/join` private, already channel member | 200 | 200 | 200 | 200* | n/a | n/a |\\n| `POST .../leave` | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | see edge cases | |\\n| `PATCH` topic | channel member **or** workspace owner | same | same | same if channel member | — | — |\\n| `POST archive/unarchive` | **yes** (workspace owner only) | **403** | **403** | **403** | **404** | **404** |\\n\\n\\\\* Guest who somehow has channel membership (seeded) may leave; guest **cannot** newly join public.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M16)** | Bearer; body `{}`; disable submit; on 200 persist slug + enter shell (use returned `channels` if present else detail GET); on 4xx show `join-workspace-error` |\\n| **Server** | Resolve slug; if missing → 404; if already workspace member → 200 `{workspace}` (+ optional channels/read_state); if `join_mode=open` → insert `workspace_members` role=`member`, then return 200; if `invite_only` → 403 |\\n\\n**Recommended 200 body** (SPA-friendly, matches optional M16 fields):\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"workspace\\\": { /* WorkspaceObj */ },\\n  \\\"channels\\\": [ /* visible ChannelObj[] */ ],\\n  \\\"read_state\\\": [ /* ReadStateEntry[] */ ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n`channels`/`read_state` **should** be included using the same visibility rules as `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` (default: exclude archived). Minimum required by M16 is `{workspace}`; including channels avoids a second round-trip.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M17)** | Bearer; body `{name, is_private?, topic?}`; show create-channel modal errors; on 201 append channel to sidebar (`data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name`); on 409 show duplicate-name validation; on 403 show permission error |\\n| **Server** | Require workspace membership; enforce role matrix; validate; insert channel + creator `channel_members`; return 201 |\\n\\n**Request:**\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"name\\\": \\\"eng\\\", \\\"is_private\\\": false, \\\"topic\\\": \\\"optional\\\" }\\n```\\n\\n- `name` required; kebab regex **`^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`** (same family as workspace slug; strip not applied — must already match).\\n- `is_private` optional, default `false`; non-bool → 400.\\n- `topic` optional, default `\\\"\\\"`; if present must be string length ≤ 250 code points; longer → 400.\\n- Unknown fields ignored. Do **not** accept `description` as topic alias (product: no description→topic).\\n- `is_dm` always `false` for this route (DMs are MARATHON-9).\\n\\n**Response 201:** `{ \\\"channel\\\": { /* ChannelObj */ } }`\\n\\n**Errors:** 401; 404 non-member/unknown slug; 403 guest or member+private; 400 validation; 409 duplicate name (`conflict`, e.g. `\\\"channel name already taken\\\"`); IntegrityError race → same 409.\\n\\n**On success transaction:** INSERT channel; INSERT creator into `channel_members`; bump `channels.updated_at`/`created_at`.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/join`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Bearer; empty body; on 200 refresh channel membership / sidebar; on 403/404 surface error |\\n| **Server** | Resolve channel by id; apply join rules below; return **200** (envelope: prefer `{ \\\"channel\\\": ChannelObj }` for consistency with leave/archive; if returning bare 200 with empty body is undesired — **always return `{channel}`**) |\\n\\n**Join algorithm (ordered):**\\n\\n1. Channel missing → **404** `not_found`.\\n2. Load workspace for `channel.workspace_id`.\\n3. If caller already in `channel_members` → **200** `{channel}` (idempotent; no role change).\\n4. If channel `is_private` → **403** `forbidden` (“private without invite”).\\n5. If channel is public (`is_private=0`, `is_dm` irrelevant for join gate here):\\n   - Resolve workspace membership.\\n   - If **not** a workspace member:\\n     - `join_mode=open` → INSERT `workspace_members` (`role=member`) then continue.\\n     - `join_mode=invite_only` → **403**.\\n   - If workspace member with `role=guest` → **403** (cannot join public).\\n   - Else INSERT `channel_members` → **200**.\\n\\n**DM channels (`is_dm=1`):** treat like private for join — non-members **403** (actual DM membership is MARATHON-9). Do not auto-onboard via DM join.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/leave`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Bearer; on 200 update UI (remove from private list / mark left); treat repeat leave as success |\\n| **Server** | Idempotent remove from `channel_members`; return **200** `{channel}` |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n\\n- Unknown channel → **404**.\\n- Public channel: any authenticated user may call leave; if not a member, still **200** `{channel}` (no-op).\\n- Private channel: if caller is not a channel member **and** not a workspace member → **404** (do not leak). If workspace member but not channel member → **200** no-op `{channel}` (idempotent). If channel member → delete membership → **200**.\\n- Leaving does **not** remove workspace membership.\\n- Leave is allowed on archived channels (membership mgmt, not a “write” for 423 purposes).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{id}/members`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M18)** | Bearer; render `channel-members-list` / `channel-member-row` |\\n| **Server** | Authz then return `{members: UserObj[]}` |\\n\\n**Authz:**\\n\\n- Unknown channel → 404.\\n- Public: caller must be **workspace member** else 404.\\n- Private: caller must be **channel member** else **403** (align with pin-list private rule). Workspace owner who is not a channel member still gets **403** unless also a channel member (owner can PATCH topic without membership, but members list follows private pin rule). *Clarification:* workspace **owner** may list members of private channels in their workspace even without channel membership (settings UX); implementer **should** allow workspace owner OR channel member for private member list. Prefer: **channel member OR workspace owner**.\\n\\n**Ordering:** `username ASC` (case-insensitive), tie-break `id ASC`.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `PATCH /api/channels/{id}`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Body `{topic}`; disable topic submit; on 200 update `channel-topic` header; on 423 show archived error |\\n| **Server** | Authz; validate topic; reject if archived; update; return `{channel}` |\\n\\n**Request:** `{ \\\"topic\\\": \\\"Ship week\\\" }` — `topic` required when patching (only mutable field in this task). Omit/`exclude_unset`: empty `{}` → 200 no-op if authorized. Explicit `null` → 400. Max **250** Unicode code points.\\n\\n**Authz:** caller is **channel member** OR **workspace owner** (`workspaces.owner_id`). Else if can see channel → 403; else 404.\\n\\n**Archived:** if `is_archived` → **423** `archived` (do not update).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/archive` and `.../unarchive`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M18)** | Bearer; owner-only controls; on 200 flip archived UI / buttons |\\n| **Server** | Workspace **owner** only; set `is_archived` 1/0; return `{channel}` |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n\\n- Unknown channel → 404.\\n- Caller not workspace member → 404.\\n- Caller member but not `owner_id` → **403**.\\n- Archive when already archived / unarchive when not → **200** idempotent.\\n- Unarchive restores write access (clears 423 path).\\n- These endpoints themselves are **not** subject to 423.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ pins\\n\\n#### `GET /api/channels/{id}/pins` → `200 {pins:[…]}` newest-first (`pinned_at DESC`, tie-break `message_id DESC`)\\n\\n- Unknown channel → 404.\\n- Private + caller not channel member → **403**.\\n- Public + caller not workspace member → 404.\\n- Each entry: `{message: MessageObj, pinned_by, pinned_at}`.\\n- Reads allowed when archived (not a write).\\n\\n#### `POST /api/messages/{id}/pin` → `200 {pin:{message_id,pinned_by,pinned_at}}` idempotent\\n\\n- Unknown message → 404.\\n- Resolve channel from message; apply same visibility as pin list.\\n- If channel archived → **423**.\\n- Caller must be **channel member** (public: must have joined; being only a workspace member of a public channel without `channel_members` → **403**). Workspace owner without channel membership → **403** unless also member (pin is a membership action).\\n- If already pinned → 200 with existing `pinned_by`/`pinned_at` (do not change pinner).\\n- Else INSERT pin with `pinned_by=caller`, `pinned_at=now`.\\n\\n#### `DELETE /api/messages/{id}/pin` → `200 {\\\"unpinned\\\":true}` idempotent\\n\\n- Unknown message → 404.\\n- Same visibility/membership as POST pin.\\n- Archived → **423**.\\n- If no pin row → still **200** `{unpinned:true}`.\\n\\n### Client slow/fail summary\\n\\n| Condition | Client behavior |\\n|-----------|-----------------|\\n| In flight | Disable create/join/topic/archive/pin controls; keep prior lists |\\n| 401 | Re-auth (M16) |\\n| 403 | Show `error.message`; do not optimistic-join |\\n| 409 | Duplicate channel name inline validation |\\n| 423 | Show archived/locked state; disable composers (M17/18) |\\n| 404 | Treat channel/workspace inaccessible |\\n| Network/5xx | Retry; do not assume membership/pin applied |\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Migration v3 (additive, backward compatible)\\n\\n#### `messages` (minimal — MARATHON-8 extends)\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | UUID4 |\\n| `channel_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → channels ON DELETE CASCADE |\\n| `author_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\\n| `body` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| `parent_id` | TEXT | NULL | FK → messages (threads later) |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| `edited_at` | TEXT | NULL | |\\n| `deleted_at` | TEXT | NULL | reserved for M8 soft-delete |\\n\\nIndexes: `idx_messages_channel_id` on `channel_id`.\\n\\n**This task does not expose message CRUD.** Rows exist for pin tests / future M8.\\n\\n#### `channel_pins`\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `message_id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE; one pin per message |\\n| `channel_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → channels (denormalized for list-by-channel) |\\n| `pinned_by` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\\n| `pinned_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UTC Z |\\n\\nIndex: `idx_channel_pins_channel_pinned_at` on `(channel_id, pinned_at DESC)`.\\n\\n### Existing tables used (no change to DDL)\\n\\n- `channels`, `channel_members`, `workspaces`, `workspace_members`, `users`, `channel_read_state`\\n\\n### Schema change summary\\n\\n| Change | Compatible? |\\n|--------|-------------|\\n| v3 new tables | **Yes** — additive |\\n| No alters to v2 columns | **Yes** |\\n\\n### Invariants\\n\\n1. `UNIQUE(workspace_id, name)` on channels enforced; API maps violations to 409.\\n2. Channel create always inserts creator into `channel_members`.\\n3. Open workspace join/channel-join auto-onboard inserts `workspace_members.role='member'` (never owner/admin/guest).\\n4. At most one pin row per `message_id`.\\n5. `is_dm` channels are not creatable via `POST .../channels` (`is_dm=0` always).\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Router `/api/channels`: join, leave, PATCH, members, archive, unarchive, GET pins |\\n| `server/messages/__init__.py` | Package init |\\n| `server/messages/store.py` | Minimal message fetch + `row_to_message_obj` (thin); pin helpers may live here or in channels store |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | `POST/DELETE /api/messages/{id}/pin` |\\n| `tests/test_channels.py` | Contract tests: create/join/leave/topic/archive/roles/423/workspace-join |\\n| `tests/test_pins.py` | Pin list/POST/DELETE/idempotency/403 private/423 archived (SQL-seed messages) |\\n\\n### Modify\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/db.py` | Add `_migrate_v3` / `_reverse_v3`; register in `MIGRATIONS` / `REVERSES` |\\n| `server/channels/store.py` | `validate_channel_name`, `validate_topic`, `create_channel`, `get_channel`, `add_member`, `remove_member`, `list_members_as_users`, `set_archived`, `update_topic`, `assert_channel_writable`, pin list queries; keep existing list/general helpers |\\n| `server/workspaces/store.py` | `add_workspace_member(role='member')` helper for open join / auto-onboard (if not present) |\\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` | `POST /{slug}/join`, `POST /{slug}/channels` |\\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` for channels + messages routers |\\n| `server/channels/__init__.py` | Docstring update if needed |\\n| `server/errors.py` | No change required unless 423 helper desired (prefer raising `ApiError(423,\\\"archived\\\",…)`) |\\n\\n### Do not touch\\n\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `static/**` | Frontend MARATHON-17/18 |\\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume only |\\n| `tests/test_workspaces.py`, `tests/test_workspace_members.py` | Keep green; do not rewrite |\\n| `server/events.py` | Fan-out later |\\n| Message POST/GET/PATCH/DELETE, reactions | MARATHON-8 |\\n| Invitations / private invite redeem | MARATHON-12 |\\n| DM get-or-create | MARATHON-9 |\\n| Slash `/archive` `/topic` | MARATHON-11 (will call same store helpers) |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Build order\\n\\n1. `db.py` v3 migration (+ reverse).\\n2. Channel store mutations + writable guard + workspace member insert helper.\\n3. Workspace routes: join + create channel.\\n4. Channels routes: join/leave/patch/members/archive.\\n5. Messages store thin mapper + pin routes.\\n6. Tests.\\n\\n### Parallelism\\n\\n- Pin routes can proceed in parallel with join/leave once `messages`/`channel_pins` DDL and `get_channel` exist.\\n- Workspace join can land before channel create.\\n\\n### Downstream seams this task owns\\n\\n| Contract | Consumed by |\\n|----------|-------------|\\n| `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` + `ChannelObj` create | MARATHON-17 SPA create modal |\\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` + open auto-onboard | Graders; IRC later; SPA may use later |\\n| `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` | MARATHON-16 shell (already calling) |\\n| leave / members / PATCH topic / archive | MARATHON-18 settings; MARATHON-11 slash cmds |\\n| `assert_channel_writable` → 423 `archived` | MARATHON-8 messages/reactions; MARATHON-11 |\\n| Pin routes + `channel_pins` + minimal `MessageObj` | SPA (future); MARATHON-8 must not break keys |\\n| Minimal `messages` table | MARATHON-8 **must extend**, not drop/recreate |\\n\\n### Upstream\\n\\n- MARATHON-5/6 closed: schema v2, roles, ChannelObj, join_mode.\\n- MARATHON-16 closed: client join path.\\n\\n### Declared dependents\\n\\n- MARATHON-8 (messages), MARATHON-9 (DMs) block on this task.\\n\\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\\n\\n- Message CRUD / reactions / reply_count maintenance → MARATHON-8.\\n- `POST /api/dms` → MARATHON-9.\\n- Private channel add-member / invitations → MARATHON-12 (+ optional channel invite API if still missing).\\n- Slash command side effects → MARATHON-11 (reuse archive/topic store).\\n- WS membership/channel events → MARATHON-13/14.\\n- SPA channel UI → MARATHON-17/18.\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\\n|------|----------------|--------------|\\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages` and message list/edit/delete | future `server/messages/routes.py` CRUD | MARATHON-8 |\\n| Reactions endpoints | `/api/messages/{id}/reactions` | MARATHON-8 |\\n| `POST /api/dms` | — | MARATHON-9 |\\n| Invitation redeem unlocking invite_only join | — | MARATHON-12; this task only 403s non-members |\\n| Explicit `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` add-member | SPA `channel-add-member-*` | Not in product Channels section; file follow-up if M18 needs it before invites — **neighborhood hit**: frontend hooks list add-member controls; **excluded** here; recommend small follow-up or fold into M12/M18 backend notes |\\n| `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` | — | MARATHON-11 |\\n| Slash `/topic` `/archive` | message body commands | MARATHON-11 |\\n| Redis/WS fan-out on join/archive | `server/events.py` | MARATHON-13/14 |\\n| SPA create-channel-modal / settings | `static/**` | MARATHON-17/18 |\\n| Changing workspace detail visibility rules | `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` | Already correct in M5 |\\n| IRC JOIN mapping | — | MARATHON-15 |\\n\\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\\n\\n| Hit | Disposition |\\n|-----|-------------|\\n| `server/channels/store.py` — ChannelObj, general, list, read_state | **In scope** — extend |\\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` — create/list/detail/members | **In scope** — add join + create channel only |\\n| `server/workspaces/store.py` — membership helpers | **In scope** — add member insert for open join |\\n| `server/db.py` — v1/v2 | **In scope** — add v3 |\\n| `server/app.py` — routers | **In scope** — mount new routers |\\n| `static/js/shell.js` — `POST .../join` | **Out of scope** — already client-complete; server must satisfy |\\n| `tests/test_workspaces.py` archive fixtures | **Out of scope** — keep green; new tests in `test_channels.py` |\\n| Grep: no `/api/channels` routes yet | Greenfield routes |\\n| `channel-add-member-*` testids in product frontend hooks | **Out of scope** — no REST in Channels contract; separate task |\\n| `server/events.py` | **Out of scope** — no-op OK |\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\\n|-----------|-------------------|\\n| Unauthenticated any new route | **401** |\\n| Create channel name `General` / `eng_ops` / `e` / empty | **400** |\\n| Create name `general` when `#general` exists | **409** |\\n| Concurrent duplicate name | IntegrityError → **409** (no 500) |\\n| Guest creates public channel | **403** |\\n| Member creates `is_private:true` | **403** |\\n| Admin/owner creates private | **201**; creator is only initial channel member |\\n| Topic length 250 OK; 251 → **400** |\\n| Topic PATCH by workspace owner who left channel | **200** allowed (owner clause) |\\n| Topic PATCH by random workspace member not in channel | **403** |\\n| Join public on open as non-member | Workspace row `member` + channel member; **200** |\\n| Join public on invite_only as non-member | **403** (even if they know channel id) |\\n| Join public as guest workspace member | **403** |\\n| Join private without channel_members | **403** |\\n| Join unknown id | **404** |\\n| Leave twice | Both **200** `{channel}` |\\n| Leave `#general` | Allowed; channel remains |\\n| Archive by admin | **403** |\\n| Archive by owner | **200**; `is_archived=true` |\\n| PATCH topic on archived | **423** `archived` |\\n| POST pin on archived | **423** |\\n| GET pins on archived | **200** (read OK) |\\n| Unarchive then pin | **200** |\\n| POST pin twice | Same `pinned_at`/`pinned_by` as first |\\n| DELETE pin when absent | **200** `{unpinned:true}` |\\n| Pin message in other channel’s pin list | Listed only under its `channel_id` |\\n| Workspace join invite_only | **403** |\\n| Workspace join open idempotent | **200**; single membership row |\\n| DM channel create via this POST | Impossible (`is_dm` forced false) |\\n| SQLite busy | busy_timeout; still fail closed after timeout |\\n| Extra JSON fields | Ignore |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` with valid `{name}` as member → **201** `{channel}` with `ChannelObj` keys; `topic` default `\\\"\\\"`; `is_dm=false`; creator in `channel_members`.\\n2. Duplicate channel name in workspace → **409** `conflict`.\\n3. Invalid kebab name or topic \\u003e 250 → **400** `validation_error`.\\n4. Guest create → **403**; member create private → **403**; admin/owner create private → **201**.\\n5. `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` on open as non-member → **200** and subsequent workspace detail succeeds; invite_only → **403**; unknown slug → **404**; already member → **200** idempotent.\\n6. `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` public on open workspace auto-onboards non-member as workspace `member` + channel member → **200**; invite_only non-member → **403**; guest → **403**; private without membership → **403**; unknown → **404**; already member → **200**.\\n7. `POST /api/channels/{id}/leave` twice → both **200** `{channel}`; membership removed after first.\\n8. `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` → **200** `{members:[UserObj,…]}` with exact UserObj keys; private non-member → **403** (unless workspace owner per contract above).\\n9. `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}` as channel member or workspace owner → **200** `{channel}`; archived → **423** `archived`.\\n10. `POST .../archive` and `.../unarchive` owner-only → **200**; non-owner member → **403**.\\n11. `GET /api/channels/{id}/pins` newest-first; private non-member → **403**.\\n12. `POST /api/messages/{id}/pin` idempotent → **200** `{pin:{message_id,pinned_by,pinned_at}}`; `DELETE` → **200** `{unpinned:true}` idempotent; archived channel → **423** on POST/DELETE pin.\\n13. **Cluster:** create channel / join on `:8000`, read members/pins on `:8001` with same token (shared DB).\\n14. **Negative:** must **not** accept `description` as topic; must **not** allow guest public join; must **not** implement message CRUD routes; must **not** store channel SoT in Redis; must **not** change `ChannelObj` key set; must **not** use 404 for archived writes.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Automated\\n\\n**`tests/test_channels.py`**\\n\\n- Register users; create workspace; exercise create public/private + role matrix (seed guest/member/admin via SQL or members PATCH).\\n- Workspace join open vs invite_only (PATCH join_mode as owner first).\\n- Channel join auto-onboard + guest 403 + private 403.\\n- Leave idempotent; members list shape.\\n- Topic validation + owner-without-membership path; 423 when archived.\\n- Archive/unarchive authz + idempotency.\\n- Optional: two `create_app` sharing `data_dir` for cross-node.\\n\\n**`tests/test_pins.py`**\\n\\n- SQL insert message row in a channel; pin/unpin/list ordering; idempotency; private 403; archived 423; unknown message 404.\\n\\n### Manual / cluster\\n\\n```bash\\ncd /app \\u0026\\u0026 ./start.sh \\u0026\\n# register A and B; A creates workspace; B joins via POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join\\n# A creates #eng; B joins channel; A archives; B PATCH topic → 423\\n# seed/post message when available; pin; GET pins on :8001\\n```\\n\\n### Human checks\\n\\n1. SPA join form succeeds on open workspace after this lands.\\n2. Create channel appears on workspace detail for members; private hidden from non-members.\\n3. Owner archive flips `is_archived`; writes return 423 until unarchive.\\n4. Pin list newest-first; delete pin is safe to repeat.\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"Design complete for channels create/join/leave/topic/archive/pins + workspace join (SPA seam). Implements product Channels contract; migration v3 minimal messages+channel_pins; 423 archived guard for M8. Keep label backend for implementer after architect approval.\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:01.554495638Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:01:59.186009979Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"ChannelObj {id,workspace_id,name,is_private,is_dm,topic,is_archived}; topic default \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\", max 250. POST workspaces/{slug}/channels; name kebab \\u003c=32; duplicate 409. Role rules: guest cannot join public or create channels (403); member cannot create private (403); private create admin/owner. Join: open workspace auto-onboards non-members; invite_only non-members 403; private without invite 403. leave idempotent; members list; PATCH topic (member or workspace owner); archive/unarchive owner-only; archived writes → 423. Pins: GET channels/{id}/pins; POST/DELETE messages/{id}/pin per contract.\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-7\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Messages, threads, reactions REST API\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:16.906189799Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-9\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-7\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"DMs: get-or-create DM channel\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:16.923269269Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 34,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-7\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"DESIGN-AUTO-APPROVED pass=16\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:01:59.196756018Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T00:02:34.695Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":391,"interleavedOutput":"time=2026-08-23T00:02:34.695Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-7\",\n  \"title\": \"Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"priority\": 0,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"assignee\": \"backend-dev-1\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"backend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-7 — Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task completes channel lifecycle for Huddle on top of the workspace tenancy shipped in MARATHON-5/6: authenticated callers can create public/private channels under a workspace slug, join and leave channels (with open-workspace auto-onboard and invite_only/guest/private gates), list channel members as `UserObj`, patch topic, archive/unarchive (owner-only), and pin/unpin messages. It also implements the SPA-locked workspace join seam (`POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join`) that MARATHON-16 already calls. It locks the `/api/channels/*` and pin REST contracts, introduces migration **v3** (`messages` minimal + `channel_pins`), and exports a shared **archived-write guard** (`423`) that MARATHON-8/11 must reuse.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite SoT; **migration version 3** additive: minimal `messages` + `channel_pins` (pins need message rows; same “schema-ahead” pattern as M5 channels-before-CRUD) |\\n| Route layout | (1) Extend `server/workspaces/routes.py`: `POST /{slug}/join`, `POST /{slug}/channels`. (2) New `server/channels/routes.py` prefix `/api/channels`: join, leave, PATCH, members, archive, unarchive, pins. (3) New `server/messages/routes.py` (or pin routes mounted under `/api/messages`) for `POST/DELETE /{id}/pin` |\\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all new endpoints require Bearer |\\n| `ChannelObj` | **Unchanged** key set from MARATHON-5 (`CHANNEL_OBJ_KEYS`); this task owns create/mutate behavior |\\n| Workspace join vs channel join | **Both**: SPA uses workspace join (M16); product grader uses channel join with open auto-onboard. Same membership insert helper |\\n| Private “invite” | No private-invite table yet (MARATHON-12). “Without invite” ≡ caller lacks `channel_members` row → **403** on join. Creator is auto-member on create; tests may SQL-seed members until add-member API exists |\\n| Pins without full Message API | Minimal `messages` table + thin `MessageObj` mapper (empty `files`/`reactions`/`mentions`, `reply_count=0`) so pin list/embed works; MARATHON-8 owns message CRUD and enriches the same object |\\n| Archived writes | Shared helper `assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived`; used by topic PATCH + pin mutate now; documented for M8 message/reaction writes |\\n| Events / Redis | No pub/sub (MARATHON-13/14); optional no-op hooks OK but not required |\\n| Timestamps | Reuse `utc_now_z()` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) consistent with M3–M6 |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- Product contract is explicit on paths, envelopes, role matrix, 423, and pin shapes; inventing alternate routes would fail the grader and diverge from SPA settings (MARATHON-17/18).\\n- Workspace join is already wired in `static/js/shell.js`; omitting it leaves onboarding broken despite channel-join auto-onboard.\\n- Introducing a minimal `messages` table for pins mirrors M5 shipping `channels` early — one migration, stable FKs, no pin→message soft-orphan mess.\\n- Centralizing the archived guard prevents M8 from inventing a second 423 code/message.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| Only channel-join auto-onboard; skip workspace join | Breaks MARATHON-16 SPA contract already shipped |\\n| Defer pins entirely to MARATHON-8 | Task + product contract require pin routes in this task |\\n| Pin table without messages; return message stubs | Violates `{pins:[{message,...}]}` and FK integrity |\\n| Allow members to create private channels | Product: member → **403** on `is_private:true` |\\n| Soft 200 on guest join | Product: guest → **403** |\\n| Use `MemberObj` for channel members list | Product: `UserObj[]` under `members` |\\n| 404 for archived writes | Product: **423** |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\nMinimal `messages` lands before message CRUD. Implementers must not invent message POST here; tests for pins SQL-insert message rows (or a tiny test helper). MARATHON-8 must **extend** v3 `messages` (additive columns/tables), not replace the table or diverge `MessageObj` keys listed below.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: UUID4 string ids; `ApiError` + `{error:{code,message}}`; ignore unknown JSON body fields; `400` `validation_error`; `401` `unauthorized`; `409` `conflict` on uniqueness.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: `UserObj` exact keys via `row_to_user_obj`.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-5**: `ChannelObj` exact keys; `WorkspaceObj`; workspace slug resolution; non-member workspace routes → **404** (do not leak); `include_archived` semantics unchanged; `#general` name without `#`.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-6**: roles `owner|admin|member|guest`; **403** `forbidden` when member lacks privilege; `join_mode` ∈ {`open`,`invite_only`}; dual ownership invariant.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-16**: `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` body `{}`; **200** `{workspace}` (+ optional `channels`/`read_state`); open → member; invite_only → 403; unknown → 404; idempotent if already member.\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Shared types\\n\\n#### `ChannelObj` (unchanged)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"workspace_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"eng\\\",\\n  \\\"is_private\\\": false,\\n  \\\"is_dm\\\": false,\\n  \\\"topic\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"is_archived\\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\nExact keys: `id`, `workspace_id`, `name`, `is_private`, `is_dm`, `topic`, `is_archived`.\\n\\n#### `UserObj` (channel members list — MARATHON-4)\\n\\nExact keys: `id`, `username`, `display_name`, `timezone`, `avatar_url`, `status_text`, `status_emoji`.\\n\\n#### Minimal `MessageObj` (for pin embed; MARATHON-8 owns enrichment)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"author_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": { /* UserObj */ },\\n  \\\"body\\\": \\\"hello\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_id\\\": null,\\n  \\\"reply_count\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-08-22T23:00:00Z\\\",\\n  \\\"edited_at\\\": null,\\n  \\\"files\\\": [],\\n  \\\"reactions\\\": [],\\n  \\\"mentions\\\": []\\n}\\n```\\n\\nUntil M8 lands, pin responses use this shape with empty lists / zero reply_count / `edited_at` null when unset. **Do not** omit keys.\\n\\n#### `PinObj` (POST pin response nested under `pin`)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"message_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"pinned_by\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"pinned_at\\\": \\\"2026-08-22T23:00:00Z\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n#### Pin list entry\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"message\\\": { /* MessageObj */ },\\n  \\\"pinned_by\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"pinned_at\\\": \\\"…\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n#### Error codes (this task)\\n\\n| `code` | HTTP | When |\\n|--------|------|------|\\n| `validation_error` | 400 | Bad name/topic; topic \\u003e 250; null where disallowed |\\n| `unauthorized` | 401 | Missing/invalid bearer |\\n| `forbidden` | 403 | Guest create/join; member create private; invite_only non-member join; private join without membership; private pin list/mutate for non-members; archive by non-owner |\\n| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown workspace slug (create/join workspace); unknown channel/message id; non-member on workspace-scoped create (same as M5/6) |\\n| `conflict` | 409 | Duplicate channel name in workspace |\\n| `archived` | 423 | Mutating write against `is_archived=1` channel (topic, pin, and future message writes) |\\n\\n### Role / join capability matrix (normative)\\n\\n| Action | owner | admin | member | guest | non-member (open ws) | non-member (invite_only) |\\n|--------|-------|-------|--------|-------|----------------------|---------------------------|\\n| `POST .../workspaces/{slug}/join` | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | **200** add as `member` | **403** |\\n| `POST .../workspaces/{slug}/channels` public | yes | yes | yes | **403** | **404** | **404** |\\n| `POST .../channels` private (`is_private:true`) | yes | yes | **403** | **403** | **404** | **404** |\\n| `POST /channels/{id}/join` public | yes | yes | yes | **403** | **200** + auto workspace `member` | **403** |\\n| `POST /channels/{id}/join` private, not channel member | **403** | **403** | **403** | **403** | **403** (open) / **403** (invite_only) | **403** |\\n| `POST /channels/{id}/join` private, already channel member | 200 | 200 | 200 | 200* | n/a | n/a |\\n| `POST .../leave` | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | see edge cases | |\\n| `PATCH` topic | channel member **or** workspace owner | same | same | same if channel member | — | — |\\n| `POST archive/unarchive` | **yes** (workspace owner only) | **403** | **403** | **403** | **404** | **404** |\\n\\n\\\\* Guest who somehow has channel membership (seeded) may leave; guest **cannot** newly join public.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M16)** | Bearer; body `{}`; disable submit; on 200 persist slug + enter shell (use returned `channels` if present else detail GET); on 4xx show `join-workspace-error` |\\n| **Server** | Resolve slug; if missing → 404; if already workspace member → 200 `{workspace}` (+ optional channels/read_state); if `join_mode=open` → insert `workspace_members` role=`member`, then return 200; if `invite_only` → 403 |\\n\\n**Recommended 200 body** (SPA-friendly, matches optional M16 fields):\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"workspace\\\": { /* WorkspaceObj */ },\\n  \\\"channels\\\": [ /* visible ChannelObj[] */ ],\\n  \\\"read_state\\\": [ /* ReadStateEntry[] */ ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n`channels`/`read_state` **should** be included using the same visibility rules as `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` (default: exclude archived). Minimum required by M16 is `{workspace}`; including channels avoids a second round-trip.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M17)** | Bearer; body `{name, is_private?, topic?}`; show create-channel modal errors; on 201 append channel to sidebar (`data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name`); on 409 show duplicate-name validation; on 403 show permission error |\\n| **Server** | Require workspace membership; enforce role matrix; validate; insert channel + creator `channel_members`; return 201 |\\n\\n**Request:**\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"name\\\": \\\"eng\\\", \\\"is_private\\\": false, \\\"topic\\\": \\\"optional\\\" }\\n```\\n\\n- `name` required; kebab regex **`^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`** (same family as workspace slug; strip not applied — must already match).\\n- `is_private` optional, default `false`; non-bool → 400.\\n- `topic` optional, default `\\\"\\\"`; if present must be string length ≤ 250 code points; longer → 400.\\n- Unknown fields ignored. Do **not** accept `description` as topic alias (product: no description→topic).\\n- `is_dm` always `false` for this route (DMs are MARATHON-9).\\n\\n**Response 201:** `{ \\\"channel\\\": { /* ChannelObj */ } }`\\n\\n**Errors:** 401; 404 non-member/unknown slug; 403 guest or member+private; 400 validation; 409 duplicate name (`conflict`, e.g. `\\\"channel name already taken\\\"`); IntegrityError race → same 409.\\n\\n**On success transaction:** INSERT channel; INSERT creator into `channel_members`; bump `channels.updated_at`/`created_at`.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/join`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Bearer; empty body; on 200 refresh channel membership / sidebar; on 403/404 surface error |\\n| **Server** | Resolve channel by id; apply join rules below; return **200** (envelope: prefer `{ \\\"channel\\\": ChannelObj }` for consistency with leave/archive; if returning bare 200 with empty body is undesired — **always return `{channel}`**) |\\n\\n**Join algorithm (ordered):**\\n\\n1. Channel missing → **404** `not_found`.\\n2. Load workspace for `channel.workspace_id`.\\n3. If caller already in `channel_members` → **200** `{channel}` (idempotent; no role change).\\n4. If channel `is_private` → **403** `forbidden` (“private without invite”).\\n5. If channel is public (`is_private=0`, `is_dm` irrelevant for join gate here):\\n   - Resolve workspace membership.\\n   - If **not** a workspace member:\\n     - `join_mode=open` → INSERT `workspace_members` (`role=member`) then continue.\\n     - `join_mode=invite_only` → **403**.\\n   - If workspace member with `role=guest` → **403** (cannot join public).\\n   - Else INSERT `channel_members` → **200**.\\n\\n**DM channels (`is_dm=1`):** treat like private for join — non-members **403** (actual DM membership is MARATHON-9). Do not auto-onboard via DM join.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/leave`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Bearer; on 200 update UI (remove from private list / mark left); treat repeat leave as success |\\n| **Server** | Idempotent remove from `channel_members`; return **200** `{channel}` |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n\\n- Unknown channel → **404**.\\n- Public channel: any authenticated user may call leave; if not a member, still **200** `{channel}` (no-op).\\n- Private channel: if caller is not a channel member **and** not a workspace member → **404** (do not leak). If workspace member but not channel member → **200** no-op `{channel}` (idempotent). If channel member → delete membership → **200**.\\n- Leaving does **not** remove workspace membership.\\n- Leave is allowed on archived channels (membership mgmt, not a “write” for 423 purposes).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{id}/members`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M18)** | Bearer; render `channel-members-list` / `channel-member-row` |\\n| **Server** | Authz then return `{members: UserObj[]}` |\\n\\n**Authz:**\\n\\n- Unknown channel → 404.\\n- Public: caller must be **workspace member** else 404.\\n- Private: caller must be **channel member** else **403** (align with pin-list private rule). Workspace owner who is not a channel member still gets **403** unless also a channel member (owner can PATCH topic without membership, but members list follows private pin rule). *Clarification:* workspace **owner** may list members of private channels in their workspace even without channel membership (settings UX); implementer **should** allow workspace owner OR channel member for private member list. Prefer: **channel member OR workspace owner**.\\n\\n**Ordering:** `username ASC` (case-insensitive), tie-break `id ASC`.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `PATCH /api/channels/{id}`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Body `{topic}`; disable topic submit; on 200 update `channel-topic` header; on 423 show archived error |\\n| **Server** | Authz; validate topic; reject if archived; update; return `{channel}` |\\n\\n**Request:** `{ \\\"topic\\\": \\\"Ship week\\\" }` — `topic` required when patching (only mutable field in this task). Omit/`exclude_unset`: empty `{}` → 200 no-op if authorized. Explicit `null` → 400. Max **250** Unicode code points.\\n\\n**Authz:** caller is **channel member** OR **workspace owner** (`workspaces.owner_id`). Else if can see channel → 403; else 404.\\n\\n**Archived:** if `is_archived` → **423** `archived` (do not update).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/archive` and `.../unarchive`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M18)** | Bearer; owner-only controls; on 200 flip archived UI / buttons |\\n| **Server** | Workspace **owner** only; set `is_archived` 1/0; return `{channel}` |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n\\n- Unknown channel → 404.\\n- Caller not workspace member → 404.\\n- Caller member but not `owner_id` → **403**.\\n- Archive when already archived / unarchive when not → **200** idempotent.\\n- Unarchive restores write access (clears 423 path).\\n- These endpoints themselves are **not** subject to 423.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ pins\\n\\n#### `GET /api/channels/{id}/pins` → `200 {pins:[…]}` newest-first (`pinned_at DESC`, tie-break `message_id DESC`)\\n\\n- Unknown channel → 404.\\n- Private + caller not channel member → **403**.\\n- Public + caller not workspace member → 404.\\n- Each entry: `{message: MessageObj, pinned_by, pinned_at}`.\\n- Reads allowed when archived (not a write).\\n\\n#### `POST /api/messages/{id}/pin` → `200 {pin:{message_id,pinned_by,pinned_at}}` idempotent\\n\\n- Unknown message → 404.\\n- Resolve channel from message; apply same visibility as pin list.\\n- If channel archived → **423**.\\n- Caller must be **channel member** (public: must have joined; being only a workspace member of a public channel without `channel_members` → **403**). Workspace owner without channel membership → **403** unless also member (pin is a membership action).\\n- If already pinned → 200 with existing `pinned_by`/`pinned_at` (do not change pinner).\\n- Else INSERT pin with `pinned_by=caller`, `pinned_at=now`.\\n\\n#### `DELETE /api/messages/{id}/pin` → `200 {\\\"unpinned\\\":true}` idempotent\\n\\n- Unknown message → 404.\\n- Same visibility/membership as POST pin.\\n- Archived → **423**.\\n- If no pin row → still **200** `{unpinned:true}`.\\n\\n### Client slow/fail summary\\n\\n| Condition | Client behavior |\\n|-----------|-----------------|\\n| In flight | Disable create/join/topic/archive/pin controls; keep prior lists |\\n| 401 | Re-auth (M16) |\\n| 403 | Show `error.message`; do not optimistic-join |\\n| 409 | Duplicate channel name inline validation |\\n| 423 | Show archived/locked state; disable composers (M17/18) |\\n| 404 | Treat channel/workspace inaccessible |\\n| Network/5xx | Retry; do not assume membership/pin applied |\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Migration v3 (additive, backward compatible)\\n\\n#### `messages` (minimal — MARATHON-8 extends)\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | UUID4 |\\n| `channel_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → channels ON DELETE CASCADE |\\n| `author_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\\n| `body` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| `parent_id` | TEXT | NULL | FK → messages (threads later) |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| `edited_at` | TEXT | NULL | |\\n| `deleted_at` | TEXT | NULL | reserved for M8 soft-delete |\\n\\nIndexes: `idx_messages_channel_id` on `channel_id`.\\n\\n**This task does not expose message CRUD.** Rows exist for pin tests / future M8.\\n\\n#### `channel_pins`\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `message_id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE; one pin per message |\\n| `channel_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → channels (denormalized for list-by-channel) |\\n| `pinned_by` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\\n| `pinned_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UTC Z |\\n\\nIndex: `idx_channel_pins_channel_pinned_at` on `(channel_id, pinned_at DESC)`.\\n\\n### Existing tables used (no change to DDL)\\n\\n- `channels`, `channel_members`, `workspaces`, `workspace_members`, `users`, `channel_read_state`\\n\\n### Schema change summary\\n\\n| Change | Compatible? |\\n|--------|-------------|\\n| v3 new tables | **Yes** — additive |\\n| No alters to v2 columns | **Yes** |\\n\\n### Invariants\\n\\n1. `UNIQUE(workspace_id, name)` on channels enforced; API maps violations to 409.\\n2. Channel create always inserts creator into `channel_members`.\\n3. Open workspace join/channel-join auto-onboard inserts `workspace_members.role='member'` (never owner/admin/guest).\\n4. At most one pin row per `message_id`.\\n5. `is_dm` channels are not creatable via `POST .../channels` (`is_dm=0` always).\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Router `/api/channels`: join, leave, PATCH, members, archive, unarchive, GET pins |\\n| `server/messages/__init__.py` | Package init |\\n| `server/messages/store.py` | Minimal message fetch + `row_to_message_obj` (thin); pin helpers may live here or in channels store |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | `POST/DELETE /api/messages/{id}/pin` |\\n| `tests/test_channels.py` | Contract tests: create/join/leave/topic/archive/roles/423/workspace-join |\\n| `tests/test_pins.py` | Pin list/POST/DELETE/idempotency/403 private/423 archived (SQL-seed messages) |\\n\\n### Modify\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/db.py` | Add `_migrate_v3` / `_reverse_v3`; register in `MIGRATIONS` / `REVERSES` |\\n| `server/channels/store.py` | `validate_channel_name`, `validate_topic`, `create_channel`, `get_channel`, `add_member`, `remove_member`, `list_members_as_users`, `set_archived`, `update_topic`, `assert_channel_writable`, pin list queries; keep existing list/general helpers |\\n| `server/workspaces/store.py` | `add_workspace_member(role='member')` helper for open join / auto-onboard (if not present) |\\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` | `POST /{slug}/join`, `POST /{slug}/channels` |\\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` for channels + messages routers |\\n| `server/channels/__init__.py` | Docstring update if needed |\\n| `server/errors.py` | No change required unless 423 helper desired (prefer raising `ApiError(423,\\\"archived\\\",…)`) |\\n\\n### Do not touch\\n\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `static/**` | Frontend MARATHON-17/18 |\\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume only |\\n| `tests/test_workspaces.py`, `tests/test_workspace_members.py` | Keep green; do not rewrite |\\n| `server/events.py` | Fan-out later |\\n| Message POST/GET/PATCH/DELETE, reactions | MARATHON-8 |\\n| Invitations / private invite redeem | MARATHON-12 |\\n| DM get-or-create | MARATHON-9 |\\n| Slash `/archive` `/topic` | MARATHON-11 (will call same store helpers) |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Build order\\n\\n1. `db.py` v3 migration (+ reverse).\\n2. Channel store mutations + writable guard + workspace member insert helper.\\n3. Workspace routes: join + create channel.\\n4. Channels routes: join/leave/patch/members/archive.\\n5. Messages store thin mapper + pin routes.\\n6. Tests.\\n\\n### Parallelism\\n\\n- Pin routes can proceed in parallel with join/leave once `messages`/`channel_pins` DDL and `get_channel` exist.\\n- Workspace join can land before channel create.\\n\\n### Downstream seams this task owns\\n\\n| Contract | Consumed by |\\n|----------|-------------|\\n| `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` + `ChannelObj` create | MARATHON-17 SPA create modal |\\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` + open auto-onboard | Graders; IRC later; SPA may use later |\\n| `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` | MARATHON-16 shell (already calling) |\\n| leave / members / PATCH topic / archive | MARATHON-18 settings; MARATHON-11 slash cmds |\\n| `assert_channel_writable` → 423 `archived` | MARATHON-8 messages/reactions; MARATHON-11 |\\n| Pin routes + `channel_pins` + minimal `MessageObj` | SPA (future); MARATHON-8 must not break keys |\\n| Minimal `messages` table | MARATHON-8 **must extend**, not drop/recreate |\\n\\n### Upstream\\n\\n- MARATHON-5/6 closed: schema v2, roles, ChannelObj, join_mode.\\n- MARATHON-16 closed: client join path.\\n\\n### Declared dependents\\n\\n- MARATHON-8 (messages), MARATHON-9 (DMs) block on this task.\\n\\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\\n\\n- Message CRUD / reactions / reply_count maintenance → MARATHON-8.\\n- `POST /api/dms` → MARATHON-9.\\n- Private channel add-member / invitations → MARATHON-12 (+ optional channel invite API if still missing).\\n- Slash command side effects → MARATHON-11 (reuse archive/topic store).\\n- WS membership/channel events → MARATHON-13/14.\\n- SPA channel UI → MARATHON-17/18.\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\\n|------|----------------|--------------|\\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages` and message list/edit/delete | future `server/messages/routes.py` CRUD | MARATHON-8 |\\n| Reactions endpoints | `/api/messages/{id}/reactions` | MARATHON-8 |\\n| `POST /api/dms` | — | MARATHON-9 |\\n| Invitation redeem unlocking invite_only join | — | MARATHON-12; this task only 403s non-members |\\n| Explicit `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` add-member | SPA `channel-add-member-*` | Not in product Channels section; file follow-up if M18 needs it before invites — **neighborhood hit**: frontend hooks list add-member controls; **excluded** here; recommend small follow-up or fold into M12/M18 backend notes |\\n| `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` | — | MARATHON-11 |\\n| Slash `/topic` `/archive` | message body commands | MARATHON-11 |\\n| Redis/WS fan-out on join/archive | `server/events.py` | MARATHON-13/14 |\\n| SPA create-channel-modal / settings | `static/**` | MARATHON-17/18 |\\n| Changing workspace detail visibility rules | `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` | Already correct in M5 |\\n| IRC JOIN mapping | — | MARATHON-15 |\\n\\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\\n\\n| Hit | Disposition |\\n|-----|-------------|\\n| `server/channels/store.py` — ChannelObj, general, list, read_state | **In scope** — extend |\\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` — create/list/detail/members | **In scope** — add join + create channel only |\\n| `server/workspaces/store.py` — membership helpers | **In scope** — add member insert for open join |\\n| `server/db.py` — v1/v2 | **In scope** — add v3 |\\n| `server/app.py` — routers | **In scope** — mount new routers |\\n| `static/js/shell.js` — `POST .../join` | **Out of scope** — already client-complete; server must satisfy |\\n| `tests/test_workspaces.py` archive fixtures | **Out of scope** — keep green; new tests in `test_channels.py` |\\n| Grep: no `/api/channels` routes yet | Greenfield routes |\\n| `channel-add-member-*` testids in product frontend hooks | **Out of scope** — no REST in Channels contract; separate task |\\n| `server/events.py` | **Out of scope** — no-op OK |\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\\n|-----------|-------------------|\\n| Unauthenticated any new route | **401** |\\n| Create channel name `General` / `eng_ops` / `e` / empty | **400** |\\n| Create name `general` when `#general` exists | **409** |\\n| Concurrent duplicate name | IntegrityError → **409** (no 500) |\\n| Guest creates public channel | **403** |\\n| Member creates `is_private:true` | **403** |\\n| Admin/owner creates private | **201**; creator is only initial channel member |\\n| Topic length 250 OK; 251 → **400** |\\n| Topic PATCH by workspace owner who left channel | **200** allowed (owner clause) |\\n| Topic PATCH by random workspace member not in channel | **403** |\\n| Join public on open as non-member | Workspace row `member` + channel member; **200** |\\n| Join public on invite_only as non-member | **403** (even if they know channel id) |\\n| Join public as guest workspace member | **403** |\\n| Join private without channel_members | **403** |\\n| Join unknown id | **404** |\\n| Leave twice | Both **200** `{channel}` |\\n| Leave `#general` | Allowed; channel remains |\\n| Archive by admin | **403** |\\n| Archive by owner | **200**; `is_archived=true` |\\n| PATCH topic on archived | **423** `archived` |\\n| POST pin on archived | **423** |\\n| GET pins on archived | **200** (read OK) |\\n| Unarchive then pin | **200** |\\n| POST pin twice | Same `pinned_at`/`pinned_by` as first |\\n| DELETE pin when absent | **200** `{unpinned:true}` |\\n| Pin message in other channel’s pin list | Listed only under its `channel_id` |\\n| Workspace join invite_only | **403** |\\n| Workspace join open idempotent | **200**; single membership row |\\n| DM channel create via this POST | Impossible (`is_dm` forced false) |\\n| SQLite busy | busy_timeout; still fail closed after timeout |\\n| Extra JSON fields | Ignore |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` with valid `{name}` as member → **201** `{channel}` with `ChannelObj` keys; `topic` default `\\\"\\\"`; `is_dm=false`; creator in `channel_members`.\\n2. Duplicate channel name in workspace → **409** `conflict`.\\n3. Invalid kebab name or topic \\u003e 250 → **400** `validation_error`.\\n4. Guest create → **403**; member create private → **403**; admin/owner create private → **201**.\\n5. `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` on open as non-member → **200** and subsequent workspace detail succeeds; invite_only → **403**; unknown slug → **404**; already member → **200** idempotent.\\n6. `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` public on open workspace auto-onboards non-member as workspace `member` + channel member → **200**; invite_only non-member → **403**; guest → **403**; private without membership → **403**; unknown → **404**; already member → **200**.\\n7. `POST /api/channels/{id}/leave` twice → both **200** `{channel}`; membership removed after first.\\n8. `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` → **200** `{members:[UserObj,…]}` with exact UserObj keys; private non-member → **403** (unless workspace owner per contract above).\\n9. `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}` as channel member or workspace owner → **200** `{channel}`; archived → **423** `archived`.\\n10. `POST .../archive` and `.../unarchive` owner-only → **200**; non-owner member → **403**.\\n11. `GET /api/channels/{id}/pins` newest-first; private non-member → **403**.\\n12. `POST /api/messages/{id}/pin` idempotent → **200** `{pin:{message_id,pinned_by,pinned_at}}`; `DELETE` → **200** `{unpinned:true}` idempotent; archived channel → **423** on POST/DELETE pin.\\n13. **Cluster:** create channel / join on `:8000`, read members/pins on `:8001` with same token (shared DB).\\n14. **Negative:** must **not** accept `description` as topic; must **not** allow guest public join; must **not** implement message CRUD routes; must **not** store channel SoT in Redis; must **not** change `ChannelObj` key set; must **not** use 404 for archived writes.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Automated\\n\\n**`tests/test_channels.py`**\\n\\n- Register users; create workspace; exercise create public/private + role matrix (seed guest/member/admin via SQL or members PATCH).\\n- Workspace join open vs invite_only (PATCH join_mode as owner first).\\n- Channel join auto-onboard + guest 403 + private 403.\\n- Leave idempotent; members list shape.\\n- Topic validation + owner-without-membership path; 423 when archived.\\n- Archive/unarchive authz + idempotency.\\n- Optional: two `create_app` sharing `data_dir` for cross-node.\\n\\n**`tests/test_pins.py`**\\n\\n- SQL insert message row in a channel; pin/unpin/list ordering; idempotency; private 403; archived 423; unknown message 404.\\n\\n### Manual / cluster\\n\\n```bash\\ncd /app \\u0026\\u0026 ./start.sh \\u0026\\n# register A and B; A creates workspace; B joins via POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join\\n# A creates #eng; B joins channel; A archives; B PATCH topic → 423\\n# seed/post message when available; pin; GET pins on :8001\\n```\\n\\n### Human checks\\n\\n1. SPA join form succeeds on open workspace after this lands.\\n2. Create channel appears on workspace detail for members; private hidden from non-members.\\n3. Owner archive flips `is_archived`; writes return 423 until unarchive.\\n4. Pin list newest-first; delete pin is safe to repeat.\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"Design complete for channels create/join/leave/topic/archive/pins + workspace join (SPA seam). Implements product Channels contract; migration v3 minimal messages+channel_pins; 423 archived guard for M8. Keep label backend for implementer after architect approval.\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:01.554495638Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:01:59.186009979Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"ChannelObj {id,workspace_id,name,is_private,is_dm,topic,is_archived}; topic default \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\", max 250. POST workspaces/{slug}/channels; name kebab \\u003c=32; duplicate 409. Role rules: guest cannot join public or create channels (403); member cannot create private (403); private create admin/owner. Join: open workspace auto-onboards non-members; invite_only non-members 403; private without invite 403. leave idempotent; members list; PATCH topic (member or workspace owner); archive/unarchive owner-only; archived writes → 423. Pins: GET channels/{id}/pins; POST/DELETE messages/{id}/pin per contract.\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-7\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Messages, threads, reactions REST API\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:16.906189799Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-9\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-7\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"DMs: get-or-create DM channel\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:16.923269269Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 34,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-7\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"DESIGN-AUTO-APPROVED pass=16\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:01:59.196756018Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","localExecutionTimeMs":59},"isBackground":false},"description":"Show MARATHON-7 task details"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-9d8c7914-0bf9-48ec-b9b2-153bdc99f7f2-1\nfc_7c6147e8-c784-9e1a-a719-f4a9069dfa9c_1","startedAtMs":"1787443354337","completedAtMs":"1787443354728"},"model_call_id":"672ed06b-632c-4763-9960-4aa8b819dbd0-0-yk1u","session_id":"86bf3402-21e8-4aa3-94a1-667e1b9066f8","timestamp_ms":1787443354785}
