e,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/m7-design.md"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Extract full design to file","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"86bf3402-21e8-4aa3-94a1-667e1b9066f8","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-7 --output json | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint(d['design'])\n\" > /tmp/m7-design.md && wc -l /tmp/m7-design.md && grep -n '^## \\|^### \\|POST \\|GET \\|PATCH \\|DELETE \\|CREATE TABLE\\|assert_channel\\|ChannelObj\\|validation\\|kebab' /tmp/m7-design.md | head -80","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"566 /tmp/m7-design.md\n3:## Summary\n5:This task completes channel lifecycle for Huddle on top of the workspace tenancy shipped in MARATHON-5/6: authenticated callers can create public/private channels under a workspace slug, join and leave channels (with open-workspace auto-onboard and invite_only/guest/private gates), list channel members as `UserObj`, patch topic, archive/unarchive (owner-only), and pin/unpin messages. It also implements the SPA-locked workspace join seam (`POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join`) that MARATHON-16 already calls. It locks the `/api/channels/*` and pin REST contracts, introduces migration **v3** (`messages` minimal + `channel_pins`), and exports a shared **archived-write guard** (`423`) that MARATHON-8/11 must reuse.\n7:## Technical Approach\n9:### Decision\n14:| Route layout | (1) Extend `server/workspaces/routes.py`: `POST /{slug}/join`, `POST /{slug}/channels`. (2) New `server/channels/routes.py` prefix `/api/channels`: join, leave, PATCH, members, archive, unarchive, pins. (3) New `server/messages/routes.py` (or pin routes mounted under `/api/messages`) for `POST/DELETE /{id}/pin` |\n16:| `ChannelObj` | **Unchanged** key set from MARATHON-5 (`CHANNEL_OBJ_KEYS`); this task owns create/mutate behavior |\n20:| Archived writes | Shared helper `assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived`; used by topic PATCH + pin mutate now; documented for M8 message/reaction writes |\n24:### Why\n31:### Alternatives considered\n43:### Trade-off accepted\n45:Minimal `messages` lands before message CRUD. Implementers must not invent message POST here; tests for pins SQL-insert message rows (or a tiny test helper). MARATHON-8 must **extend** v3 `messages` (additive columns/tables), not replace the table or diverge `MessageObj` keys listed below.\n47:### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n49:From **MARATHON-3**: UUID4 string ids; `ApiError` + `{error:{code,message}}`; ignore unknown JSON body fields; `400` `validation_error`; `401` `unauthorized`; `409` `conflict` on uniqueness.\n53:From **MARATHON-5**: `ChannelObj` exact keys; `WorkspaceObj`; workspace slug resolution; non-member workspace routes → **404** (do not leak); `include_archived` semantics unchanged; `#general` name without `#`.\n57:From **MARATHON-16**: `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` body `{}`; **200** `{workspace}` (+ optional `channels`/`read_state`); open → member; invite_only → 403; unknown → 404; idempotent if already member.\n59:## Interface Contracts\n61:### Shared types\n63:#### `ChannelObj` (unchanged)\n104:#### `PinObj` (POST pin response nested under `pin`)\n128:| `validation_error` | 400 | Bad name/topic; topic > 250; null where disallowed |\n135:### Role / join capability matrix (normative)\n139:| `POST .../workspaces/{slug}/join` | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | **200** add as `member` | **403** |\n140:| `POST .../workspaces/{slug}/channels` public | yes | yes | yes | **403** | **404** | **404** |\n141:| `POST .../channels` private (`is_private:true`) | yes | yes | **403** | **403** | **404** | **404** |\n142:| `POST /channels/{id}/join` public | yes | yes | yes | **403** | **200** + auto workspace `member` | **403** |\n143:| `POST /channels/{id}/join` private, not channel member | **403** | **403** | **403** | **403** | **403** (open) / **403** (invite_only) | **403** |\n144:| `POST /channels/{id}/join` private, already channel member | 200 | 200 | 200 | 200* | n/a | n/a |\n145:| `POST .../leave` | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | see edge cases | |\n147:| `POST archive/unarchive` | **yes** (workspace owner only) | **403** | **403** | **403** | **404** | **404** |\n151:### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join`\n163:  \"channels\": [ /* visible ChannelObj[] */ ],\n168:`channels`/`read_state` **should** be included using the same visibility rules as `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` (default: exclude archived). Minimum required by M16 is `{workspace}`; including channels avoids a second round-trip.\n170:### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels`\n174:| **Client (SPA M17)** | Bearer; body `{name, is_private?, topic?}`; show create-channel modal errors; on 201 append channel to sidebar (`data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name`); on 409 show duplicate-name validation; on 403 show permission error |\n183:- `name` required; kebab regex **`^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`** (same family as workspace slug; strip not applied — must already match).\n189:**Response 201:** `{ \"channel\": { /* ChannelObj */ } }`\n191:**Errors:** 401; 404 non-member/unknown slug; 403 guest or member+private; 400 validation; 409 duplicate name (`conflict`, e.g. `\"channel name already taken\"`); IntegrityError race → same 409.\n195:### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/join`\n200:| **Server** | Resolve channel by id; apply join rules below; return **200** (envelope: prefer `{ \"channel\": ChannelObj }` for consistency with leave/archive; if returning bare 200 with empty body is undesired — **always return `{channel}`**) |\n218:### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/leave`\n233:### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{id}/members`\n244:- Private: caller must be **channel member** else **403** (align with pin-list private rule). Workspace owner who is not a channel member still gets **403** unless also a channel member (owner can PATCH topic without membership, but members list follows private pin rule). *Clarification:* workspace **owner** may list members of private channels in their workspace even without channel membership (settings UX); implementer **should** allow workspace owner OR channel member for private member list. Prefer: **channel member OR workspace owner**.\n248:### Seam: Client ↔ `PATCH /api/channels/{id}`\n261:### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/archive` and `.../unarchive`\n277:### Seam: Client ↔ pins\n279:#### `GET /api/channels/{id}/pins` → `200 {pins:[…]}` newest-first (`pinned_at DESC`, tie-break `message_id DESC`)\n287:#### `POST /api/messages/{id}/pin` → `200 {pin:{message_id,pinned_by,pinned_at}}` idempotent\n296:#### `DELETE /api/messages/{id}/pin` → `200 {\"unpinned\":true}` idempotent\n299:- Same visibility/membership as POST pin.\n303:### Client slow/fail summary\n310:| 409 | Duplicate channel name inline validation |\n315:## Data Model\n317:### Migration v3 (additive, backward compatible)\n324:| `channel_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → channels ON DELETE CASCADE |\n340:| `message_id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE; one pin per message |\n347:### Existing tables used (no change to DDL)\n351:### Schema change summary\n358:### Invariants\n364:5. `is_dm` channels are not creatable via `POST .../channels` (`is_dm=0` always).\n366:## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n368:### Create\n372:| `server/channels/routes.py` | Router `/api/channels`: join, leave, PATCH, members, archive, unarchive, GET pins |\n375:| `server/messages/routes.py` | `POST/DELETE /api/messages/{id}/pin` |\n379:### Modify\n384:| `server/channels/store.py` | `validate_channel_name`, `validate_topic`, `create_channel`, `get_channel`, `add_member`, `remove_member`, `list_members_as_users`, `set_archived`, `update_topic`, 