{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-81dc70c8-aae1-49d5-ba5f-d0ec413a95ec-14\nfc_a5cd70a0-4228-9218-ad66-cbb4cc128846_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/m7-design.md","offset":170,"limit":220}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-81dc70c8-aae1-49d5-ba5f-d0ec413a95ec-14\nfc_a5cd70a0-4228-9218-ad66-cbb4cc128846_0","startedAtMs":"1787443380457"},"model_call_id":"672ed06b-632c-4763-9960-4aa8b819dbd0-3-s1in","session_id":"86bf3402-21e8-4aa3-94a1-667e1b9066f8","timestamp_ms":1787443380768}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-81dc70c8-aae1-49d5-ba5f-d0ec413a95ec-14\nfc_a5cd70a0-4228-9218-ad66-cbb4cc128846_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/m7-design.md","offset":170,"limit":220},"result":{"success":{"content":"### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client (SPA M17)** | Bearer; body `{name, is_private?, topic?}`; show create-channel modal errors; on 201 append channel to sidebar (`data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name`); on 409 show duplicate-name validation; on 403 show permission error |\n| **Server** | Require workspace membership; enforce role matrix; validate; insert channel + creator `channel_members`; return 201 |\n\n**Request:**\n\n```json\n{ \"name\": \"eng\", \"is_private\": false, \"topic\": \"optional\" }\n```\n\n- `name` required; kebab regex **`^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`** (same family as workspace slug; strip not applied — must already match).\n- `is_private` optional, default `false`; non-bool → 400.\n- `topic` optional, default `\"\"`; if present must be string length ≤ 250 code points; longer → 400.\n- Unknown fields ignored. Do **not** accept `description` as topic alias (product: no description→topic).\n- `is_dm` always `false` for this route (DMs are MARATHON-9).\n\n**Response 201:** `{ \"channel\": { /* ChannelObj */ } }`\n\n**Errors:** 401; 404 non-member/unknown slug; 403 guest or member+private; 400 validation; 409 duplicate name (`conflict`, e.g. `\"channel name already taken\"`); IntegrityError race → same 409.\n\n**On success transaction:** INSERT channel; INSERT creator into `channel_members`; bump `channels.updated_at`/`created_at`.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/join`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Bearer; empty body; on 200 refresh channel membership / sidebar; on 403/404 surface error |\n| **Server** | Resolve channel by id; apply join rules below; return **200** (envelope: prefer `{ \"channel\": ChannelObj }` for consistency with leave/archive; if returning bare 200 with empty body is undesired — **always return `{channel}`**) |\n\n**Join algorithm (ordered):**\n\n1. Channel missing → **404** `not_found`.\n2. Load workspace for `channel.workspace_id`.\n3. If caller already in `channel_members` → **200** `{channel}` (idempotent; no role change).\n4. If channel `is_private` → **403** `forbidden` (“private without invite”).\n5. If channel is public (`is_private=0`, `is_dm` irrelevant for join gate here):\n   - Resolve workspace membership.\n   - If **not** a workspace member:\n     - `join_mode=open` → INSERT `workspace_members` (`role=member`) then continue.\n     - `join_mode=invite_only` → **403**.\n   - If workspace member with `role=guest` → **403** (cannot join public).\n   - Else INSERT `channel_members` → **200**.\n\n**DM channels (`is_dm=1`):** treat like private for join — non-members **403** (actual DM membership is MARATHON-9). Do not auto-onboard via DM join.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/leave`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Bearer; on 200 update UI (remove from private list / mark left); treat repeat leave as success |\n| **Server** | Idempotent remove from `channel_members`; return **200** `{channel}` |\n\n**Rules:**\n\n- Unknown channel → **404**.\n- Public channel: any authenticated user may call leave; if not a member, still **200** `{channel}` (no-op).\n- Private channel: if caller is not a channel member **and** not a workspace member → **404** (do not leak). If workspace member but not channel member → **200** no-op `{channel}` (idempotent). If channel member → delete membership → **200**.\n- Leaving does **not** remove workspace membership.\n- Leave is allowed on archived channels (membership mgmt, not a “write” for 423 purposes).\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{id}/members`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client (SPA M18)** | Bearer; render `channel-members-list` / `channel-member-row` |\n| **Server** | Authz then return `{members: UserObj[]}` |\n\n**Authz:**\n\n- Unknown channel → 404.\n- Public: caller must be **workspace member** else 404.\n- Private: caller must be **channel member** else **403** (align with pin-list private rule). Workspace owner who is not a channel member still gets **403** unless also a channel member (owner can PATCH topic without membership, but members list follows private pin rule). *Clarification:* workspace **owner** may list members of private channels in their workspace even without channel membership (settings UX); implementer **should** allow workspace owner OR channel member for private member list. Prefer: **channel member OR workspace owner**.\n\n**Ordering:** `username ASC` (case-insensitive), tie-break `id ASC`.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `PATCH /api/channels/{id}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Body `{topic}`; disable topic submit; on 200 update `channel-topic` header; on 423 show archived error |\n| **Server** | Authz; validate topic; reject if archived; update; return `{channel}` |\n\n**Request:** `{ \"topic\": \"Ship week\" }` — `topic` required when patching (only mutable field in this task). Omit/`exclude_unset`: empty `{}` → 200 no-op if authorized. Explicit `null` → 400. Max **250** Unicode code points.\n\n**Authz:** caller is **channel member** OR **workspace owner** (`workspaces.owner_id`). Else if can see channel → 403; else 404.\n\n**Archived:** if `is_archived` → **423** `archived` (do not update).\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/archive` and `.../unarchive`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client (SPA M18)** | Bearer; owner-only controls; on 200 flip archived UI / buttons |\n| **Server** | Workspace **owner** only; set `is_archived` 1/0; return `{channel}` |\n\n**Rules:**\n\n- Unknown channel → 404.\n- Caller not workspace member → 404.\n- Caller member but not `owner_id` → **403**.\n- Archive when already archived / unarchive when not → **200** idempotent.\n- Unarchive restores write access (clears 423 path).\n- These endpoints themselves are **not** subject to 423.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ pins\n\n#### `GET /api/channels/{id}/pins` → `200 {pins:[…]}` newest-first (`pinned_at DESC`, tie-break `message_id DESC`)\n\n- Unknown channel → 404.\n- Private + caller not channel member → **403**.\n- Public + caller not workspace member → 404.\n- Each entry: `{message: MessageObj, pinned_by, pinned_at}`.\n- Reads allowed when archived (not a write).\n\n#### `POST /api/messages/{id}/pin` → `200 {pin:{message_id,pinned_by,pinned_at}}` idempotent\n\n- Unknown message → 404.\n- Resolve channel from message; apply same visibility as pin list.\n- If channel archived → **423**.\n- Caller must be **channel member** (public: must have joined; being only a workspace member of a public channel without `channel_members` → **403**). Workspace owner without channel membership → **403** unless also member (pin is a membership action).\n- If already pinned → 200 with existing `pinned_by`/`pinned_at` (do not change pinner).\n- Else INSERT pin with `pinned_by=caller`, `pinned_at=now`.\n\n#### `DELETE /api/messages/{id}/pin` → `200 {\"unpinned\":true}` idempotent\n\n- Unknown message → 404.\n- Same visibility/membership as POST pin.\n- Archived → **423**.\n- If no pin row → still **200** `{unpinned:true}`.\n\n### Client slow/fail summary\n\n| Condition | Client behavior |\n|-----------|-----------------|\n| In flight | Disable create/join/topic/archive/pin controls; keep prior lists |\n| 401 | Re-auth (M16) |\n| 403 | Show `error.message`; do not optimistic-join |\n| 409 | Duplicate channel name inline validation |\n| 423 | Show archived/locked state; disable composers (M17/18) |\n| 404 | Treat channel/workspace inaccessible |\n| Network/5xx | Retry; do not assume membership/pin applied |\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Migration v3 (additive, backward compatible)\n\n#### `messages` (minimal — MARATHON-8 extends)\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | UUID4 |\n| `channel_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → channels ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `author_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\n| `body` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| `parent_id` | TEXT | NULL | FK → messages (threads later) |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| `edited_at` | TEXT | NULL | |\n| `deleted_at` | TEXT | NULL | reserved for M8 soft-delete |\n\nIndexes: `idx_messages_channel_id` on `channel_id`.\n\n**This task does not expose message CRUD.** Rows exist for pin tests / future M8.\n\n#### `channel_pins`\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `message_id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE; one pin per message |\n| `channel_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → channels (denormalized for list-by-channel) |\n| `pinned_by` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\n| `pinned_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UTC Z |\n\nIndex: `idx_channel_pins_channel_pinned_at` on `(channel_id, pinned_at DESC)`.\n\n### Existing tables used (no change to DDL)\n\n- `channels`, `channel_members`, `workspaces`, `workspace_members`, `users`, `channel_read_state`\n\n### Schema change summary\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| v3 new tables | **Yes** — additive |\n| No alters to v2 columns | **Yes** |\n\n### Invariants\n\n1. `UNIQUE(workspace_id, name)` on channels enforced; API maps violations to 409.\n2. Channel create always inserts creator into `channel_members`.\n3. Open workspace join/channel-join auto-onboard inserts `workspace_members.role='member'` (never owner/admin/guest).\n4. At most one pin row per `message_id`.\n5. `is_dm` channels are not creatable via `POST .../channels` (`is_dm=0` always).\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Router `/api/channels`: join, leave, PATCH, members, archive, unarchive, GET pins |\n| `server/messages/__init__.py` | Package init |\n| `server/messages/store.py` | Minimal message fetch + `row_to_message_obj` (thin); pin helpers may live here or in channels store |\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | `POST/DELETE /api/messages/{id}/pin` |\n| `tests/test_channels.py` | Contract tests: create/join/leave/topic/archive/roles/423/workspace-join |\n| `tests/test_pins.py` | Pin list/POST/DELETE/idempotency/403 private/423 archived (SQL-seed messages) |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/db.py` | Add `_migrate_v3` / `_reverse_v3`; register in `MIGRATIONS` / `REVERSES` |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | `validate_channel_name`, `validate_topic`, `create_channel`, `get_channel`, `add_member`, `remove_member`, `list_members_as_users`, `set_archived`, `update_topic`, `assert_channel_writable`, pin list queries; keep existing list/general helpers |\n| `server/workspaces/store.py` | `add_workspace_member(role='member')` helper for open join / auto-onboard (if not present) |\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` | `POST /{slug}/join`, `POST /{slug}/channels` |\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` for channels + messages routers |\n| `server/channels/__init__.py` | Docstring update if needed |\n| `server/errors.py` | No change required unless 423 helper desired (prefer raising `ApiError(423,\"archived\",…)`) |","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":567,"fileSize":30076,"path":"/tmp/m7-design.md","readRange":{"startLine":170,"endLine":389},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-81dc70c8-aae1-49d5-ba5f-d0ec413a95ec-14\nfc_a5cd70a0-4228-9218-ad66-cbb4cc128846_0","startedAtMs":"1787443380457","completedAtMs":"1787443380799"},"model_call_id":"672ed06b-632c-4763-9960-4aa8b819dbd0-3-s1in","session_id":"86bf3402-21e8-4aa3-94a1-667e1b9066f8","timestamp_ms":1787443380821}
