:true,"conversationId":"0a8fcafb-36dc-47ae-b858-91f084f7ec96","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-1 && loom data show MARATHON-12 --output json | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print('depends_on:', d.get('depends_on')); print('parent:', d.get('parent')); print('comments:', [(c.get('author'), c.get('text')[:80]) for c in d.get('comments',[])])\"","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"ID:       MARATHON-1\nTitle:    Huddle: Slack-like team chat cluster\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 2\nType:     epic\nOwner:    marathon-harness\n\nDescription:\nBuild a self-contained Slack-like team chat at /app. Verifier runs /app/start.sh (foreground) which must keep serving while alive.\n\nExpose HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002, IRC on :6667, browser UI at GET /. Local Redis pub/sub on :6379. No remote services, no DinD, no Slack SDK.\n\nProduct: auth, profiles, workspaces, invitations, roles, public/private channels, DMs, messages, threads, reactions, pins, files, search, user groups, slash commands, mentions, read state, settings, SPA.\n\nCluster: dense per-channel seq shared across HTTP+IRC; replay after reconnect to different node; fan-out across nodes; survive one HTTP node SIGKILL (respawn <60s); survive Redis SIGKILL with continued dense fan-out within 5s then Redis respawn.\n\nAPI: REST + bearer auth, JSON envelopes, stable ids, UTC timestamps. UI: stable data-testid/selectors for CUA/Playwright at 1280x900.\ndepends_on: None\nparent: MARATHON-1\ncomments: [('marathon-harness', 'DESIGN-AUTO-APPROVED pass=18')]\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T00:14:35.271Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T00:14:35.299Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":97,"interleavedOutput":"time=2026-08-23T00:14:35.271Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\"