{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-3b1678ab-a074-4edd-a5c9-2a070542b995-7\nfc_04707843-9866-93e5-8c2d-914d823c6f0e_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-12 --output json | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d['design']\n# print from Invitation section through data model\nidx=design.find('### Seam: Invitations')\nprint(design[idx:idx+8000] if idx>=0 else 'not found')\nprint('---')\nidx2=design.find('## Data Model')\nprint(design[idx2:idx2+5000] if idx2>=0 else 'no data model')\n\"","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-3b1678ab-a074-4edd-a5c9-2a070542b995-7\nfc_04707843-9866-93e5-8c2d-914d823c6f0e_0","simpleCommands":["loom","python3"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-12"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-12 --output json"},{"name":"python3","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"string","value":"\"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d['design']\n# print from Invitation section through data model\nidx=design.find('### Seam: Invitations')\nprint(design[idx:idx+8000] if idx>=0 else 'not found')\nprint('---')\nidx2=design.find('## Data Model')\nprint(design[idx2:idx2+5000] if idx2>=0 else 'no data model')\n\""}],"fullText":"python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d['design']\n# print from Invitation section through data model\nidx=design.find('### Seam: Invitations')\nprint(design[idx:idx+8000] if idx>=0 else 'not found')\nprint('---')\nidx2=design.find('## Data Model')\nprint(design[idx2:idx2+5000] if idx2>=0 else 'no data model')\n\""}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Extract invitation contract and data model","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"0a8fcafb-36dc-47ae-b858-91f084f7ec96","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-12 --output json | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d['design']\n# print from Invitation section through data model\nidx=design.find('### Seam: Invitations')\nprint(design[idx:idx+8000] if idx>=0 else 'not found')\nprint('---')\nidx2=design.find('## Data Model')\nprint(design[idx2:idx2+5000] if idx2>=0 else 'no data model')\n\"","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"### Seam: Invitations (workspace-scoped admin)\n\n#### `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations`\n\n**Authz:** workspace **owner or admin** → else member **403** / non-member **404**.\n\n**Body:**\n```json\n{\n  \"expires_in_seconds\": 86400,\n  \"max_uses\": 1,\n  \"invited_username\": \"ada\",\n  \"invited_user_id\": null\n}\n```\nAll fields optional. Unknown keys ignored.\n\n| Field | Rules |\n|-------|-------|\n| `expires_in_seconds` | Omit/null → no expiry. If set: integer **≥ 60** and **≤ 2592000** (30d); else 400. `expires_at = now + seconds`. |\n| `max_uses` | Omit → **1**. If set: integer **≥ 1** and **≤ 1000**; else 400. |\n| `invited_user_id` | If set: must exist in `users`; else 400. |\n| `invited_username` | If set: resolve via username (case-sensitive per Auth store); unknown → 400. |\n| Both target fields | Must resolve to the **same** user; else 400. |\n| Targeted | Force `max_uses = 1`. If client sends `max_uses` > 1 with a target → **400** `validation_error`. |\n\n**Response 201:** `{ \"invitation\": InvitationObj }`  \n`use_count=0`; `code` unique globally.\n\n#### `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations`\n\n**Authz:** owner/admin; others 403/404 as above.\n\n**Semantics — active only:** `revoked_at IS NULL` AND (`expires_at IS NULL` OR `expires_at > now`) AND `use_count < max_uses`.\n\nOrder: `created_at` DESC.\n\n**Response 200:** `{ \"invitations\": [ InvitationObj, ... ] }`\n\n---\n\n### Seam: Invitation redeem / revoke (code-scoped)\n\n#### `POST /api/invitations/{code}/accept`\n\n**Authz:** any authenticated user (no prior workspace membership required).\n\n| Condition | HTTP | code |\n|-----------|------|------|\n| Unknown code | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Revoked | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Expired (`expires_at <= now`) | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Exhausted (`use_count >= max_uses`) | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Targeted and caller.id ≠ invited_user_id | **403** | `forbidden` |\n| Success (new or already member) | **200** | — |\n\n**Body:** `{}` or empty; ignore extras.\n\n**Response 200:**\n```json\n{\n  \"workspace\": { /* WorkspaceObj */ },\n  \"channels\": [ /* ChannelObj[] visible to caller after join */ ],\n  \"read_state\": []\n}\n```\nShape mirrors workspace detail / join success so SPA can `enterWorkspace` without a second round-trip. `channels` at minimum includes public `#general` (and any other publics per M5 visibility). `read_state` may be `[]`.\n\n**Server work (transaction):**\n1. Lock/select invitation by code; evaluate status → 404/403 as above.\n2. If caller not in `workspace_members`: INSERT role=`member`; INSERT `#general` into `channel_members` if missing; `use_count += 1`.\n3. If already member: no `use_count` change; still return workspace payload.\n4. Commit.\n\n**Client:** on success treat like join; on 403 show forbidden; on 404 show invalid/expired invite; while slow disable submit.\n\n#### `DELETE /api/invitations/{code}`\n\n**Authz:** resolve invitation → workspace; caller must be **owner or admin** of that workspace. Non-member of that workspace → **404**. Member but not admin/owner → **403**. Unknown/already-revoked → **404** (idempotent revoke of missing → 404, not 200).\n\n**Effect:** set `revoked_at = now` (soft revoke).\n\n**Response 200:** `{ \"revoked\": true }`\n\n---\n\n### Seam: invite_only join gate (cross-task)\n\n| Endpoint (MARATHON-7) | Behavior with this task |\n|----------------------|-------------------------|\n| `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` | `open` + non-member → add member (M7). `invite_only` + non-member → **403** (unchanged). After accept, caller is member → join is idempotent 200. |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` | invite_only workspace + non-member → **403** (unchanged). Members who accepted can join public channels per M7. |\n\n**Shared helper (this task owns the name/contract):**  \n`workspaces_store.add_workspace_member(conn, workspace_id=, user_id=, role=\"member\")` — INSERT OR ignore / check-then-insert; used by accept and by M7 open-join.\n\nIf M7 is not yet merged when implementing: still ship the helper + accept path; add a short comment at the future join call sites documenting the invite_only 403 rule (already in M7 design). When M7 lands, join **must** call the same helper (do not duplicate INSERT logic).\n\n---\n\n### Error code summary\n\n| code | HTTP | When |\n|------|------|------|\n| `validation_error` | 400 | Bad handle/name/user_ids/expiry/max_uses/target mismatch |\n| `unauthorized` | 401 | Missing/invalid bearer |\n| `forbidden` | 403 | Guest creates group; non-creator non-owner mutates group; non-admin invitation admin APIs; targeted accept by wrong user |\n| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown slug/handle/code; non-member on workspace-scoped routes; inactive invites |\n| `conflict` | 409 | Duplicate group handle in workspace |\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Migration **v4** (additive, backward compatible)\n\n#### `user_groups`\n\n| Column | Type | Notes |\n|--------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | UUID4 |\n| `workspace_id` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK workspaces ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `handle` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| `name` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| `created_by` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK users |\n| `created_at` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| `updated_at` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| UNIQUE `(workspace_id, handle)` | | |\n\n#### `user_group_members`\n\n| Column | Type | Notes |\n|--------|------|-------|\n| `group_id` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK user_groups ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `user_id` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK users ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `created_at` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| PRIMARY KEY `(group_id, user_id)` | | |\n\nIndex: `user_group_members(user_id)` optional.\n\n#### `workspace_invitations`\n\n| Column | Type | Notes |\n|--------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | UUID4 |\n| `workspace_id` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK workspaces ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `code` | TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE | |\n| `created_by` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK users |\n| `created_at` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| `expires_at` | TEXT NULL | |\n| `max_uses` | INTEGER NOT NULL | |\n| `use_count` | INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 | |\n| `invited_user_id` | TEXT NULL | FK users |\n| `invited_username` | TEXT NULL | snapshot at create |\n| `revoked_at` | TEXT NULL | null = not revoked |\n\nIndex: `workspace_invitations(workspace_id)`; unique on `code`.\n\n**No changes** to `workspaces.join_mode` CHECK or `workspace_members` schema.\n\n**Reverse v4:** DROP the three tables (local verification only), matching M2/M3 reverse style.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/groups/__init__.py` | Package marker |\n| `server/groups/store.py` | Handle/name validation; CRUD; `row_to_group_obj`; membership replace |\n| `server/groups/routes.py` | GET/POST list-create; PATCH/DELETE by handle under `/api/workspaces/{slug}/groups` |\n| `server/invitations/__init__.py` | Package marker |\n| `server/invitations/store.py` | Create/list active/get-by-code/revoke/accept transaction helpers; code generation |\n| `server/invitations/routes.py` | Workspace POST/GET invitations; `POST/DELETE /api/invitations/{code}` (+ `/accept`) |\n| `tests/test_groups.py` | Group CRUD, authz, validation, conflict, guest 403 |\n| `tests/test_invitations.py` | Create defaults, targeted 403, 404 matrix, accept membership + general, revoke, invite_only still 403 on join without accept |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/db.py` | `_migrate_v4` / `_reverse_v4`; register version **4** in `MIGRATIONS` / reverse map |\n| `server/workspaces/store.py` | Add `add_workspace_member(...)` helper if not present after M7 |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | Tiny helper `ensure_channel_member(channel_id, user_id)` for `#general` on accept (or inline in invitations store via SQL); **do not** invent channel CRUD |\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` for groups + invitations routers |\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` | Only if M7 join already exists here: ensure invite_only gate unchanged and open-join uses shared member helper. **Do not** re-implement full M7. |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/**` | MARATHON-18 owns invitation/settings UI |\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume userna\n---\n## Data Model\n\n### Migration **v4** (additive, backward compatible)\n\n#### `user_groups`\n\n| Column | Type | Notes |\n|--------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | UUID4 |\n| `workspace_id` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK workspaces ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `handle` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| `name` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| `created_by` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK users |\n| `created_at` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| `updated_at` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| UNIQUE `(workspace_id, handle)` | | |\n\n#### `user_group_members`\n\n| Column | Type | Notes |\n|--------|------|-------|\n| `group_id` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK user_groups ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `user_id` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK users ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `created_at` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| PRIMARY KEY `(group_id, user_id)` | | |\n\nIndex: `user_group_members(user_id)` optional.\n\n#### `workspace_invitations`\n\n| Column | Type | Notes |\n|--------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | UUID4 |\n| `workspace_id` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK workspaces ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `code` | TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE | |\n| `created_by` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK users |\n| `created_at` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| `expires_at` | TEXT NULL | |\n| `max_uses` | INTEGER NOT NULL | |\n| `use_count` | INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 | |\n| `invited_user_id` | TEXT NULL | FK users |\n| `invited_username` | TEXT NULL | snapshot at create |\n| `revoked_at` | TEXT NULL | null = not revoked |\n\nIndex: `workspace_invitations(workspace_id)`; unique on `code`.\n\n**No changes** to `workspaces.join_mode` CHECK or `workspace_members` schema.\n\n**Reverse v4:** DROP the three tables (local verification only), matching M2/M3 reverse style.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/groups/__init__.py` | Package marker |\n| `server/groups/store.py` | Handle/name validation; CRUD; `row_to_group_obj`; membership replace |\n| `server/groups/routes.py` | GET/POST list-create; PATCH/DELETE by handle under `/api/workspaces/{slug}/groups` |\n| `server/invitations/__init__.py` | Package marker |\n| `server/invitations/store.py` | Create/list active/get-by-code/revoke/accept transaction helpers; code generation |\n| `server/invitations/routes.py` | Workspace POST/GET invitations; `POST/DELETE /api/invitations/{code}` (+ `/accept`) |\n| `tests/test_groups.py` | Group CRUD, authz, validation, conflict, guest 403 |\n| `tests/test_invitations.py` | Create defaults, targeted 403, 404 matrix, accept membership + general, revoke, invite_only still 403 on join without accept |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/db.py` | `_migrate_v4` / `_reverse_v4`; register version **4** in `MIGRATIONS` / reverse map |\n| `server/workspaces/store.py` | Add `add_workspace_member(...)` helper if not present after M7 |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | Tiny helper `ensure_channel_member(channel_id, user_id)` for `#general` on accept (or inline in invitations store via SQL); **do not** invent channel CRUD |\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` for groups + invitations routers |\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` | Only if M7 join already exists here: ensure invite_only gate unchanged and open-join uses shared member helper. **Do not** re-implement full M7. |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/**` | MARATHON-18 owns invitation/settings UI |\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume username lookup only |\n| Existing workspace/member tests | Keep green; add new test modules |\n| Message/search/mention expansion | MARATHON-8/11 |\n| Private channel add-member API | Optional follow-up; not in this task text |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order\n\n1. `db.py` v4 migration (+ reverse).\n2. `workspaces_store.add_workspace_member` + general channel member ensure.\n3. Groups store + routes + tests.\n4. Invitations store + routes + tests (accept depends on member helper).\n5. If M7 join routes exist: verify invite_only still 403; open join uses helper.\n6. Cluster smoke: create invite on :8000, accept on :8001, detail on :8002.\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Groups and invitations schemas are independent after migration; routes can be built in parallel once migration + member helper exist.\n- Tests can split across two files as listed.\n\n### Downstream seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumed by |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `GroupObj` + groups CRUD | MARATHON-11 `@group-handle`; future SPA |\n| `InvitationObj` + create/list/revoke | MARATHON-18 settings invitations tab |\n| `POST /api/invitations/{code}/accept` → workspace payload | MARATHON-18 (redeem UX) / graders |\n| invite_only on-ramp via accept | Completes M7 join matrix |\n\n### Upstream\n\n- MARATHON-5/6 closed (workspaces, roles, join_mode).\n- MARATHON-7 design (join gates) — implement join wiring against that contract; soft-seq after M7 code if join routes missing.\n- MARATHON-16 closed (SPA join path unchanged).\n\n### Declared dependent\n\n- **MARATHON-18** blocked on this task (settings invitations UI).\n\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- SPA create/list/accept UI → MARATHON-18.\n\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T00:14:42.434Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":65,"interleavedOutput":"time=2026-08-23T00:14:42.434Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n### Seam: Invitations (workspace-scoped admin)\n\n#### `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations`\n\n**Authz:** workspace **owner or admin** → else member **403** / non-member **404**.\n\n**Body:**\n```json\n{\n  \"expires_in_seconds\": 86400,\n  \"max_uses\": 1,\n  \"invited_username\": \"ada\",\n  \"invited_user_id\": null\n}\n```\nAll fields optional. Unknown keys ignored.\n\n| Field | Rules |\n|-------|-------|\n| `expires_in_seconds` | Omit/null → no expiry. If set: integer **≥ 60** and **≤ 2592000** (30d); else 400. `expires_at = now + seconds`. |\n| `max_uses` | Omit → **1**. If set: integer **≥ 1** and **≤ 1000**; else 400. |\n| `invited_user_id` | If set: must exist in `users`; else 400. |\n| `invited_username` | If set: resolve via username (case-sensitive per Auth store); unknown → 400. |\n| Both target fields | Must resolve to the **same** user; else 400. |\n| Targeted | Force `max_uses = 1`. If client sends `max_uses` > 1 with a target → **400** `validation_error`. |\n\n**Response 201:** `{ \"invitation\": InvitationObj }`  \n`use_count=0`; `code` unique globally.\n\n#### `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations`\n\n**Authz:** owner/admin; others 403/404 as above.\n\n**Semantics — active only:** `revoked_at IS NULL` AND (`expires_at IS NULL` OR `expires_at > now`) AND `use_count < max_uses`.\n\nOrder: `created_at` DESC.\n\n**Response 200:** `{ \"invitations\": [ InvitationObj, ... ] }`\n\n---\n\n### Seam: Invitation redeem / revoke (code-scoped)\n\n#### `POST /api/invitations/{code}/accept`\n\n**Authz:** any authenticated user (no prior workspace membership required).\n\n| Condition | HTTP | code |\n|-----------|------|------|\n| Unknown code | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Revoked | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Expired (`expires_at <= now`) | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Exhausted (`use_count >= max_uses`) | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Targeted and caller.id ≠ invited_user_id | **403** | `forbidden` |\n| Success (new or already member) | **200** | — |\n\n**Body:** `{}` or empty; ignore extras.\n\n**Response 200:**\n```json\n{\n  \"workspace\": { /* WorkspaceObj */ },\n  \"channels\": [ /* ChannelObj[] visible to caller after join */ ],\n  \"read_state\": []\n}\n```\nShape mirrors workspace detail / join success so SPA can `enterWorkspace` without a second round-trip. `channels` at minimum includes public `#general` (and any other publics per M5 visibility). `read_state` may be `[]`.\n\n**Server work (transaction):**\n1. Lock/select invitation by code; evaluate status → 404/403 as above.\n2. If caller not in `workspace_members`: INSERT role=`member`; INSERT `#general` into `channel_members` if missing; `use_count += 1`.\n3. If already member: no `use_count` change; still return workspace payload.\n4. Commit.\n\n**Client:** on success treat like join; on 403 show forbidden; on 404 show invalid/expired invite; while slow disable submit.\n\n#### `DELETE /api/invitations/{code}`\n\n**Authz:** resolve invitation → workspace; caller must be **owner or admin** of that workspace. Non-member of that workspace → **404**. Member but not admin/owner → **403**. Unknown/already-revoked → **404** (idempotent revoke of missing → 404, not 200).\n\n**Effect:** set `revoked_at = now` (soft revoke).\n\n**Response 200:** `{ \"revoked\": true }`\n\n---\n\n### Seam: invite_only join gate (cross-task)\n\n| Endpoint (MARATHON-7) | Behavior with this task |\n|----------------------|-------------------------|\n| `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` | `open` + non-member → add member (M7). `invite_only` + non-member → **403** (unchanged). After accept, caller is member → join is idempotent 200. |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` | invite_only workspace + non-member → **403** (unchanged). Members who accepted can join public channels per M7. |\n\n**Shared helper (this task owns the name/contract):**  \n`workspaces_store.add_workspace_member(conn, workspace_id=, user_id=, role=\"member\")` — INSERT OR ignore / check-then-insert; used by accept and by M7 open-join.\n\nIf M7 is not yet merged when implementing: still ship the helper + accept path; add a short comment at the future join call sites documenting the invite_only 403 rule (already in M7 design). When M7 lands, join **must** call the same helper (do not duplicate INSERT logic).\n\n---\n\n### Error code summary\n\n| code | HTTP | When |\n|------|------|------|\n| `validation_error` | 400 | Bad handle/name/user_ids/expiry/max_uses/target mismatch |\n| `unauthorized` | 401 | Missing/invalid bearer |\n| `forbidden` | 403 | Guest creates group; non-creator non-owner mutates group; non-admin invitation admin APIs; targeted accept by wrong user |\n| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown slug/handle/code; non-member on workspace-scoped routes; inactive invites |\n| `conflict` | 409 | Duplicate group handle in workspace |\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Migration **v4** (additive, backward compatible)\n\n#### `user_groups`\n\n| Column | Type | Notes |\n|--------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | UUID4 |\n| `workspace_id` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK workspaces ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `handle` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| `name` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| `created_by` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK users |\n| `created_at` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| `updated_at` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| UNIQUE `(workspace_id, handle)` | | |\n\n#### `user_group_members`\n\n| Column | Type | Notes |\n|--------|------|-------|\n| `group_id` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK user_groups ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `user_id` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK users ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `created_at` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| PRIMARY KEY `(group_id, user_id)` | | |\n\nIndex: `user_group_members(user_id)` optional.\n\n#### `workspace_invitations`\n\n| Column | Type | Notes |\n|--------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | UUID4 |\n| `workspace_id` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK workspaces ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `code` | TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE | |\n| `created_by` | TEXT NOT NULL | FK users |\n| `created_at` | TEXT NOT NULL | |\n| `expires_at` | TEXT NULL | |\n| `max_uses` | INTEGER NOT NULL | |\n| `use_count` | INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 | |\n| `invited_user_id` | TEXT NULL | FK users |\n| `invited_username` | TEXT NULL | snapshot at create |\n| `revoked_at` | TEXT NULL | null = not revoked |\n\nIndex: `workspace_invitations(workspace_id)`; unique on `code`.\n\n**No changes** to `workspaces.join_mode` CHECK or `workspace_members` schema.\n\n**Reverse v4:** DROP the three tables (local verification only), matching M2/M3 reverse style.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/groups/__init__.py` | Package marker |\n| `server/groups/store.py` | Handle/name validation; CRUD; `row_to_group_obj`; membership replace |\n| `server/groups/routes.py` | GET/POST list-create; PATCH/DELETE by handle under `/api/workspaces/{slug}/groups` |\n| `server/invitations/__init__.py` | Package marker |\n| `server/invitations/store.py` | Create/list active/get-by-code/revoke/accept transaction helpers; code generation |\n| `server/invitations/routes.py` | Workspace POST/GET invitations; `POST/DELETE /api/invitations/{code}` (+ `/accept`) |\n| `tests/test_groups.py` | Group CRUD, authz, validation, conflict, guest 403 |\n| `tests/test_invitations.py` | Create defaults, targeted 403, 404 matrix, accept membership + general, revoke, invite_only still 403 on join without accept |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/db.py` | `_migrate_v4` / `_reverse_v4`; register version **4** in `MIGRATIONS` / reverse map |\n| `server/workspaces/store.py` | Add `add_workspace_member(...)` helper if not present after M7 |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | Tiny hel