POST /api/invitations/{code}/accept`\n\n**Authz:** any authenticated user (no prior workspace membership required).\n\n| Condition | HTTP | code |\n|-----------|------|------|\n| Unknown code | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Revoked | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Expired (`expires_at <= now`) | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Exhausted (`use_count >= max_uses`) | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Targeted and caller.id ≠ invited_user_id | **403** | `forbidden` |\n| Success (new or already member) | **200** | — |\n\n**Body:** `{}` or empty; ignore extras.\n\n**Response 200:**\n```json\n{\n  \"workspace\": { /* WorkspaceObj */ },\n  \"channels\": [ /* ChannelObj[] visible to caller after join */ ],\n  \"read_state\": []\n}\n```\nShape mirrors workspace detail / join success so SPA can `enterWorkspace` without a second round-trip. `channels` at minimum includes public `#general` (and any other publics per M5 visibility). `read_state` may be `[]`.\n\n**Server work (transaction):**\n1. Lock/select invitation by code; evaluate status → 404/403 as above.\n2. If caller not in `workspace_members`: INSERT role=`member`; INSERT `#general` into `channel_members` if missing; `use_count += 1`.\n3. If already member: no `use_count` change; still return workspace \n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T00:23:44.353Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":68,"interleavedOutput":"time=2026-08-23T00:23:44.353Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\nPOST /api/invitations/{code}/accept`\n\n**Authz:** any authenticated user (no prior workspace membership required).\n\n| Condition | HTTP | code |\n|-----------|------|------|\n| Unknown code | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Revoked | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Expired (`expires_at <= now`) | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Exhausted (`use_count >= max_uses`) | 404 | `not_found` |\n| Targeted and caller.id ≠ invited_user_id | **403** | `forbidden` |\n| Success (new or already member) | **200** | — |\n\n**Body:** `{}` or empty; ignore extras.\n\n**Response 200:**\n```json\n{\n  \"workspace\": { /* WorkspaceObj */ },\n  \"channels\": [ /* ChannelObj[] visible to caller after join */ ],\n  \"read_state\": []\n}\n```\nShape mirrors workspace detail / join success so SPA can `enterWorkspace` without a second round-trip. `channels` at minimum includes public `#general` (and any other publics per M5 visibility). `read_state` may be `[]`.\n\n**Server work (transaction):**\n1. Lock/select invitation by code; evaluate status → 404/403 as above.\n2. If caller not in `workspace_members`: INSERT role=`member`; INSERT `#general` into `channel_members` if missing; `use_count += 1`.\n3. If already member: no `use_count` change; still return workspace \n","localExecutionTimeMs":28},"isBackground":false},"description":"Extract accept response contract from design"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-8cfb53c4-19a6-4089-a6ca-beeab93a7efc-82\nfc_554689d1-e3b5-9039-9db5-675ce07670c1_0","startedAtMs":"1787444624315","completedAtMs":"1787444624384"},"model_call_id":"0fbfa7d9-7075-4140-98fa-5162e36b06ee-26-vghy","session_id":"0a8fcafb-36dc-47ae-b858-91f084f7ec96","timestamp_ms":1787444624403}
