{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-32310ab2-55f8-486e-90df-a81025d89202-0\nfc_6088b184-8310-9214-9423-fe731e494f1c_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1 && git merge --no-edit main && loom data show MARATHON-8 --output json && loom data comments MARATHON-8 --output json 2>/dev/null || loom data show MARATHON-8 --output json | head -c 50000","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-32310ab2-55f8-486e-90df-a81025d89202-0\nfc_6088b184-8310-9214-9423-fe731e494f1c_0","simpleCommands":["cd","git","loom","loom","loom","head"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1"}],"fullText":"cd /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1"},{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"merge"},{"type":"word","value":"--no-edit"},{"type":"word","value":"main"}],"fullText":"git merge --no-edit main"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-8"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-8 --output json"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"comments"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-8"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data comments MARATHON-8 --output json"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-8"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-8 --output json"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"number","value":"50000"}],"fullText":"head -c 50000"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Merge main and show MARATHON-8 task","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"5de21c73-718e-49ab-8d79-ce218632b44f","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1 && git merge --no-edit main && loom data show MARATHON-8 --output json && loom data comments MARATHON-8 --output json 2>/dev/null || loom data show MARATHON-8 --output json | head -c 50000","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"Already up to date.\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n  \"title\": \"Messages, threads, reactions REST API\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"priority\": 0,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"assignee\": \"backend-dev-1\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"backend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-8 — Messages, threads, reactions REST API\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task completes the core chat write/read path for Huddle on top of MARATHON-7 channels and the minimal `messages` / pin embed already shipped: authenticated channel members can post top-level messages and one-level thread replies, list channel history (newest-first, cursor pagination) and thread replies (oldest-first), edit their own messages, soft-delete as author or workspace owner, and add/remove emoji reactions. It locks the REST `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` contracts the SPA (MARATHON-17) and downstream search/WS tasks consume, extends schema with reaction (and optional attachment join) tables while **preserving** the v3 `messages` table and pin routes, and leaves slash-command interception, full mention forms, file upload ownership, and dense `seq` fan-out to their owning tasks.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite SoT; **migration version 4** additive: `message_reactions`, optional `message_files`, optional `messages.blocks_json`; **do not** drop/recreate v3 `messages` |\\n| Route layout | Channel-scoped on `server/channels/routes.py`: `POST`/`GET /api/channels/{id}/messages`. Message-scoped on existing `server/messages/routes.py`: `PATCH`/`DELETE /{id}`, `GET /{parent_id}/replies`, `POST`/`DELETE .../reactions`, keep existing pin routes |\\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all endpoints require Bearer |\\n| `MessageObj` | **Same key set as MARATHON-7** (`MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`); enrich `reply_count`, `files`, `reactions`, `mentions` for real data; **no `seq`** on REST objects (product: seq lives on WS frames — MARATHON-13) |\\n| Soft delete | Set `deleted_at`; **exclude** deleted rows from channel history and reply lists; DELETE idempotent; PATCH / react on deleted → **409** `conflict` |\\n| Archived writes | Reuse `server.channels.store.assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived` for POST message, PATCH, DELETE (mutating), POST/DELETE reaction (same as pin) |\\n| Membership for writes | Same as pin mutate: caller must be **channel member**; workspace owner without membership → **403** |\\n| Membership for reads | Same as GET pins: public → workspace member else 404; private/DM → channel member else 403 (non-member workspace) / 404 (stranger) |\\n| Threads | Single level only: `parent_id` must reference a **top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`), same-channel, non-deleted message |\\n| Reactions | Table unique on `(message_id, user_id, emoji)`; aggregate to `[{emoji, count, user_ids}]`; POST/DELETE idempotent |\\n| `file_ids` / `blocks` | Accept on POST for product shape; `blocks` persisted as JSON text (not exposed on `MessageObj` keys); `file_ids` validated against files when present — **non-empty `file_ids` → 400** until MARATHON-10 provides attachable `files` rows (seam documented) |\\n| Mentions (this task) | Resolve `@username` only (word-boundary, no mid-word, no self, dedupe, must be workspace member); `@channel`/`@here`/`@group-handle` → MARATHON-11 |\\n| Slash commands | **Not** interpreted here; body stored literally (including `/me`, `/shrug`, …). MARATHON-11 intercepts |\\n| Events | Add no-op hooks in `server/events.py` (`publish_message_created` / `updated` / `deleted` / `reaction_changed`) for MARATHON-13; call after successful commit; must not raise |\\n| Timestamps | `utc_now_z()` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) |\\n| Ids | UUID4 strings |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- Product contract (epic planning) is explicit on paths, envelopes (`201 {message}`, `{replies}`, `{reactions}`, `{deleted:true}`), reaction shape, and delete/edit conflict semantics; inventing alternates breaks graders and MARATHON-17.\\n- Extending v3 (not replacing) keeps pin FKs and MARATHON-7 tests stable; `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` remains the single key source (pin tests import it).\\n- Aligning write authz with pin membership + `assert_channel_writable` avoids a second archived/private matrix.\\n- Deferring seq, slash, file upload, and advanced mentions prevents this task from blocking on MARATHON-10/11/13 while still accepting forward-compatible POST fields.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| Put all routes under `/api/messages` only | Product: `POST/GET /api/channels/{id}/messages` |\\n| Hard-delete rows | Breaks pin FK / audit; product soft-delete + 409 on edit |\\n| Tombstone deleted messages in channel history | Product allows either; **excluding** from listings is simpler for SPA empty states and matches “disappear”; pins still resolve via store for already-pinned ids |\\n| Nested threads (reply-to-reply) | Product is parent/replies one level; reject deep `parent_id` with 400 |\\n| Include `seq` on `MessageObj` | Product: seq on WS frames only |\\n| Implement slash / @channel in this task | Owned by MARATHON-11 |\\n| Create full `files` upload schema here | Owned by MARATHON-10; accept `file_ids` but 400 when unsatisfiable |\\n| Allow any workspace member to post in public without join | Diverges from pin write rule (must be channel member) |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\n`file_ids` and rich mention forms are accepted or partially implemented: non-empty attachments fail closed with 400 until MARATHON-10; only `@username` mentions populate `mentions` until MARATHON-11. Implementers must not invent FileObj upload or slash side effects here.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: UUID4 ids; `ApiError` + `{error:{code,message}}`; ignore unknown JSON fields; `400` `validation_error`; `401` `unauthorized`; `409` `conflict`.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: nested `author` is full `UserObj` via `row_to_user_obj` / joined columns.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-5/6**: workspace slug/`owner_id`; roles; non-member → **404** (no leak); privilege lack → **403**.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj`; `assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived`; minimal `MessageObj` key set; pin routes stay; private vs public visibility matrix for pins/messages reads; channel-member required for pin/message **writes**.\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Shared types\\n\\n#### `MessageObj` (normative keys — do not omit; do not add `seq` / `blocks` / `deleted_at` to JSON)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"author_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": { \\\"id\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"username\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"display_name\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"timezone\\\": null, \\\"avatar_url\\\": null, \\\"status_text\\\": null, \\\"status_emoji\\\": null },\\n  \\\"body\\\": \\\"hello\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_id\\\": null,\\n  \\\"reply_count\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-08-23T00:00:00Z\\\",\\n  \\\"edited_at\\\": null,\\n  \\\"files\\\": [],\\n  \\\"reactions\\\": [],\\n  \\\"mentions\\\": []\\n}\\n```\\n\\nExact keys = `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` already in `server/messages/store.py`.\\n\\n| Field | Rules |\\n|-------|--------|\\n| `reply_count` | Count of **non-deleted** children with `parent_id = this.id` |\\n| `edited_at` | `null` until first successful PATCH; then UTC Z timestamp |\\n| `files` | `FileObj[]` (see MARATHON-10). Until files exist / attach works → always `[]` |\\n| `reactions` | `ReactionObj[]` aggregated (below) |\\n| `mentions` | `string[]` of user ids (deduped), from `@username` resolution at create/edit |\\n\\n#### `ReactionObj`\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"👍\\\", \\\"count\\\": 2, \\\"user_ids\\\": [\\\"uuid-a\\\", \\\"uuid-b\\\"] }\\n```\\n\\nProduct name for the emoji field is **`emoji`** (not `name`). Do not add a `me` boolean; clients derive that from `user_ids` containing the caller id.\\n\\n- Group by exact `emoji` string.\\n- `count` = `len(user_ids)`.\\n- `user_ids` ordered by reaction `created_at ASC`, then `user_id ASC`.\\n- Reaction groups ordered by first-reaction `created_at ASC`, tie-break `emoji ASC`.\\n\\n#### `FileObj` (embed only; created by MARATHON-10)\\n\\n`{id, uploader_id, filename, content_type, size, created_at}` per product Files section — M8 returns `files: []` unless MARATHON-10 rows are resolvable.\\n\\n#### Error codes (this task)\\n\\n| `code` | HTTP | When |\\n|--------|------|------|\\n| `validation_error` | 400 | Empty/whitespace body; body too long; bad `limit`/`before`; bad `parent_id`; bad `emoji`; non-empty unsatisfiable `file_ids`; `blocks` not a list when present |\\n| `unauthorized` | 401 | Missing/invalid bearer |\\n| `forbidden` | 403 | Not channel member on write; not author on PATCH; not author/owner on DELETE; private read without membership |\\n| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown channel/message; public channel + non-workspace-member; stranger on private |\\n| `conflict` | 409 | PATCH or react on soft-deleted message |\\n| `archived` | 423 | Mutating write on archived channel |\\n\\n### Authz helpers (implement once, reuse)\\n\\nMirror MARATHON-7 pin access:\\n\\n**`require_channel_message_read(channel, user)`** — same rules as `GET /api/channels/{id}/pins` (public: workspace member; private/DM: channel member).\\n\\n**`require_channel_message_write(channel, user)`** — channel **member** required (public or private); then `assert_channel_writable`. Workspace owner without membership → **403** (same as pin).\\n\\nFor message-id routes: load message → load channel → apply read or write helper; missing message → **404** (do not leak across workspaces).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M17)** | Bearer; body `{body, parent_id?, file_ids?, blocks?}`; disable composer while in flight; on 201 append message / bump thread `reply_count`; on 400 show empty-message validation; on 423 show archived lock |\\n| **Server** | Authz write; validate; insert; resolve mentions; optional file attach; bump nothing external yet; return **201** |\\n\\n**Request:**\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"body\\\": \\\"hello @alice\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_id\\\": null,\\n  \\\"file_ids\\\": [],\\n  \\\"blocks\\\": null\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Validation:**\\n\\n- `body` required string; after Unicode trim of leading/trailing whitespace, length **1..4000** code points; empty/whitespace-only → **400**.\\n- `parent_id` optional; if set: must exist, same `channel_id`, `deleted_at IS NULL`, and parent’s `parent_id IS NULL`; else **400**.\\n- `file_ids` optional list of strings; default omit/`[]`. **Each** id must refer to a file owned by caller and not already attached (MARATHON-10). If files table/rows unavailable or any id fails → **400** `validation_error`. Empty list OK → `files: []`.\\n- `blocks` optional; if present must be a **JSON array** (elements unchecked beyond JSON); persist as `blocks_json`; **not** included in `MessageObj` response keys.\\n- Unknown fields ignored.\\n\\n**Response:** `201 { \\\"message\\\": MessageObj }`\\n\\n**Effects:** Insert row (`edited_at=null`, `deleted_at=null`); compute `mentions`; if `parent_id` set, child’s presence increases parent `reply_count` on subsequent reads; call `publish_message_created` after commit (no-op OK).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages?limit=\\u0026before=`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Bearer; initial load + scroll-up with `before=\\u003coldest_seen_id\\u003e`; keep prior list on error; render newest at bottom per UI |\\n| **Server** | Authz read; return **only top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`) **non-deleted** messages; **newest-first** |\\n\\n**Query:**\\n\\n- `limit` optional int, default **50**, min 1, max **100**; invalid → 400.\\n- `before` optional message id cursor: return messages strictly older than the cursor message’s (`created_at`, `id`) pair within the same channel; cursor must be a message in this channel (deleted cursor still OK as position); unknown id → **400**.\\n\\n**Response:** `200 { \\\"messages\\\": [MessageObj, ...] }`\\n\\nEach element fully enriched (`author`, `reply_count`, `reactions`, `mentions`, `files`).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `PATCH /api/messages/{message_id}`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Body `{body}`; show edited indicator from `edited_at`; on 409 treat as deleted |\\n| **Server** | Author-only; not deleted; writable channel; set `body`, `edited_at=now`, re-resolve `mentions` |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n\\n- Unknown → 404 (after read visibility check on channel).\\n- `caller.id != author_id` → **403**.\\n- `deleted_at` set → **409** `conflict`.\\n- Archived channel → **423**.\\n- Same body validation as create (empty → 400).\\n- `parent_id` / `file_ids` **not** patchable in this task (ignore if sent).\\n- **200** `{ \\\"message\\\": MessageObj }`; call `publish_message_updated` after commit.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `DELETE /api/messages/{message_id}`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Remove row from UI on 200; treat repeat delete as success |\\n| **Server** | Soft-delete; idempotent |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n\\n- Unknown message → 404 (visibility as read).\\n- Allowed if `caller.id == author_id` **OR** `caller.id == workspace.owner_id`; else **403**.\\n- Archived → **423** (mutating).\\n- If already `deleted_at` set → still **200** `{\\\"deleted\\\": true}` (no-op).\\n- Else set `deleted_at=now`; clear reaction rows for that message (so they “no longer count”); leave pin row if any (pin list uses tombstone mapping — see edge cases).\\n- **200** `{\\\"deleted\\\": true}`; call `publish_message_deleted` after commit.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/messages/{parent_id}/replies`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (thread panel)** | Bearer; render oldest-first; bump parent reply badge from parent `reply_count` |\\n| **Server** | Authz read via parent’s channel; return non-deleted children **oldest-first** |\\n\\n**Response:** `200 { \\\"replies\\\": [MessageObj, ...] }`  \\n(Product name is **`replies`**, not `messages`.)\\n\\n- Unknown parent → 404.\\n- Parent deleted → still allow listing non-deleted replies (or 404 — **choose: 404** if parent missing/deleted to match “disappear”).\\n- No `limit` required in this task (return all replies); if \\u003e1000, still return all for v1 (document; optional soft cap out of scope).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ reactions\\n\\n#### `POST /api/messages/{message_id}/reactions` body `{ \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"👍\\\" }` → `200 { \\\"reactions\\\": [ReactionObj, ...] }`\\n\\n- Authz: channel **write** membership + writable (423 if archived).\\n- Message missing → 404; deleted → **409**.\\n- `emoji` required non-empty string; max **32** code points; reject whitespace-only; allow Unicode emoji and shortcodes as opaque strings (no server-side emoji validation library).\\n- Insert ignore if `(message_id, user_id, emoji)` exists (idempotent).\\n- Return **full** aggregated `reactions` for that message (not only the one emoji).\\n- `publish_reaction_changed` after commit.\\n\\n#### `DELETE /api/messages/{message_id}/reactions/{emoji}` → `200 { \\\"reactions\\\": [...] }`\\n\\n- Same authz/404/409/423 as POST.\\n- URL-decode `emoji` path segment.\\n- Delete caller’s row if present; if absent → still 200 with current aggregate (idempotent).\\n- Return full aggregate after delete.\\n\\n### Client slow/fail summary\\n\\n| Condition | Client behavior |\\n|-----------|-----------------|\\n| In flight | Disable send/edit/delete/react; keep prior transcript |\\n| 401 | Re-auth (M16) |\\n| 400 | Inline validation (empty body, etc.) |\\n| 403 | Show forbidden; do not optimistic-post |\\n| 409 | Treat message as deleted; remove editor |\\n| 423 | Lock composer; show archived |\\n| 404 | Channel/message inaccessible |\\n| Network/5xx | Retry; do not assume message persisted |\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Existing (v3 — unchanged DDL)\\n\\n`messages(id, channel_id, author_id, body, parent_id, created_at, edited_at, deleted_at)` — already created in MARATHON-7 v3 + `idx_messages_channel_id`.\\n\\n### Migration v4 (additive, backward compatible)\\n\\n#### Alter `messages` (optional column)\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `blocks_json` | TEXT | NULL | JSON array text; omit from `MessageObj` |\\n\\nIf implementer prefers zero ALTER, store blocks in a side table — **prefer single nullable column** for simplicity.\\n\\n#### Indexes on `messages`\\n\\n- `idx_messages_channel_created` on `(channel_id, created_at DESC, id DESC)` for history.\\n- `idx_messages_parent_created` on `(parent_id, created_at ASC, id ASC)` for replies.\\n\\n#### `message_reactions`\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `message_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE |\\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\\n| `emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| PRIMARY KEY | `(message_id, user_id, emoji)` | | Enforces idempotent POST |\\n\\nIndex: `(message_id, created_at ASC)` for aggregate ordering.\\n\\n#### `message_files` (forward seam for MARATHON-10)\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `message_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE |\\n| `file_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | No FK until M10 `files` exists **or** FK added in M10 |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| PRIMARY KEY | `(message_id, file_id)` | | |\\n| UNIQUE | `(file_id)` | | A file attaches to at most one message |\\n\\n**M8 behavior:** if `files` table absent, refuse non-empty `file_ids` with 400 and leave `message_files` unused. M10 creates `files` and wires validation (uploader_id == caller, not already attached).\\n\\n### Schema change summary\\n\\n| Change | Compatible? |\\n|--------|-------------|\\n| v4 new tables + indexes + optional column | **Yes** — additive |\\n| v3 messages columns | **Unchanged** |\\n\\n### Invariants\\n\\n1. Soft-deleted messages have `deleted_at` non-null; excluded from history/reply lists.\\n2. `reply_count` never includes deleted children.\\n3. At most one reaction row per `(message_id, user_id, emoji)`.\\n4. `parent_id` either NULL or points to top-level message in same channel.\\n5. Pin routes continue to work; `get_message` / `row_to_message_obj` enrich reactions/mentions/files/reply_count for pin embeds too.\\n6. REST `MessageObj` never carries `seq`.\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `tests/test_messages.py` | Contract tests: post/list/pagination/edit/delete/replies/reactions/authz/423/409/empty body/parent rules/idempotent delete \\u0026 reactions; cluster read-after-write on second node |\\n\\n### Modify\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/db.py` | `_migrate_v4` / `_reverse_v4`; register in `MIGRATIONS` / `REVERSES` |\\n| `server/messages/store.py` | Create/list/get with enrichment; soft delete; reply list; reaction insert/delete/aggregate; mention resolve helper; `row_to_message_obj` fills real `reply_count`/`reactions`/`mentions`/`files` (files empty until M10); keep `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` unchanged |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | Add PATCH, DELETE, GET replies, POST/DELETE reactions; keep pin routes; factor `_require_pin_access` into shared `_require_message_channel_access(read|write)` used by pins + CRUD + reactions |\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Add `POST`/`GET /{channel_id}/messages` using messages store + same authz patterns as pins |\\n| `server/events.py` | No-op `publish_message_created/updated/deleted`, `publish_reaction_changed` with docstring payloads for M13 (`type`, `channel_id`, message/reactions fields — **seq assigned by M13**) |\\n| `server/messages/__init__.py` | Docstring: CRUD owned here |\\n| `tests/test_pins.py` | Only if enrichment changes assertions (prefer keep using `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`; update empty `reactions` expectations only if pins now return aggregates — still `[]` without reaction rows) |\\n| `tests/test_channels.py` | Optionally assert v4 migration present; do not break v3 assertions |\\n\\n### Do not touch\\n\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `static/**` | MARATHON-17 |\\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume only |\\n| File upload routes | MARATHON-10 |\\n| Search / slash / read_state | MARATHON-11 |\\n| WS / Redis fan-out | MARATHON-13/14 |\\n| DM create | MARATHON-9 |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Build order\\n\\n1. `db.py` v4 migration (+ reverse).\\n2. `messages/store.py` enrichment + CRUD + reactions + mentions.\\n3. Channel message POST/GET routes.\\n4. Message PATCH/DELETE/replies/reactions routes.\\n5. Event no-op hooks + call sites.\\n6. `tests/test_messages.py` (+ keep pins green).\\n\\n### Parallelism\\n\\n- Reaction endpoints can land in parallel with list pagination once insert/get exist.\\n- Channel GET/POST messages can land before PATCH/DELETE.\\n\\n### Downstream seams this task owns\\n\\n| Contract | Consumed by |\\n|----------|-------------|\\n| `MessageObj` + POST/GET channel messages + PATCH/DELETE | MARATHON-17 SPA; MARATHON-11 search/slash (reads body); MARATHON-13 event payloads |\\n| `{replies}` oldest-first | MARATHON-17 thread panel |\\n| `{reactions}` aggregate + POST/DELETE idempotent | MARATHON-17 emoji picker |\\n| Soft-delete + 409 on edit deleted | SPA + graders |\\n| `mentions: user_id[]` from `@username` | MARATHON-11 extends forms / mention_count |\\n| `file_ids` accept + `message_files` / 400 seam | MARATHON-10 attach rules |\\n| No-op message/reaction publish hooks | MARATHON-13 assigns dense `seq` + WS frames |\\n| Pin embed still `MessageObj` | Existing pin UI / tests |\\n\\n### Upstream\\n\\n- MARATHON-7 closed: v3 messages, pins, `assert_channel_writable`, channel membership matrix.\\n\\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\\n\\n- File upload + ownership attach enforcement details → MARATHON-10 (may tighten `file_ids` validation once `files` exists).\\n- Slash commands + `@channel`/`@here`/`@group` + read_state → MARATHON-11.\\n- Dense seq + WS resume → MARATHON-13.\\n- SPA transcript UI → MARATHON-17.\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\\n|------|----------------|--------------|\\n| `POST /api/files` multipart + download | future `server/files/*` | MARATHON-10 |\\n| Slash `/me` `/shrug` `/topic` … interception | message POST body | MARATHON-11 (M8 stores literal body) |\\n| `@channel` / `@here` / `@group-handle` | mentions | MARATHON-11 |\\n| `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` | read_state | MARATHON-11 |\\n| `GET /api/search` | search | MARATHON-11 |\\n| WS subscribe/resume + `seq` on frames | `server/events.py` real fan-out | MARATHON-13/14 |\\n| `POST /api/dms` | DM channels | MARATHON-9 |\\n| SPA message/thread/reaction UI | `static/**` | MARATHON-17 |\\n| Changing pin route semantics | `server/messages/routes.py` pin | Already shipped; only share helpers/enrichment |\\n| IRC message bridge | — | MARATHON-15 |\\n\\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\\n\\n| Hit | Disposition |\\n|-----|-------------|\\n| `server/messages/store.py` — thin `MessageObj` / get | **In scope** — enrich + CRUD |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` — pin only | **In scope** — add CRUD/reactions; keep pins |\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` — join/leave/pins | **In scope** — add messages POST/GET |\\n| `server/channels/store.py` — `assert_channel_writable`, membership | **In scope** — reuse; no ChannelObj key changes |\\n| `server/db.py` — v3 messages | **In scope** — add v4; do not recreate messages |\\n| `server/events.py` — `publish_user_updated` | **In scope** — add message/reaction no-ops |\\n| `server/app.py` — routers already mounted | **Out of scope** unless new router (none) |\\n| `tests/test_pins.py` — SQL-seed messages + MSG_KEYS | **Keep green**; enrichment must preserve keys |\\n| `tests/test_channels.py` — v3 schema asserts | **Keep green**; additive v4 OK |\\n| `static/js/*` — no message API yet | **Out of scope** — M17 |\\n| Grep: no channel messages routes yet | Greenfield under channels router |\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\\n|-----------|-------------------|\\n| Unauthenticated | **401** |\\n| Empty / whitespace `body` on POST/PATCH | **400** |\\n| `body` length 4000 OK; 4001 → **400** |\\n| POST without channel membership (public, workspace member only) | **403** |\\n| POST as channel member on archived | **423** |\\n| POST with `parent_id` pointing at a reply | **400** |\\n| POST with `parent_id` in another channel | **400** |\\n| POST with `parent_id` deleted | **400** |\\n| GET history includes replies | **Must not** — top-level only |\\n| GET history includes deleted | **Must not** |\\n| `before` on first page omitted | Newest `limit` messages |\\n| `limit=0` or `limit=101` | **400** |\\n| PATCH by non-author member | **403** |\\n| PATCH by workspace owner who is not author | **403** (owner is not enough for edit) |\\n| PATCH deleted | **409** |\\n| DELETE by author | **200** `{deleted:true}` |\\n| DELETE by workspace `owner_id` (not author) | **200** |\\n| DELETE by admin who is not owner_id | **403** |\\n| DELETE twice | Both **200** `{deleted:true}` |\\n| DELETE then GET history | Message absent |\\n| DELETE then PATCH | **409** |\\n| DELETE then POST reaction | **409** |\\n| POST reaction twice same emoji | **200**; single row; aggregate count unchanged |\\n| DELETE reaction never added | **200**; aggregate unchanged |\\n| Reaction emoji `\\\":+1:\\\"` vs `\\\"👍\\\"` | Distinct opaque strings |\\n| Mentions `@alice` mid-word `foo@alice` | No match |\\n| Mention self `@me` | Not included in `mentions` |\\n| Mention unknown user | Skipped (not 400) |\\n| `file_ids: [\\\"…\\\"]` before M10 files | **400** |\\n| `blocks: {}` (object not array) | **400** |\\n| `blocks: []` | Persist; MessageObj unchanged keys |\\n| Extra JSON fields | Ignore |\\n| Pin list after message soft-delete | Return pin entry with tombstone `MessageObj`: `body=\\\"\\\"`, `files=[]`, `reactions=[]`, `mentions=[]`, `reply_count` as computed; **or** skip pin — **prefer tombstone** so pin list length stable |\\n| SQLite busy | busy_timeout; fail closed after timeout (no 500 envelope inventiveness) |\\n| Concurrent reaction inserts | PK conflict → treat as idempotent success |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages` `{body:\\\"hi\\\"}` as channel member → **201** `{message}` with exact `MessageObj` keys; `edited_at=null`; `parent_id=null`; `reply_count=0`; `reactions=[]`; `files=[]`; `mentions` reflects `@username` rules.\\n2. Empty / whitespace body → **400** `validation_error`; message **not** inserted.\\n3. `GET /api/channels/{id}/messages` → **200** `{messages}` newest-first; only top-level non-deleted; supports `limit` + `before` cursor.\\n4. Reply via `parent_id` → **201**; parent’s subsequent `reply_count` is 1; `GET /api/messages/{parent}/replies` → **200** `{replies:[…]}` oldest-first.\\n5. `PATCH /api/messages/{id}` as author → **200**; `edited_at` set; non-author → **403**; after DELETE → PATCH **409**.\\n6. `DELETE /api/messages/{id}` as author or workspace owner → **200** `{deleted:true}` idempotent; message omitted from later GET history; non-author non-owner → **403**.\\n7. `POST /api/messages/{id}/reactions` `{emoji}` → **200** `{reactions:[{emoji,count,user_ids}]}` idempotent per `(user,emoji)`; `DELETE .../reactions/{emoji}` → **200** `{reactions}` idempotent.\\n8. Archived channel → POST/PATCH/DELETE message and reaction mutate → **423** `archived`; GET history/replies still **200** if authorized.\\n9. Private channel non-member → read/write **403** (workspace member) or **404** (stranger), consistent with pins.\\n10. **Cluster:** POST message on `:8000`, GET on `:8001` with same token sees it (shared SQLite).\\n11. Existing pin tests remain green; pin embed still exposes full `MessageObj` keys.\\n12. **Negative:** must **not** put `seq` on `MessageObj`; must **not** interpret slash commands; must **not** drop/recreate `messages` table; must **not** allow reply-to-reply; must **not** return deleted messages in channel history; must **not** use `{messages}` as the replies envelope key.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Automated (`tests/test_messages.py`)\\n\\n- Happy path create → list ordering → pagination with `before`.\\n- Thread create + replies ordering + `reply_count`.\\n- Edit sets `edited_at`; edit deleted → 409; delete idempotent; owner delete.\\n- Reactions aggregate shape, idempotent POST/DELETE, multi-user counts.\\n- Authz matrix: non-member, private, archived 423, author-only patch.\\n- Mentions: `@user` resolved; mid-word ignored; self excluded.\\n- `file_ids` non-empty → 400 (until files seeded/M10).\\n- Migration v4 applied; reverse drops v4 objects without destroying v3 unexpectedly in reverse tests (follow existing reverse pattern).\\n- Regression: run `tests/test_pins.py` + `tests/test_channels.py`.\\n\\n### Manual / human\\n\\n1. Boot cluster via `start.sh` (do not required for architect; implementer verifies).\\n2. Register two users; create workspace; join `#general`.\\n3. POST messages; confirm GET newest-first; reply; open replies oldest-first.\\n4. React twice; confirm count 1; second user react; count 2; delete own reaction.\\n5. Delete message; confirm absent from list; PATCH returns 409.\\n6. Archive channel; confirm POST message 423; unarchive; POST works.\\n7. Repeat GET against another node port to confirm shared DB.\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"Design complete for MARATHON-8 (messages/threads/reactions REST). Grounded in epic product contract + MARATHON-7 MessageObj/pin/423/membership seams + current server/messages + db v3. Extends schema (v4 reactions/files join), does not recreate messages. file_ids/slash/@channel deferred to M10/M11 with explicit seams. Ready for lead review; implementer label remains backend after architect approval.\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:01.573541406Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:40:54.565406517Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"Note: depends on channels task. POST channels/{id}/messages {body,parent_id?,file_ids?,blocks?}; empty body 400; MessageObj with author, reply_count, edited_at, files, reactions, mentions. GET messages newest-first with limit/before. PATCH author-only sets edited_at; edit deleted → 409. DELETE author or workspace owner, idempotent 200 {deleted:true}. GET messages/{parent_id}/replies oldest-first. Reactions POST/DELETE idempotent per (user,emoji) return {reactions}.\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-11\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:16.962464474Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-13\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:29.97263884Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-10\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Files: upload, metadata, download, attach\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:47.139019113Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-17\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:47.207494951Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 42,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"DESIGN-AUTO-APPROVED pass=22\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:40:54.576884693Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nThe 'loom data' subtree contains thin CLI commands that interact\nwith the configured loom issue backend. When --server or LOOM_SERVER_URL is\nset, commands talk to that loom server over HTTP. Without a server, issue\ncommands use the local backend selected by the workspace configuration and\ndaemon IPC environment.\n\nUse 'loom data' commands when:\n  • You want a backend-aware command surface for agents and scripts.\n  • You want to manage agents on a remote loom server.\n  • You are scripting against a hosted loom deployment.\n\nExamples:\n  loom data show <id> --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data ready --limit 10\n  loom data list --server http://localhost:8080 -o json | jq '.[].id'\n  loom data monitor --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data agent stop falcon --server http://localhost:8080\n\nRoot-level --server / --workspace are mirrored into LOOM_SERVER_URL /\nLOOM_WORKSPACE in PersistentPreRunE, so 'loom --server URL data show ID'\nand 'loom data show ID --server URL' resolve identically. The data\nsubcommand reads from env, not from its own flag.\n\nUsage:\n  loom data [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  agent       Control a single agent on the loom server (stop/start/restart/yield)\n  agents      List agents managed by the loom server daemon (HTTP)\n  blocked     List issues that are blocked by other open issues (HTTP)\n  claim       Atomically claim an issue\n  close       Close an issue (HTTP)\n  comment     Add a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n  create      Create an issue\n  list        List issues (HTTP)\n  monitor     Show monitor dashboard from a loom server (HTTP, single-shot)\n  ready       List issues that are ready to work on (HTTP)\n  show        Show a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n  update      Update issue fields\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help            help for data\n  -o, --output string   Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string   Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\n\nUse \"loom data [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T00:41:06.358Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":384,"interleavedOutput":"Already up to date.\ntime=2026-08-23T00:41:06.358Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n  \"title\": \"Messages, threads, reactions REST API\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"priority\": 0,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"assignee\": \"backend-dev-1\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"backend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-8 — Messages, threads, reactions REST API\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task completes the core chat write/read path for Huddle on top of MARATHON-7 channels and the minimal `messages` / pin embed already shipped: authenticated channel members can post top-level messages and one-level thread replies, list channel history (newest-first, cursor pagination) and thread replies (oldest-first), edit their own messages, soft-delete as author or workspace owner, and add/remove emoji reactions. It locks the REST `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` contracts the SPA (MARATHON-17) and downstream search/WS tasks consume, extends schema with reaction (and optional attachment join) tables while **preserving** the v3 `messages` table and pin routes, and leaves slash-command interception, full mention forms, file upload ownership, and dense `seq` fan-out to their owning tasks.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite SoT; **migration version 4** additive: `message_reactions`, optional `message_files`, optional `messages.blocks_json`; **do not** drop/recreate v3 `messages` |\\n| Route layout | Channel-scoped on `server/channels/routes.py`: `POST`/`GET /api/channels/{id}/messages`. Message-scoped on existing `server/messages/routes.py`: `PATCH`/`DELETE /{id}`, `GET /{parent_id}/replies`, `POST`/`DELETE .../reactions`, keep existing pin routes |\\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all endpoints require Bearer |\\n| `MessageObj` | **Same key set as MARATHON-7** (`MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`); enrich `reply_count`, `files`, `reactions`, `mentions` for real data; **no `seq`** on REST objects (product: seq lives on WS frames — MARATHON-13) |\\n| Soft delete | Set `deleted_at`; **exclude** deleted rows from channel history and reply lists; DELETE idempotent; PATCH / react on deleted → **409** `conflict` |\\n| Archived writes | Reuse `server.channels.store.assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived` for POST message, PATCH, DELETE (mutating), POST/DELETE reaction (same as pin) |\\n| Membership for writes | Same as pin mutate: caller must be **channel member**; workspace owner without membership → **403** |\\n| Membership for reads | Same as GET pins: public → workspace member else 404; private/DM → channel member else 403 (non-member workspace) / 404 (stranger) |\\n| Threads | Single level only: `parent_id` must reference a **top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`), same-channel, non-deleted message |\\n| Reactions | Table unique on `(message_id, user_id, emoji)`; aggregate to `[{emoji, count, user_ids}]`; POST/DELETE idempotent |\\n| `file_ids` / `blocks` | Accept on POST for product shape; `blocks` persisted as JSON text (not exposed on `MessageObj` keys); `file_ids` validated against files when present — **non-empty `file_ids` → 400** until MARATHON-10 provides attachable `files` rows (seam documented) |\\n| Mentions (this task) | Resolve `@username` only (word-boundary, no mid-word, no self, dedupe, must be workspace member); `@channel`/`@here`/`@group-handle` → MARATHON-11 |\\n| Slash commands | **Not** interpreted here; body stored literally (including `/me`, `/shrug`, …). MARATHON-11 intercepts |\\n| Events | Add no-op hooks in `server/events.py` (`publish_message_created` / `updated` / `deleted` / `reaction_changed`) for MARATHON-13; call after successful commit; must not raise |\\n| Timestamps | `utc_now_z()` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) |\\n| Ids | UUID4 strings |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- Product contract (epic planning) is explicit on paths, envelopes (`201 {message}`, `{replies}`, `{reactions}`, `{deleted:true}`), reaction shape, and delete/edit conflict semantics; inventing alternates breaks graders and MARATHON-17.\\n- Extending v3 (not replacing) keeps pin FKs and MARATHON-7 tests stable; `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` remains the single key source (pin tests import it).\\n- Aligning write authz with pin membership + `assert_channel_writable` avoids a second archived/private matrix.\\n- Deferring seq, slash, file upload, and advanced mentions prevents this task from blocking on MARATHON-10/11/13 while still accepting forward-compatible POST fields.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| Put all routes under `/api/messages` only | Product: `POST/GET /api/channels/{id}/messages` |\\n| Hard-delete rows | Breaks pin FK / audit; product soft-delete + 409 on edit |\\n| Tombstone deleted messages in channel history | Product allows either; **excluding** from listings is simpler for SPA empty states and matches “disappear”; pins still resolve via store for already-pinned ids |\\n| Nested threads (reply-to-reply) | Product is parent/replies one level; reject deep `parent_id` with 400 |\\n| Include `seq` on `MessageObj` | Product: seq on WS frames only |\\n| Implement slash / @channel in this task | Owned by MARATHON-11 |\\n| Create full `files` upload schema here | Owned by MARATHON-10; accept `file_ids` but 400 when unsatisfiable |\\n| Allow any workspace member to post in public without join | Diverges from pin write rule (must be channel member) |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\n`file_ids` and rich mention forms are accepted or partially implemented: non-empty attachments fail closed with 400 until MARATHON-10; only `@username` mentions populate `mentions` until MARATHON-11. Implementers must not invent FileObj upload or slash side effects here.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: UUID4 ids; `ApiError` + `{error:{code,message}}`; ignore unknown JSON fields; `400` `validation_error`; `401` `unauthorized`; `409` `conflict`.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: nested `author` is full `UserObj` via `row_to_user_obj` / joined columns.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-5/6**: workspace slug/`owner_id`; roles; non-member → **404** (no leak); privilege lack → **403**.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj`; `assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived`; minimal `MessageObj` key set; pin routes stay; private vs public visibility matrix for pins/messages reads; channel-member required for pin/message **writes**.\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Shared types\\n\\n#### `MessageObj` (normative keys — do not omit; do not add `seq` / `blocks` / `deleted_at` to JSON)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"author_id\\\": \\\"…\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": { \\\"id\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"username\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"display_name\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"timezone\\\": null, \\\"avatar_url\\\": null, \\\"status_text\\\": null, \\\"status_emoji\\\": null },\\n  \\\"body\\\": \\\"hello\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_id\\\": null,\\n  \\\"reply_count\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"created_at\\\": \\\"2026-08-23T00:00:00Z\\\",\\n  \\\"edited_at\\\": null,\\n  \\\"files\\\": [],\\n  \\\"reactions\\\": [],\\n  \\\"mentions\\\": []\\n}\\n```\\n\\nExact keys = `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` already in `server/messages/store.py`.\\n\\n| Field | Rules |\\n|-------|--------|\\n| `reply_count` | Count of **non-deleted** children with `parent_id = this.id` |\\n| `edited_at` | `null` until first successful PATCH; then UTC Z timestamp |\\n| `files` | `FileObj[]` (see MARATHON-10). Until files exist / attach works → always `[]` |\\n| `reactions` | `ReactionObj[]` aggregated (below) |\\n| `mentions` | `string[]` of user ids (deduped), from `@username` resolution at create/edit |\\n\\n#### `ReactionObj`\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"👍\\\", \\\"count\\\": 2, \\\"user_ids\\\": [\\\"uuid-a\\\", \\\"uuid-b\\\"] }\\n```\\n\\nProduct name for the emoji field is **`emoji`** (not `name`). Do not add a `me` boolean; clients derive that from `user_ids` containing the caller id.\\n\\n- Group by exact `emoji` string.\\n- `count` = `len(user_ids)`.\\n- `user_ids` ordered by reaction `created_at ASC`, then `user_id ASC`.\\n- Reaction groups ordered by first-reaction `created_at ASC`, tie-break `emoji ASC`.\\n\\n#### `FileObj` (embed only; created by MARATHON-10)\\n\\n`{id, uploader_id, filename, content_type, size, created_at}` per product Files section — M8 returns `files: []` unless MARATHON-10 rows are resolvable.\\n\\n#### Error codes (this task)\\n\\n| `code` | HTTP | When |\\n|--------|------|------|\\n| `validation_error` | 400 | Empty/whitespace body; body too long; bad `limit`/`before`; bad `parent_id`; bad `emoji`; non-empty unsatisfiable `file_ids`; `blocks` not a list when present |\\n| `unauthorized` | 401 | Missing/invalid bearer |\\n| `forbidden` | 403 | Not channel member on write; not author on PATCH; not author/owner on DELETE; private read without membership |\\n| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown channel/message; public channel + non-workspace-member; stranger on private |\\n| `conflict` | 409 | PATCH or react on soft-deleted message |\\n| `archived` | 423 | Mutating write on archived channel |\\n\\n### Authz helpers (implement once, reuse)\\n\\nMirror MARATHON-7 pin access:\\n\\n**`require_channel_message_read(channel, user)`** — same rules as `GET /api/channels/{id}/pins` (public: workspace member; private/DM: channel member).\\n\\n**`require_channel_message_write(channel, user)`** — channel **member** required (public or private); then `assert_channel_writable`. Workspace owner without membership → **403** (same as pin).\\n\\nFor message-id routes: load message → load channel → apply read or write helper; missing message → **404** (do not leak across workspaces).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M17)** | Bearer; body `{body, parent_id?, file_ids?, blocks?}`; disable composer while in flight; on 201 append message / bump thread `reply_count`; on 400 show empty-message validation; on 423 show archived lock |\\n| **Server** | Authz write; validate; insert; resolve mentions; optional file attach; bump nothing external yet; return **201** |\\n\\n**Request:**\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"body\\\": \\\"hello @alice\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_id\\\": null,\\n  \\\"file_ids\\\": [],\\n  \\\"blocks\\\": null\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Validation:**\\n\\n- `body` required string; after Unicode trim of leading/trailing whitespace, length **1..4000** code points; empty/whitespace-only → **400**.\\n- `parent_id` optional; if set: must exist, same `channel_id`, `deleted_at IS NULL`, and parent’s `parent_id IS NULL`; else **400**.\\n- `file_ids` optional list of strings; default omit/`[]`. **Each** id must refer to a file owned by caller and not already attached (MARATHON-10). If files table/rows unavailable or any id fails → **400** `validation_error`. Empty list OK → `files: []`.\\n- `blocks` optional; if present must be a **JSON array** (elements unchecked beyond JSON); persist as `blocks_json`; **not** included in `MessageObj` response keys.\\n- Unknown fields ignored.\\n\\n**Response:** `201 { \\\"message\\\": MessageObj }`\\n\\n**Effects:** Insert row (`edited_at=null`, `deleted_at=null`); compute `mentions`; if `parent_id` set, child’s presence increases parent `reply_count` on subsequent reads; call `publish_message_created` after commit (no-op OK).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages?limit=\\u0026before=`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Bearer; initial load + scroll-up with `before=\\u003coldest_seen_id\\u003e`; keep prior list on error; render newest at bottom per UI |\\n| **Server** | Authz read; return **only top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`) **non-deleted** messages; **newest-first** |\\n\\n**Query:**\\n\\n- `limit` optional int, default **50**, min 1, max **100**; invalid → 400.\\n- `before` optional message id cursor: return messages strictly older than the cursor message’s (`created_at`, `id`) pair within the same channel; cursor must be a message in this channel (deleted cursor still OK as position); unknown id → **400**.\\n\\n**Response:** `200 { \\\"messages\\\": [MessageObj, ...] }`\\n\\nEach element fully enriched (`author`, `reply_count`, `reactions`, `mentions`, `files`).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `PATCH /api/messages/{message_id}`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Body `{body}`; show edited indicator from `edited_at`; on 409 treat as deleted |\\n| **Server** | Author-only; not deleted; writable channel; set `body`, `edited_at=now`, re-resolve `mentions` |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n\\n- Unknown → 404 (after read visibility check on channel).\\n- `caller.id != author_id` → **403**.\\n- `deleted_at` set → **409** `conflict`.\\n- Archived channel → **423**.\\n- Same body validation as create (empty → 400).\\n- `parent_id` / `file_ids` **not** patchable in this task (ignore if sent).\\n- **200** `{ \\\"message\\\": MessageObj }`; call `publish_message_updated` after commit.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `DELETE /api/messages/{message_id}`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Remove row from UI on 200; treat repeat delete as success |\\n| **Server** | Soft-delete; idempotent |\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n\\n- Unknown message → 404 (visibility as read).\\n- Allowed if `caller.id == author_id` **OR** `caller.id == workspace.owner_id`; else **403**.\\n- Archived → **423** (mutating).\\n- If already `deleted_at` set → still **200** `{\\\"deleted\\\": true}` (no-op).\\n- Else set `deleted_at=now`; clear reaction rows for that message (so they “no longer count”); leave pin row if any (pin list uses tombstone mapping — see edge cases).\\n- **200** `{\\\"deleted\\\": true}`; call `publish_message_deleted` after commit.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/messages/{parent_id}/replies`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (thread panel)** | Bearer; render oldest-first; bump parent reply badge from parent `reply_count` |\\n| **Server** | Authz read via parent’s channel; return non-deleted children **oldest-first** |\\n\\n**Response:** `200 { \\\"replies\\\": [MessageObj, ...] }`  \\n(Product name is **`replies`**, not `messages`.)\\n\\n- Unknown parent → 404.\\n- Parent deleted → still allow listing non-deleted replies (or 404 — **choose: 404** if parent missing/deleted to match “disappear”).\\n- No `limit` required in this task (return all replies); if \\u003e1000, still return all for v1 (document; optional soft cap out of scope).\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ reactions\\n\\n#### `POST /api/messages/{message_id}/reactions` body `{ \\\"emoji\\\": \\\"👍\\\" }` → `200 { \\\"reactions\\\": [ReactionObj, ...] }`\\n\\n- Authz: channel **write** membership + writable (423 if archived).\\n- Message missing → 404; deleted → **409**.\\n- `emoji` required non-empty string; max **32** code points; reject whitespace-only; allow Unicode emoji and shortcodes as opaque strings (no server-side emoji validation library).\\n- Insert ignore if `(message_id, user_id, emoji)` exists (idempotent).\\n- Return **full** aggregated `reactions` for that message (not only the one emoji).\\n- `publish_reaction_changed` after commit.\\n\\n#### `DELETE /api/messages/{message_id}/reactions/{emoji}` → `200 { \\\"reactions\\\": [...] }`\\n\\n- Same authz/404/409/423 as POST.\\n- URL-decode `emoji` path segment.\\n- Delete caller’s row if present; if absent → still 200 with current aggregate (idempotent).\\n- Return full aggregate after delete.\\n\\n### Client slow/fail summary\\n\\n| Condition | Client behavior |\\n|-----------|-----------------|\\n| In flight | Disable send/edit/delete/react; keep prior transcript |\\n| 401 | Re-auth (M16) |\\n| 400 | Inline validation (empty body, etc.) |\\n| 403 | Show forbidden; do not optimistic-post |\\n| 409 | Treat message as deleted; remove editor |\\n| 423 | Lock composer; show archived |\\n| 404 | Channel/message inaccessible |\\n| Network/5xx | Retry; do not assume message persisted |\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Existing (v3 — unchanged DDL)\\n\\n`messages(id, channel_id, author_id, body, parent_id, created_at, edited_at, deleted_at)` — already created in MARATHON-7 v3 + `idx_messages_channel_id`.\\n\\n### Migration v4 (additive, backward compatible)\\n\\n#### Alter `messages` (optional column)\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `blocks_json` | TEXT | NULL | JSON array text; omit from `MessageObj` |\\n\\nIf implementer prefers zero ALTER, store blocks in a side table — **prefer single nullable column** for simplicity.\\n\\n#### Indexes on `messages`\\n\\n- `idx_messages_channel_created` on `(channel_id, created_at DESC, id DESC)` for history.\\n- `idx_messages_parent_created` on `(parent_id, created_at ASC, id ASC)` for replies.\\n\\n#### `message_reactions`\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `message_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE |\\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\\n| `emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| PRIMARY KEY | `(message_id, user_id, emoji)` | | Enforces idempotent POST |\\n\\nIndex: `(message_id, created_at ASC)` for aggregate ordering.\\n\\n#### `message_files` (forward seam for MARATHON-10)\\n\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `message_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE |\\n| `file_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | No FK until M10 `files` exists **or** FK added in M10 |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| PRIMARY KEY | `(message_id, file_id)` | | |\\n| UNIQUE | `(file_id)` | | A file attaches to at most one message |\\n\\n**M8 behavior:** if `files` table absent, refuse non-empty `file_ids` with 400 and leave `message_files` unused. M10 creates `files` and wires validation (uploader_id == caller, not already attached).\\n\\n### Schema change summary\\n\\n| Change | Compatible? |\\n|--------|-------------|\\n| v4 new tables + indexes + optional column | **Yes** — additive |\\n| v3 messages columns | **Unchanged** |\\n\\n### Invariants\\n\\n1. Soft-deleted messages have `deleted_at` non-null; excluded from history/reply lists.\\n2. `reply_count` never includes deleted children.\\n3. At most one reaction row per `(message_id, user_id, emoji)`.\\n4. `parent_id` either NULL or points to top-level message in same channel.\\n5. Pin routes continue to work; `get_message` / `row_to_message_obj` enrich reactions/mentions/files/reply_count for pin embeds too.\\n6. REST `MessageObj` never carries `seq`.\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `tests/test_messages.py` | Contract tests: post/list/pagination/edit/delete/replies/reactions/authz/423/409/empty body/parent rules/idempotent delete \\u0026 reactions; cluster read-after-write on second node |\\n\\n### Modify\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/db.py` | `_migrate_v4` / `_reverse_v4`; register in `MIGRATIONS` / `REVERSES` |\\n| `server/messages/store.py` | Create/list/get with enrichment; soft delete; reply list; reaction insert/delete/aggregate; mention resolve helper; `row_to_message_obj` fills real `reply_count`/`reactions`/`mentions`/`files` (files empty until M10); keep `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` unchanged |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | Add PATCH, DELETE, GET replies, POST/DELETE reactions; keep pin routes; factor `_require_pin_access` into shared `_require_message_channel_access(read|write)` used by pins + CRUD + reactions |\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Add `POST`/`GET /{channel_id}/messages` using messages store + same authz patterns as pins |\\n| `server/events.py` | No-op `publish_message_created/updated/deleted`, `publish_reaction_changed` with docstring payloads for M13 (`type`, `channel_id`, message/reactions fields — **seq assigned by M13**) |\\n| `server/messages/__init__.py` | Docstring: CRUD owned here |\\n| `tests/test_pins.py` | Only if enrichment changes assertions (prefer keep using `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`; update empty `reactions` expectations only if pins now return aggregates — still `[]` without reaction rows) |\\n| `tests/test_channels.py` | Optionally assert v4 migration present; do not break v3 assertions |\\n\\n### Do not touch\\n\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `static/**` | MARATHON-17 |\\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume only |\\n| File upload routes | MARATHON-10 |\\n| Search / slash / read_state | MARATHON-11 |\\n| WS / Redis fan-out | MARATHON-13/14 |\\n| DM create | MARATHON-9 |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Build order\\n\\n1. `db.py` v4 migration (+ reverse).\\n2. `messages/store.py` enrichment + CRUD + reactions + mentions.\\n3. Channel message POST/GET routes.\\n4. Message PATCH/DELETE/replies/reactions routes.\\n5. Event no-op hooks + call sites.\\n6. `tests/test_messages.py` (+ keep pins green).\\n\\n### Parallelism\\n\\n- Reaction endpoints can land in parallel with list pagination once insert/get exist.\\n- Channel GET/POST messages can land before PATCH/DELETE.\\n\\n### Downstream seams this task owns\\n\\n| Contract | Consumed by |\\n|----------|-------------|\\n| `MessageObj` + POST/GET channel messages + PATCH/DELETE | MARATHON-17 SPA; MARATHON-11 search/slash (reads body); MARATHON-13 event payloads |\\n| `{replies}` oldest-first | MARATHON-17 thread panel |\\n| `{reactions}` aggregate + POST/DELETE idempotent | MARATHON-17 emoji picker |\\n| Soft-delete + 409 on edit deleted | SPA + graders |\\n| `mentions: user_id[]` from `@username` | MARATHON-11 extends forms / mention_count |\\n| `file_ids` accept + `message_files` / 400 seam | MARATHON-10 attach rules |\\n| No-op message/reaction publish hooks | MARATHON-13 assigns dense `seq` + WS frames |\\n| Pin embed still `MessageObj` | Existing pin UI / tests |\\n\\n### Upstream\\n\\n- MARATHON-7 closed: v3 messages, pins, `assert_channel_writable`, channel membership matrix.\\n\\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\\n\\n- File upload + ownership attach enforcement details → MARATHON-10 (may tighten `file_ids` validation once `files` exists).\\n- Slash commands + `@channel`/`@here`/`@group` + read_state → MARATHON-11.\\n- Dense seq + WS resume → MARATHON-13.\\n- SPA transcript UI → MARATHON-17.\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\\n|------|----------------|--------------|\\n| `POST /api/files` multipart + download | future `server/files/*` | MARATHON-10 |\\n| Slash `/me` `/shrug` `/topic` … interception | message POST body | MARATHON-11 (M8 stores literal body) |\\n| `@channel` / `@here` / `@group-handle` | mentions | MARATHON-11 |\\n| `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` | read_state | MARATHON-11 |\\n| `GET /api/search` | search | MARATHON-11 |\\n| WS subscribe/resume + `seq` on frames | `server/events.py` real fan-out | MARATHON-13/14 |\\n| `POST /api/dms` | DM channels | MARATHON-9 |\\n| SPA message/thread/reaction UI | `static/**` | MARATHON-17 |\\n| Changing pin route semantics | `server/messages/routes.py` pin | Already shipped; only share helpers/enrichment |\\n| IRC message bridge | — | MARATHON-15 |\\n\\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\\n\\n| Hit | Disposition |\\n|-----|-------------|\\n| `server/messages/store.py` — thin `MessageObj` / get | **In scope** — enrich + CRUD |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` — pin only | **In scope** — add CRUD/reactions; keep pins |\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` — join/leave/pins | **In scope** — add messages POST/GET |\\n| `server/channels/store.py` — `assert_channel_writable`, membership | **In scope** — reuse; no ChannelObj key changes |\\n| `server/db.py` — v3 messages | **In scope** — add v4; do not recreate messages |\\n| `server/events.py` — `publish_user_updated` | **In scope** — add message/reaction no-ops |\\n| `server/app.py` — routers already mounted | **Out of scope** unless new router (none) |\\n| `tests/test_pins.py` — SQL-seed messages + MSG_KEYS | **Keep green**; enrichment must preserve keys |\\n| `tests/test_channels.py` — v3 schema asserts | **Keep green**; additive v4 OK |\\n| `static/js/*` — no message API yet | **Out of scope** — M17 |\\n| Grep: no channel messages routes yet | Greenfield under channels router |\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\\n|-----------|-------------------|\\n| Unauthenticated | **401** |\\n| Empty / whitespace `body` on POST/PATCH | **400** |\\n| `body` length 4000 OK; 4001 → **400** |\\n| POST without channel membership (public, workspace member only) | **403** |\\n| POST as channel member on archived | **423** |\\n| POST with `parent_id` pointing at a reply | **400** |\\n| POST with `parent_id` in another channel | **400** |\\n| POST with `parent_id` deleted | **400** |\\n| GET history includes replies | **Must not** — top-level only |\\n| GET history includes deleted | **Must not** |\\n| `before` on first page omitted | Newest `limit` messages |\\n| `limit=0` or `limit=101` | **400** |\\n| PATCH by non-author member | **403** |\\n| PATCH by workspace owner who is not author | **403** (owner is not enough for edit) |\\n| PATCH deleted | **409** |\\n| DELETE by author | **200** `{deleted:true}` |\\n| DELETE by workspace `owner_id` (not author) | **200** |\\n| DELETE by admin who is not owner_id | **403** |\\n| DELETE twice | Both **200** `{deleted:true}` |\\n| DELETE then GET history | Message absent |\\n| DELETE then PATCH | **409** |\\n| DELETE then POST reaction | **409** |\\n| POST reaction twice same emoji | **200**; single row; aggregate count unchanged |\\n| DELETE reaction never added | **200**; aggregate unchanged |\\n| Reaction emoji `\\\":+1:\\\"` vs `\\\"👍\\\"` | Distinct opaque strings |\\n| Mentions `@alice` mid-word `foo@alice` | No match |\\n| Mention self `@me` | Not included in `mentions` |\\n| Mention unknown user | Skipped (not 400) |\\n| `file_ids: [\\\"…\\\"]` before M10 files | **400** |\\n| `blocks: {}` (object not array) | **400** |\\n| `blocks: []` | Persist; MessageObj unchanged keys |\\n| Extra JSON fields | Ignore |\\n| Pin list after message soft-delete | Return pin entry with tombstone `MessageObj`: `body=\\\"\\\"`, `files=[]`, `reactions=[]`, `mentions=[]`, `reply_count` as computed; **or** skip pin — **prefer tombstone** so pin list length stable |\\n| SQLite busy | busy_timeout; fail closed after timeout (no 500 envelope inventiveness) |\\n| Concurrent reaction inserts | PK conflict → treat as idempotent success |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages` `{body:\\\"hi\\\"}` as channel member → **201** `{message}` with exact `MessageObj` keys; `edited_at=null`; `parent_id=null`; `reply_count=0`; `reactions=[]`; `files=[]`; `mentions` reflects `@username` rules.\\n2. Empty / whitespace body → **400** `validation_error`; message **not** inserted.\\n3. `GET /api/channels/{id}/messages` → **200** `{messages}` newest-first; only top-level non-deleted; supports `limit` + `before` cursor.\\n4. Reply via `parent_id` → **201**; parent’s subsequent `reply_count` is 1; `GET /api/messages/{parent}/replies` → **200** `{replies:[…]}` oldest-first.\\n5. `PATCH /api/messages/{id}` as author → **200**; `edited_at` set; non-author → **403**; after DELETE → PATCH **409**.\\n6. `DELETE /api/messages/{id}` as author or workspace owner → **200** `{deleted:true}` idempotent; message omitted from later GET history; non-author non-owner → **403**.\\n7. `POST /api/messages/{id}/reactions` `{emoji}` → **200** `{reactions:[{emoji,count,user_ids}]}` idempotent per `(user,emoji)`; `DELETE .../reactions/{emoji}` → **200** `{reactions}` idempotent.\\n8. Archived channel → POST/PATCH/DELETE message and reaction mutate → **423** `archived`; GET history/replies still **200** if authorized.\\n9. Private channel non-member → read/write **403** (workspace member) or **404** (stranger), consistent with pins.\\n10. **Cluster:** POST message on `:8000`, GET on `:8001` with same token sees it (shared SQLite).\\n11. Existing pin tests remain green; pin embed still exposes full `MessageObj` keys.\\n12. **Negative:** must **not** put `seq` on `MessageObj`; must **not** interpret slash commands; must **not** drop/recreate `messages` table; must **not** allow reply-to-reply; must **not** return deleted messages in channel history; must **not** use `{messages}` as the replies envelope key.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Automated (`tests/test_messages.py`)\\n\\n- Happy path create → list ordering → pagination with `before`.\\n- Thread create + replies ordering + `reply_count`.\\n- Edit sets `edited_at`; edit deleted → 409; delete idempotent; owner delete.\\n- Reactions aggregate shape, idempotent POST/DELETE, multi-user counts.\\n- Authz matrix: non-member, private, archived 423, author-only patch.\\n- Mentions: `@user` resolved; mid-word ignored; self excluded.\\n- `file_ids` non-empty → 400 (until files seeded/M10).\\n- Migration v4 applied; reverse drops v4 objects without destroying v3 unexpectedly in reverse tests (follow existing reverse pattern).\\n- Regression: run `tests/test_pins.py` + `tests/test_channels.py`.\\n\\n### Manual / human\\n\\n1. Boot cluster via `start.sh` (do not required for architect; implementer verifies).\\n2. Register two users; create workspace; join `#general`.\\n3. POST messages; confirm GET newest-first; reply; open replies oldest-first.\\n4. React twice; confirm count 1; second user react; count 2; delete own reaction.\\n5. Delete message; confirm absent from list; PATCH returns 409.\\n6. Archive channel; confirm POST message 423; unarchive; POST works.\\n7. Repeat GET against another node port to confirm shared DB.\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"Design complete for MARATHON-8 (messages/threads/reactions REST). Grounded in epic product contract + MARATHON-7 MessageObj/pin/423/membership seams + current server/messages + db v3. Extends schema (v4 reactions/files join), does not recreate messages. file_ids/slash/@channel deferred to M10/M11 with explicit seams. Ready for lead review; implementer label remains backend after architect approval.\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:01.573541406Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:40:54.565406517Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"Note: depends on channels task. POST channels/{id}/messages {body,parent_id?,file_ids?,blocks?}; empty body 400; MessageObj with author, reply_count, edited_at, files, reactions, mentions. GET messages newest-first with limit/before. PATCH author-only sets edited_at; edit deleted → 409. DELETE author or workspace owner, idempotent 200 {deleted:true}. GET messages/{parent_id}/replies oldest-first. Reactions POST/DELETE idempotent per (user,emoji) return {reactions}.\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-11\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:16.962464474Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-13\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:29.97263884Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-10\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Files: upload, metadata, download, attach\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:47.139019113Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-17\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:47.207494951Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 42,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-8\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"DESIGN-AUTO-APPROVED pass=22\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:40:54.576884693Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nThe 'loom data' subtree contains thin CLI commands that interact\nwith the configured loom issue backend. When --server or LOOM_SERVER_URL is\nset, commands talk to that loom server over HTTP. Without a server, issue\ncommands use the local backend selected by the workspace configuration and\ndaemon IPC environment.\n\nUse 'loom data' commands when:\n  • You want a backend-aware command surface for agents and scripts.\n  • You want to manage agents on a remote loom server.\n  • You are scripting against a hosted loom deployment.\n\nExamples:\n  loom data show <id> --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data ready --limit 10\n  loom data list --server http://localhost:8080 -o json | jq '.[].id'\n  loom data monitor --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data agent stop falcon --server http://localhost:8080\n\nRoot-level --server / --workspace are mirrored into LOOM_SERVER_URL /\nLOOM_WORKSPACE in PersistentPreRunE, so 'loom --server URL data show ID'\nand 'loom data show ID --server URL' resolve identically. The data\nsubcommand reads from env, not from its own flag.\n\nUsage:\n  loom data [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  agent       Control a single agent on the loom server (stop/start/restart/yield)\n  agents      List agents managed by the loom server daemon (HTTP)\n  blocked     List issues that are blocked by other open issues (HTTP)\n  claim       Atomically claim an issue\n  close       Close an issue (HTTP)\n  comment     Add a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n  create      Create an issue\n  list        List issues (HTTP)\n  monitor     Show monitor dashboard from a loom server (HTTP, single-shot)\n  ready       List issues that are ready to work on (HTTP)\n  show        Show a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n  update      Update issue fields\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help            help for data\n  -o, --output string   Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string   Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\n\nUse \"loom data [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","localExecutionTimeMs":52},"isBackground":false},"description":"Merge main and show MARATHON-8 task"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-32310ab2-55f8-486e-90df-a81025d89202-0\nfc_6088b184-8310-9214-9423-fe731e494f1c_0","startedAtMs":"1787445666011","completedAtMs":"1787445666396"},"model_call_id":"c218b17a-bebf-49fa-8762-54ad8e9c3c31-0-58tw","session_id":"5de21c73-718e-49ab-8d79-ce218632b44f","timestamp_ms":1787445666443}
