{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-ec0d4b95-2040-4b14-bf7b-b2e802c4bd4a-7\nfc_ca733bd4-d761-9320-a4ed-a26fc1a946f8_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-9 --output json | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d.get('design') or ''\n# print the rest of design after 'List-query defense'\nidx=design.find('List-query defense')\nprint(design[idx:] if idx>=0 else design[-8000:])\n\"","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-ec0d4b95-2040-4b14-bf7b-b2e802c4bd4a-7\nfc_ca733bd4-d761-9320-a4ed-a26fc1a946f8_0","simpleCommands":["loom","python3"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-9"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-9 --output json"},{"name":"python3","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"string","value":"\"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d.get('design') or ''\n# print the rest of design after 'List-query defense'\nidx=design.find('List-query defense')\nprint(design[idx:] if idx>=0 else design[-8000:])\n\""}],"fullText":"python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d.get('design') or ''\n# print the rest of design after 'List-query defense'\nidx=design.find('List-query defense')\nprint(design[idx:] if idx>=0 else design[-8000:])\n\""}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Fetch remainder of design doc","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"aec3e14e-ecc5-40d6-b9d9-d0b4accedb3f","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-9 --output json | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d.get('design') or ''\n# print the rest of design after 'List-query defense'\nidx=design.find('List-query defense')\nprint(design[idx:] if idx>=0 else design[-8000:])\n\"","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"List-query defense (in scope)\n\nUpdate `list_channels_for_workspace_user` visibility predicate from “public OR member” to:\n\n- visible if **member**, OR\n- visible if **`is_dm=0` AND `is_private=0`** (true public)\n\nEquivalently: `(c.is_dm = 0 AND c.is_private = 0) OR cm.user_id IS NOT NULL`.\n\n### Schema change summary\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| No DDL | **Yes** |\n| List SQL predicate tighten | **Yes** — only hides rows that should not have been visible |\n| DM owner-bypass removal | Behavior change for owners on `is_dm` only |\n\n### Invariants\n\n1. At most one `is_dm` channel per `(workspace_id, unordered user pair)` (enforced by deterministic name + UNIQUE).\n2. `POST .../channels` still forces `is_dm=false` (MARATHON-7).\n3. Get-or-create never creates a second row for the same pair.\n4. After a successful `POST /api/dms`, both users have `channel_members` rows.\n5. `ChannelObj.is_dm === true` for these rows; SPA list split continues to work.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/dms/__init__.py` | Package marker / docstring: DM get-or-create owned here |\n| `server/dms/routes.py` | `APIRouter(prefix=\"/api/dms\")`; `POST \"\"` handler; pydantic body; transaction; map errors |\n| `server/dms/store.py` | `canonical_dm_name(...)`; `get_or_create_dm_channel(conn, *, workspace_id, caller_id, peer_id) -> channel_id`; peer/workspace checks raising `ApiError` |\n| `tests/test_dms.py` | Contract tests (see Testing Strategy) |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` for dms router |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | Add `create_dm_channel(...)` (bypass public name validation path used by user-created channels **or** validate synthetic name after generation); fix `list_channels_for_workspace_user` predicate for DM/private; optional `find_dm_by_name` |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | In `_require_channel_read_access`, pin list, PATCH, leave as needed: **`is_dm` ⇒ membership required** (no owner-only bypass) |\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | Same DM membership rule in `_require_pin_access` (and document for M8 shared helper) |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/**` | MARATHON-17 owns DM picker UI; M16 list split already correct |\n| `server/db.py` | No migration in this design |\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume `get_user_by_id` / deps only |\n| Message CRUD routes | MARATHON-8 |\n| IRC / WS / Redis | MARATHON-13/14/15 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order (this task)\n\n1. `channels/store.py` — `create_dm_channel` + list predicate.\n2. `dms/store.py` + `dms/routes.py` + mount in `app.py`.\n3. Authz tighten for `is_dm` in channel/message routes.\n4. `tests/test_dms.py` (+ any small assertion updates if list tests assume old predicate).\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Independent of MARATHON-8 message CRUD **except** shared DM authz rule (coordinate via this design’s Interface Contracts).\n- Independent of MARATHON-12 groups/invitations.\n- MARATHON-17 can stub against this contract once merged.\n\n### Cross-task seams\n\n| Contract | Owner | Consumer |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| `POST /api/dms` → `{channel_id}` | **MARATHON-9** | MARATHON-17 (DM open), graders |\n| `ChannelObj.is_dm` + list visibility | MARATHON-5/7 + **this list fix** | MARATHON-16 shell, MARATHON-17 |\n| DM member-only authz (no owner bypass) | **MARATHON-9** | MARATHON-8 message helpers must match |\n| Message post in DM channel | MARATHON-8 | Needs channel membership (created here) |\n| DM display labels / picker UI | MARATHON-17 | Uses `channel_id` + members/profiles |\n\n### Declared dependents\n\n- MARATHON-17 (SPA channels/DMs UX)\n- MARATHON-8 (messages in DM channels; authz note)\n\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- Group DMs / multi-user conversations.\n- `dm_pairs` table if hash-in-name is ever insufficient.\n- Forbidding archive/leave on DMs.\n- Client-side peer label rendering.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| SPA DM picker / open-DM button / peer label | `static/js/*`, MARATHON-17 | Frontend task; shell already has empty-capable `dms-list` |\n| Message send/list inside DM | MARATHON-8 | Separate REST surface |\n| Search / read_state / slash | MARATHON-11 | |\n| WS fan-out `channel` events | MARATHON-13/14 | |\n| IRC DM mapping | MARATHON-15 | |\n| Group DMs | — | Not in task |\n| Changing private-channel **owner** bypass for non-DM privates | `channels/routes.py` | Keep MARATHON-7 behavior for `is_private && !is_dm` |\n| `POST /api/channels` creating `is_dm` | already forbidden | Remains forbidden |\n| Migration v4/v5 DDL | `server/db.py` | Avoid M8/M12 version collision; name uniqueness sufficient |\n| `channel-add-member-*` for DMs | SPA hooks | DMs are pair-only via this endpoint |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `server/channels/store.py` `is_dm` always false on create; list predicate | **In scope** — DM create helper + list fix |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` private/DM treated alike; owner bypass | **In scope** — DM membership tighten |\n| `server/messages/routes.py` private/DM pin authz | **In scope** — same DM rule |\n| `server/db.py` `is_dm` column | **Unchanged** |\n| `static/js/shell.js` `dms-list` / `is_dm` split | **Out of scope** — already correct |\n| `tests/test_channels.py` `is_dm is False` on normal create | **Out of scope** — keep; add `test_dms.py` |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` / `test_workspaces.py` `is_dm` assertions | **Out of scope** unless list predicate breaks a fixture |\n| Grep: no `/api/dms` router yet | Greenfield `server/dms` |\n| MARATHON-7/8/16 designs reserving `POST /api/dms` | **This task** |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| A→B then B→A | Same `channel_id` |\n| Repeat A→B | Same `channel_id`; **200**; no second row |\n| Concurrent A→B and B→A | One INSERT wins; loser hits UNIQUE/`IntegrityError` on `(workspace_id,name)` → re-SELECT by name → return existing id (no **500**) |\n| Caller left DM earlier | Ensure re-INSERT `channel_members` for caller (and peer if missing); return same id |\n| Peer left DM earlier | Same ensure-both-memberships |\n| Self `user_id` | **400** `validation_error` |\n| Peer not in workspace | **404** `user not found` |\n| Caller not in workspace | **404** `workspace not found` |\n| Archived DM exists | Still return its `channel_id` (do not create replacement). Messaging may **423** via existing guard (MARATHON-7/8) |\n| Workspace owner not in DM opens channel routes | **403** (member of ws) / **404** (stranger) — **not** owner bypass |\n| Guest DMs a member | **200** if both are workspace members |\n| Extra body keys | Ignored |\n| `workspace_id` is a slug string | **404** (id lookup fails) — clients must send UUID `workspace.id` |\n| User creates public channel whose name collides with a DM hash | Astronomically unlikely; if IntegrityError on DM insert and re-read finds non-`is_dm` row → **409** `conflict` with clear message (abort; do not hijack) |\n| Unauthenticated | **401** |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Authenticated `POST /api/dms` with `{user_id, workspace_id}` for two distinct workspace members → **200** `{ \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }`.\n2. Calling again with the same pair (same caller) → **200** with **identical** `channel_id`.\n3. Peer calling with the caller’s id (swapped direction) → **200** with the **same** `channel_id`.\n4. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as either participant includes a channel with that id where `is_dm === true` (and typically `is_private === true`).\n5. A third workspace member’s workspace detail must **NOT** include that DM channel.\n6. Persisted row has `is_dm=1` (verify via API list/detail or DB in tests).\n7. Self-DM → **400** `validation_error`; must **NOT** create a channel.\n8. Unknown peer id → **404**; must **NOT** create a channel.\n9. Peer registered globally but not in workspace → **404**; must **NOT** create a channel.\n10. Caller not in workspace → **404**.\n11. Unauthenticated → **401**.\n12. After participant `POST /api/channels/{id}/leave`, a subsequent `POST /api/dms` for the same pair returns the **same** `channel_id` and restores membership (subsequent channel member list / message write authz succeeds for that user).\n13. Workspace owner who is **not** a DM member must **NOT** read DM pins/members via owner bypass (**403** or **404** per rules above).\n14. Negative: `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` still cannot create `is_dm=true` channels.\n15. Negative: response must **NOT** require a `channel` object key for success (only `channel_id`).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (`tests/test_dms.py`)\n\n- Happy path create + idempotent repeat + reverse direction same id.\n- Both users see DM on workspace detail; third member does not.\n- Self / missing peer / non-member peer / non-member caller / unauthenticated.\n- Leave then get-or-create restores membership.\n- Owner-without-membership denied on `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` (or pins) for the DM.\n- Optional: concurrent create smoke (two threads) still yields one row.\n- Regression: existing `tests/test_channels.py` / `test_workspaces.py` stay green.\n\n### Manual / cluster\n\n1. Register users A,B,C; create workspace; add B and C as members.\n2. On `:8000`, A `POST /api/dms` with B → note `channel_id`.\n3. On `:8001`, B `POST /api/dms` with A → same id (shared SQLite).\n4. A and B `GET` workspace detail → DM present; C’s detail → absent.\n5. Confirm `is_dm` true in listed channel object.\n\n### Human verify\n\n- No SPA change required; `curl`/httpie against any node with bearer token is enough for this task.\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T00:59:17.696Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":72,"interleavedOutput":"time=2026-08-23T00:59:17.696Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\nList-query defense (in scope)\n\nUpdate `list_channels_for_workspace_user` visibility predicate from “public OR member” to:\n\n- visible if **member**, OR\n- visible if **`is_dm=0` AND `is_private=0`** (true public)\n\nEquivalently: `(c.is_dm = 0 AND c.is_private = 0) OR cm.user_id IS NOT NULL`.\n\n### Schema change summary\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| No DDL | **Yes** |\n| List SQL predicate tighten | **Yes** — only hides rows that should not have been visible |\n| DM owner-bypass removal | Behavior change for owners on `is_dm` only |\n\n### Invariants\n\n1. At most one `is_dm` channel per `(workspace_id, unordered user pair)` (enforced by deterministic name + UNIQUE).\n2. `POST .../channels` still forces `is_dm=false` (MARATHON-7).\n3. Get-or-create never creates a second row for the same pair.\n4. After a successful `POST /api/dms`, both users have `channel_members` rows.\n5. `ChannelObj.is_dm === true` for these rows; SPA list split continues to work.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/dms/__init__.py` | Package marker / docstring: DM get-or-create owned here |\n| `server/dms/routes.py` | `APIRouter(prefix=\"/api/dms\")`; `POST \"\"` handler; pydantic body; transaction; map errors |\n| `server/dms/store.py` | `canonical_dm_name(...)`; `get_or_create_dm_channel(conn, *, workspace_id, caller_id, peer_id) -> channel_id`; peer/workspace checks raising `ApiError` |\n| `tests/test_dms.py` | Contract tests (see Testing Strategy) |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` for dms router |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | Add `create_dm_channel(...)` (bypass public name validation path used by user-created channels **or** validate synthetic name after generation); fix `list_channels_for_workspace_user` predicate for DM/private; optional `find_dm_by_name` |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | In `_require_channel_read_access`, pin list, PATCH, leave as needed: **`is_dm` ⇒ membership required** (no owner-only bypass) |\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | Same DM membership rule in `_require_pin_access` (and document for M8 shared helper) |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/**` | MARATHON-17 owns DM picker UI; M16 list split already correct |\n| `server/db.py` | No migration in this design |\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume `get_user_by_id` / deps only |\n| Message CRUD routes | MARATHON-8 |\n| IRC / WS / Redis | MARATHON-13/14/15 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order (this task)\n\n1. `channels/store.py` — `create_dm_channel` + list predicate.\n2. `dms/store.py` + `dms/routes.py` + mount in `app.py`.\n3. Authz tighten for `is_dm` in channel/message routes.\n4. `tests/test_dms.py` (+ any small assertion updates if list tests assume old predicate).\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Independent of MARATHON-8 message CRUD **except** shared DM authz rule (coordinate via this design’s Interface Contracts).\n- Independent of MARATHON-12 groups/invitations.\n- MARATHON-17 can stub against this contract once merged.\n\n### Cross-task seams\n\n| Contract | Owner | Consumer |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| `POST /api/dms` → `{channel_id}` | **MARATHON-9** | MARATHON-17 (DM open), graders |\n| `ChannelObj.is_dm` + list visibility | MARATHON-5/7 + **this list fix** | MARATHON-16 shell, MARATHON-17 |\n| DM member-only authz (no owner bypass) | **MARATHON-9** | MARATHON-8 message helpers must match |\n| Message post in DM channel | MARATHON-8 | Needs channel membership (created here) |\n| DM display labels / picker UI | MARATHON-17 | Uses `channel_id` + members/profiles |\n\n### Declared dependents\n\n- MARATHON-17 (SPA channels/DMs UX)\n- MARATHON-8 (messages in DM channels; authz note)\n\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- Group DMs / multi-user conversations.\n- `dm_pairs` table if hash-in-name is ever insufficient.\n- Forbidding archive/leave on DMs.\n- Client-side peer label rendering.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| SPA DM picker / open-DM button / peer label | `static/js/*`, MARATHON-17 | Frontend task; shell already has empty-capable `dms-list` |\n| Message send/list inside DM | MARATHON-8 | Separate REST surface |\n| Search / read_state / slash | MARATHON-11 | |\n| WS fan-out `channel` events | MARATHON-13/14 | |\n| IRC DM mapping | MARATHON-15 | |\n| Group DMs | — | Not in task |\n| Changing private-channel **owner** bypass for non-DM privates | `channels/routes.py` | Keep MARATHON-7 behavior for `is_private && !is_dm` |\n| `POST /api/channels` creating `is_dm` | already forbidden | Remains forbidden |\n| Migration v4/v5 DDL | `server/db.py` | Avoid M8/M12 version collision; name uniqueness sufficient |\n| `channel-add-member-*` for DMs | SPA hooks | DMs are pair-only via this endpoint |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `server/channels/store.py` `is_dm` always false on create; list predicate | **In scope** — DM create helper + list fix |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` private/DM treated alike; owner bypass | **In scope** — DM membership tighten |\n| `server/messages/routes.py` private/DM pin authz | **In scope** — same DM rule |\n| `server/db.py` `is_dm` column | **Unchanged** |\n| `static/js/shell.js` `dms-list` / `is_dm` split | **Out of scope** — already correct |\n| `tests/test_channels.py` `is_dm is False` on normal create | **Out of scope** — keep; add `test_dms.py` |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` / `test_workspaces.py` `is_dm` assertions | **Out of scope** unless list predicate breaks a fixture |\n| Grep: no `/api/dms` router yet | Greenfield `server/dms` |\n| MARATHON-7/8/16 designs reserving `POST /api/dms` | **This task** |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| A→B then B→A | Same `channel_id` |\n| Repeat A→B | Same `channel_id`; **200**; no second row |\n| Concurrent A→B and B→A | One INSERT wins; loser hits UNIQUE/`IntegrityError` on `(workspace_id,name)` → re-SELECT by name → return existing id (no **500**) |\n| Caller left DM earlier | Ensure re-INSERT `channel_members` for caller (and peer if missing); return same id |\n| Peer left DM earlier | Same ensure-both-memberships |\n| Self `user_id` | **400** `validation_error` |\n| Peer not in workspace | **404** `user not found` |\n| Caller not in workspace | **404** `workspace not found` |\n| Archived DM exists | Still return its `channel_id` (do not create replacement). Messaging may **423** via existing guard (MARATHON-7/8) |\n| Workspace owner not in DM opens channel routes | **403** (member of ws) / **404** (stranger) — **not** owner bypass |\n| Guest DMs a member | **200** if both are workspace members |\n| Extra body keys | Ignored |\n| `workspace_id` is a slug string | **404** (id lookup fails) — clients must send UUID `workspace.id` |\n| User creates public channel whose name collides with a DM hash | Astronomically unlikely; if IntegrityError on DM insert and re-read finds non-`is_dm` row → **409** `conflict` with clear message (abort; do not hijack) |\n| Unauthenticated | **401** |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Authenticated `POST /api/dms` with `{user_id, workspace_id}` for two distinct workspace members → **200** `{ \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }`.\n2. Calling again with the same pair (same caller) → **200** with **identical** `channel_id`.\n3. Peer calling with the caller’s id (swapped direction) → **200** with the **same** `channel_id`.\n4. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as either participant includes a channel with that id where `is_dm === true` (and typically `is_private === true`).\n5. A third workspace member’s workspace detail must **NOT** include that DM channel.\n6. Persisted row has `is_dm=1` (verify via API list/detail or DB in tests).\n7. Self-DM → **400** `validation_error`; must **NOT** create a channel.\n8. Unknown peer id → **404**; must **NOT** create a channel.\n9. Peer registered globally but not in workspace → **404**; must **NOT** create a channel.\n10. Caller not in workspace → **404**.\n11. Unauthenticated → **401**.\n12. After participant `POST /api/channels/{id}/leave`, a subsequent `POST /api/dms` for the same pair returns the **same** `channel_id` and restores membership (subsequent channel member list / message write authz succeeds for that user).\n13. Workspace owner who is **not** a DM member must **NOT** read DM pins/members via owner bypass (**403** or **404** per rules above).\n14. Negative: `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` still cannot create `is_dm=true` channels.\n15. Negative: response must **NOT** require a `channel` object key for success (only `channel_id`).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (`tests/test_dms.py`)\n\n- Happy path create + idempotent repeat + reverse direction same id.\n- Both users see DM on workspace detail; third member does not.\n- Self / missing peer / non-member peer / non-member caller / unauthenticated.\n- Leave then get-or-create restores membership.\n- Owner-without-membership denied on `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` (or pins) for the DM.\n- Optional: concurrent create smoke (two threads) still yields one row.\n- Regression: existing `tests/test_channels.py` / `test_workspaces.py` stay green.\n\n### Manual / cluster\n\n1. Register users A,B,C; create workspace; add B and C as members.\n2. On `:8000`, A `POST /api/dms` with B → note `channel_id`.\n3. On `:8001`, B `POST /api/dms` with A → same id (shared SQLite).\n4. A and B `GET` workspace detail → DM present; C’s detail → absent.\n5. Confirm `is_dm` true in listed channel object.\n\n### Human verify\n\n- No SPA change required; `curl`/httpie against any node with bearer token is enough for this task.\n","localExecutionTimeMs":31},"isBackground":false},"description":"Fetch remainder of design doc"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-ec0d4b95-2040-4b14-bf7b-b2e802c4bd4a-7\nfc_ca733bd4-d761-9320-a4ed-a26fc1a946f8_0","startedAtMs":"1787446757654","completedAtMs":"1787446757726"},"model_call_id":"8e476999-2b8c-4e02-939d-1221ca0eaa72-2-np0y","session_id":"aec3e14e-ecc5-40d6-b9d9-d0b4accedb3f","timestamp_ms":1787446757748}
