{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-997a0769-4277-4692-ac2c-befb5c41be06-9\nfc_680973d8-e6da-9547-b40e-a6c00096d3ec_1","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/m18-design.md","offset":400},"result":{"success":{"content":"| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| Message composer, reactions, thread panel open | `static/js/*`, MARATHON-17 | Different SPA task |\n| User groups CRUD UI | `settings-*` could grow; `server/groups` | Not in MARATHON-18 description |\n| Profile PATCH UI | `PATCH /api/users/me` | M16 deferred “profile” vaguely to settings; **this** task’s General tab is workspace name/join_mode only |\n| Pins UI | `/api/channels/{id}/pins` | Channel settings text is members/topic/archive only |\n| WebSocket live member updates | MARATHON-13 | Poll/refetch on tab open is enough |\n| IRC | MARATHON-15 | Unrelated |\n| Changing invitation accept semantics / join_mode gates | `server/invitations/**`, `server/workspaces/routes.py` join | Already shipped; SPA consumes |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` as substitute for add-member | existing join route | Wrong authz for private add; out of scope as the add mechanism |\n| React/Vite migration | — | Conflicts with M16 |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `static/index.html`, `static/js/shell.js`, `static/js/app.js`, `static/css/app.css` | **In scope** — extend |\n| `static/js/api.js`, `storage.js`, `auth_ui.js` | **Reuse** — no contract change |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | **In scope** — extend required selectors |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` GET members / PATCH / archive | **Consume**; add POST members |\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` PATCH/members/transfer | **Consume only** |\n| `server/invitations/routes.py` | **Consume only** |\n| `tests/test_workspace_members.py`, `test_invitations.py`, `test_channels.py` | **Out of scope** to rewrite; keep green; add new tests |\n| Grep `settings-` / `invitation-` in `static/` | No hits yet — greenfield UI |\n| M7 note `channel-add-member-*` | **In scope** via new POST + testids |\n| Groups package | **Out of scope** UI |\n| `server/events.py` | **Out of scope** |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Open workspace settings without admin role | Modal opens; General fields disabled or save → 403 visible; Members badge-only; Invitations admin-only empty/error |\n| PATCH general with blank name | Client may pre-check; server **400** → `settings-general-error` |\n| Invalid join_mode option | Must not be choosable in UI; if forced, server 400 |\n| Role select to `owner` | **Must not** be an option |\n| Admin tries to demote another admin | No select **or** PATCH 403 → revert + error |\n| Transfer to non-admin | Client only lists admins; server 400 if forced |\n| Create invitation as member | 403 → `invitation-create-error`; modal stays open |\n| Revoke already-used/expired code | 404 → refresh list (row disappears) |\n| Accept invalid/expired code | 404 → `invitation-accept-error`; stay on onboarding |\n| Accept targeted invite as wrong user | 403 → visible error |\n| Accept success while already member | 200 → enter workspace (idempotent) |\n| Topic save on archived channel | 423 → `settings-topic-error`; suggest unarchive |\n| Archive by non-owner | Control hidden/disabled; if called, 403 error |\n| Archive `#general` | Allowed if owner (server permits); UI does not special-case unless server errors |\n| Add member unknown username | 400 → `channel-add-member-error` |\n| Add member who is not workspace member | 400 → same |\n| Add to DM channel | Button hidden for `is_dm`; if called, 403 |\n| Add when already member | 200; list unchanged except refresh |\n| Network timeout | Visible error on active form; re-enable controls |\n| 401 on any settings call | Clear tokens; show auth modal; close settings |\n| Double-click save | Disable control until response; single in-flight request |\n| Modal open during workspace switch | Close modals; drop stale channel id |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET /` HTML includes DOM ids `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` and the normative `data-testid`s listed above for modal chrome, tabs, general fields, invitation accept form, and channel settings fields (list rows may be empty until data loads).\n2. Authenticated owner/admin can open workspace settings, change **name** and **join_mode**, save, and see updates in `workspace-header` / subsequent `GET` workspace detail.\n3. Member/guest **cannot** persist general settings (disabled UI and/or visible 403); must **not** silently succeed.\n4. Members tab lists all workspace members with `role-badge`; owner/admin can change permitted roles via `role-select`; forbidden changes show error and do **not** leave a lying UI role.\n5. Owner can transfer ownership to an admin via transfer controls; previous owner becomes admin in the refreshed list.\n6. Admin/owner can create an invitation; `invitation-code` is visible; list shows active invites; revoke removes the row.\n7. Onboarding `invitation-accept-*` redeems a valid code and enters the workspace shell; invite_only workspaces become accessible without using broken join-by-slug alone.\n8. With an active public/private channel, channel settings shows members (`channel-member-row`), allows topic save for authorized callers, and owner can archive/unarchive with UI reflecting `is_archived`.\n9. Topic save on archived channel surfaces **423** message and must **not** clear the topic field to empty on failure.\n10. Channel add-member with a workspace member username adds them to `channel_members` (UI list updates); guest cannot add; outsider username fails visibly.\n11. Opening one settings modal closes the other; logout closes modals and clears privileged data from the DOM on next login.\n12. Existing MARATHON-16 selectors and auth/workspace flows remain green (`tests/test_spa_shell.py` + prior SPA behavior).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- Extend/add TestClient tests asserting required ids/testids in `GET /` and that `settings_ui.js` is served as a static asset.\n- Backend tests for `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` matrix (owner/admin/member/guest, private/public, idempotent, DM rejection, non-member target).\n- Do **not** require a browser in unit CI; optional Playwright (as M16 notes) at 1280×900 for human/agent verification.\n\n### Manual / CUA script (1280×900)\n\n1. Register → create workspace → open workspace settings → rename + set `invite_only` → save → reload → values stick.\n2. Add second user via invitation create → copy `invitation-code` → logout → register other user → accept code → lands in workspace.\n3. As owner, change member role member→admin; confirm badge/select; attempt illegal admin-on-admin as admin user → error.\n4. Select `#general` → channel settings → set topic → archive → confirm topic save fails with archived error → unarchive → topic save works.\n5. Create private channel (API or future M17 UI) → add workspace member via `channel-add-member-*` → member appears in list.\n6. As guest/member, confirm invitations tab and archive controls are not usable.\n\n### Verification mindset\n\nOutside-in: selectors + REST envelopes + visible errors. No reliance on reading JS internals beyond confirming assets load.\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":490,"fileSize":28740,"path":"/tmp/m18-design.md","readRange":{"startLine":400,"endLine":490},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-997a0769-4277-4692-ac2c-befb5c41be06-9\nfc_680973d8-e6da-9547-b40e-a6c00096d3ec_1","startedAtMs":"1787447727004","completedAtMs":"1787447727233"},"model_call_id":"3beb2332-45ec-488d-928b-2b33d3bcc648-3-bw9u","session_id":"12ba3f12-6cfa-4f54-b2fb-87efd92700d6","timestamp_ms":1787447727258}
