{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-4404e6c3-6678-4c75-b41a-18bb29c6784c-0\nfc_afb8bac5-0659-9a69-8570-9a09c094dd40_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"git merge --no-edit main && loom data show MARATHON-13 --output json && loom data show MARATHON --output json 2>/dev/null || loom data show marathon --output json 2>/dev/null; pwd; ls -la","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-4404e6c3-6678-4c75-b41a-18bb29c6784c-0\nfc_afb8bac5-0659-9a69-8570-9a09c094dd40_0","simpleCommands":["git","loom","loom","loom","pwd","ls"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"merge"},{"type":"word","value":"--no-edit"},{"type":"word","value":"main"}],"fullText":"git merge --no-edit main"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-13"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-13 --output json"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON --output json"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"marathon"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show marathon --output json"},{"name":"pwd","args":[],"fullText":"pwd"},{"name":"ls","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-la"}],"fullText":"ls -la"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Merge main and load task/epic data","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"b76c730e-983d-4b18-9e06-1d6745c005de","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"git merge --no-edit main && loom data show MARATHON-13 --output json && loom data show MARATHON --output json 2>/dev/null || loom data show marathon --output json 2>/dev/null; pwd; ls -la","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"Already up to date.\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-13\",\n  \"title\": \"WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"priority\": 0,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"assignee\": \"backend-dev-1\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"backend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-13 — WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task adds the real-time seam for Huddle: an authenticated WebSocket at `GET /api/ws?token=…`, client `subscribe` / `resume` control frames, and a **dense per-channel `seq`** assigned in shared SQLite so every durable channel mutation (messages including thread replies, reactions, membership, channel mutations, pins) gets a gap-free monotonic frame `{type, seq, channel_id, …}`. Profile changes keep the existing channel-less `user.updated` shape (no `seq`). Same `seq` / event rows are visible from every HTTP node via the shared DB; **live cross-node push** remains MARATHON-14 (this task delivers live frames to connections on the writing node and makes catch-up via `resume` work on any node).\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Seq SoT | **Shared SQLite** counters + durable `channel_events` log (not Redis). Allocation is in the **same transaction** as the HTTP mutation so rollbacks never burn a seq. |\\n| Dense rule | Per `channel_id`, `seq` starts at **0** (empty) and first durable event is **1**, then `+1` per committed durable event. No gaps, no duplicates, no reuse. |\\n| WS transport | FastAPI/Starlette WebSocket on **`/api/ws`**, auth via query `token` (raw bearer, same value as `Authorization: Bearer`). |\\n| Control protocol | Client JSON: `subscribe`, `resume` (with `since_seq`). Server JSON: `subscribed`, `resumed`, `resume.gap`, plus durable/live event frames and `user.updated`. |\\n| History vs live | `subscribe` = watch from **now** (ack `head_seq`, no backlog). `resume` = authorize + **replay** `(since_seq+1)…head` then live, or `resume.gap` if `since_seq` is older than the retained tail. Channel history UI still uses REST (MARATHON-8). |\\n| Retention | Keep the last **`CHANNEL_EVENT_RETAIN = 10_000`** events per channel (constant in code). After append, prune `seq \\u003c head_seq - RETAIN + 1`. Tail = minimum retained `seq` (or `1` if none pruned yet / empty head). |\\n| Local delivery | Process-local **connection hub** on each node. `emit` records to SQLite; **after commit** `deliver(frame)` fans to local WS subscribers. Redis publish is a **no-op stub hook** owned by MARATHON-14. |\\n| Cross-node live | **Out of scope** (MARATHON-14). Reconnect-to-other-node **replay** works in this task because resume reads SQLite. |\\n| REST objects | **Do not** add `seq` to `MessageObj` / `ChannelObj` / `UserObj` (MARATHON-8/4 locks). |\\n| Thread replies | Same frame type `message.created`; “reply” is `message.parent_id != null` inside the nested `MessageObj` (no separate `reply.*` type). |\\n| Publish call sites | Refactor existing post-commit `publish_*` so **seq append happens inside the open write transaction**; hub deliver stays post-commit and must not raise. |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- Epic + MARATHON-2 forbid Redis as SoT (Redis `SIGKILL` must not break dense seq). Shared SQLite is already the cluster SoT.\\n- MARATHON-8/4 already froze event *shapes* and “seq on WS frames only”; this task completes transport + numbering without reopening REST contracts.\\n- Separating local hub (M13) from Redis fan-out (M14) lets IRC/SPA resume against any node immediately while M14 finishes cluster push and outage behavior.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| Redis `INCR` for seq | Breaks dense continuity during Redis outage (epic / M14) |\\n| Seq on `MessageObj` | Explicitly rejected in MARATHON-8 |\\n| Only in-memory events (no `channel_events`) | Cannot resume after reconnect / other node; violates epic replay |\\n| Separate `reply.*` frame types | Task wording lists “reply” as a durable class; existing hooks + MessageObj already encode replies via `parent_id` |\\n| Cookie/`Authorization` header-only WS auth | Browsers cannot set arbitrary WS headers; task specifies `?token=` |\\n| Implement Redis pub/sub in this task | Owned by MARATHON-14; stub only |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\nRetention is finite (`10_000` events/channel). Clients that disconnect longer than the retained window get `resume.gap` and must reload via REST — acceptable for the marathon cluster and keeps SQLite bounded. Live multi-node push waits for M14; until then a client subscribed only on node B will not see live frames for writes on node A until it `resume`s (or reconnects).\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\n- **MARATHON-2:** SQLite SoT; Redis ephemeral; `HUDDLE_REDIS_URL` present but unused for durability here.\\n- **MARATHON-3:** Bearer opaque tokens in SQLite; UUID4 ids; `{error:{code,message}}` for HTTP (WS uses JSON control/error frames, not HTTP envelopes after upgrade).\\n- **MARATHON-4:** `user.updated` = `{type,user}` with **no** `channel_id`/`seq`; `UserObj` keys unchanged.\\n- **MARATHON-7/8:** Channel read/write authz matrices; `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` / `ChannelObj` key sets; soft-delete semantics; archived → HTTP 423 (no WS event for rejected writes).\\n- **MARATHON-8:** No-op publish hooks become real emitters; docstring payload shapes stay the source of truth and gain `seq` where applicable.\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Shared: durable channel frame envelope\\n\\nEvery durable per-channel frame **must** include:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"\\u003cevent-type\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"seq\\\": 42,\\n  \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid\\u003e\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n| Field | Rules |\\n|-------|--------|\\n| `type` | string; one of the durable types below |\\n| `seq` | integer ≥ 1; dense per `channel_id` |\\n| `channel_id` | string; never null on durable frames |\\n| Extra fields | Per type; nested REST objects keep **exact** REST key sets (no `seq` inside nested objects) |\\n\\n**Non-durable / global:**\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"user.updated\\\", \\\"user\\\": { /* UserObj */ } }\\n```\\n\\nNo `channel_id`, no `seq`.\\n\\n### Durable event types (normative)\\n\\n| `type` | Extra fields | Emitted when (actual state change only) |\\n|--------|--------------|------------------------------------------|\\n| `message.created` | `message`: `MessageObj` | Successful message create (top-level or reply) |\\n| `message.updated` | `message`: `MessageObj` | Successful edit |\\n| `message.deleted` | `message_id`: string | Successful soft-delete |\\n| `reaction.changed` | `message_id`, `reactions`: `ReactionObj[]` | Successful add/remove reaction (full aggregate, same as REST) |\\n| `membership.joined` | `user`: `UserObj` | Channel membership row **inserted** (join, create-channel creator, DM ensure-membership that inserts) |\\n| `membership.left` | `user_id`: string | Channel membership row **deleted** (leave) |\\n| `channel.created` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Channel row created (workspace create-channel, DM create) |\\n| `channel.updated` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Topic PATCH that changes stored topic |\\n| `channel.archived` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Archive transition false→true |\\n| `channel.unarchived` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Unarchive true→false |\\n| `channel.pin_added` | `message_id`, `pinned_by`, `pinned_at` | New pin row inserted (not idempotent no-op) |\\n| `channel.pin_removed` | `message_id` | Pin row deleted (not idempotent no-op) |\\n\\nIdempotent HTTP no-ops (**must not** allocate seq / **must not** emit): join when already member; leave when not member; reaction already present/absent; pin already pinned; archive when already archived; topic PATCH with identical topic; profile PATCH with no field changes.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ WebSocket `GET /api/ws?token=\\u003craw-bearer\\u003e`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M17 / tools)** | Open `ws://127.0.0.1:800x/api/ws?token=\\u003ctoken\\u003e` (or `wss` if ever TLS). On open, `subscribe` each active channel; store last `seq` per channel; on reconnect `resume` with `since_seq`. While connecting/reconnecting: keep last REST snapshot; show reconnecting affordance (M17). Do not invent REST `seq`. |\\n| **Server** | Validate `token` **before** treating the socket as authenticated; maintain per-connection subscription set; enforce channel read authz on subscribe/resume; deliver frames; never crash the process on client disconnect. |\\n\\n**Handshake / auth**\\n\\n- Missing/empty/whitespace `token`, unknown token, or deleted user → **reject** the WebSocket with HTTP **401** during upgrade when the framework allows; otherwise `accept` then immediately close with code **4401** and reason `unauthorized`. Do not send application frames.\\n- Query param name is exactly **`token`** (not `access_token`). Extra query params ignored.\\n- Same token must work on any node (shared `auth_tokens` — already true).\\n\\n**Wire encoding:** one JSON object per WebSocket text message. Binary frames ignored (no error). Unknown client `type` → server sends:\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"error\\\", \\\"code\\\": \\\"validation_error\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"unknown type\\\" }\\n```\\n\\nand leaves subscriptions unchanged.\\n\\n#### Client → server: `subscribe`\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"subscribe\\\", \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid\\u003e\\\" }\\n```\\n\\n| Rule | Behavior |\\n|------|----------|\\n| Authz | Same as channel **message read** (MARATHON-8 `require_channel_message_read` / pin list matrix). Fail → `{type:\\\"error\\\", code:\\\"forbidden\\\"|\\\"not_found\\\", message}` — **do not** add subscription. Use `not_found` vs `forbidden` exactly as REST would for that channel. |\\n| Success | Add `channel_id` to connection set (idempotent if already subscribed). Reply **`subscribed`**. **No** historical replay. |\\n| `head_seq` | Current dense head for that channel (`0` if no events yet). |\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"subscribed\\\", \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid\\u003e\\\", \\\"head_seq\\\": 0 }\\n```\\n\\n#### Client → server: `resume`\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"resume\\\", \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid\\u003e\\\", \\\"since_seq\\\": 10 }\\n```\\n\\n| Rule | Behavior |\\n|------|----------|\\n| `since_seq` | Required integer; must be ≥ 0. Non-int / missing / negative → `error` `validation_error`. |\\n| Authz | Same as subscribe. |\\n| Subscription | On success path (including gap), connection **is** subscribed to `channel_id` (resume implies subscribe). |\\n| Let `head` = current head; `tail` = minimum retained seq for channel (`null` if `head==0`). |\\n| `head == 0` | Reply `{type:\\\"resumed\\\", channel_id, head_seq:0}` with no event frames. |\\n| `since_seq \\u003e head` | `{type:\\\"error\\\", code:\\\"validation_error\\\", message:\\\"since_seq ahead of head\\\"}`; **do not** change subscription if not already subscribed; if already subscribed, leave it. |\\n| `since_seq \\u003c tail` (retained) | Send **`resume.gap`** then **do not** replay; client must REST-reload. Still subscribed. |\\n| `tail ≤ since_seq ≤ head` | Send each stored event with `seq` in `(since_seq, head]` in ascending `seq` order, then **`resumed`**. |\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"resume.gap\\\", \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid\\u003e\\\", \\\"head_seq\\\": 50, \\\"tail_seq\\\": 20 }\\n```\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"resumed\\\", \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid\\u003e\\\", \\\"head_seq\\\": 50 }\\n```\\n\\n**Ordering on resume:** gap **or** replay frames, then `resumed`. Never interleave live frames for that channel between replay and `resumed` (buffer live until resume completes).\\n\\n#### Server → client: live delivery\\n\\n- After a connection is subscribed to `channel_id`, deliver every new durable frame for that channel (local hub).\\n- Deliver `user.updated` to **every** authenticated connection on the node (no subscribe required).\\n- Delivery after HTTP commit; at-most-once for a given connection under normal operation; clients use `seq` to detect gaps (reconnect + resume).\\n\\n#### Client slow / fail\\n\\n| Situation | Client | Server |\\n|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| WS connecting | Keep REST UI; disable optimistic “live only” assumptions | N/A |\\n| Subscribe error | Show channel unavailable; retry subscribe | Send `error` frame |\\n| `resume.gap` | Re-fetch channel history via REST; set local cursor to `head_seq`; continue live | Still subscribed |\\n| Socket drop | Reconnect with backoff; `resume` all channels with last seen seq | Drop connection state |\\n| Server backlog / slow client | May disconnect slow consumer | Prefer close rather than unbounded buffers (cap ~1000 pending frames then close 1008/1013) |\\n\\n### Seam: Backend mutation routes ↔ event core\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **HTTP route / store (existing modules)** | Inside the write transaction, after the durable row change succeeds, call `events.append_channel_event(conn, …)` (or typed helpers that wrap it). On idempotent no-op, skip. After **successful commit**, call `events.deliver(frame)` (and for profiles `deliver` of `user.updated`). |\\n| **`server/events.py` (+ hub)** | Allocate seq, insert log row, return frame; post-commit deliver to local subscribers; never raise from `deliver` after commit. |\\n\\n**Refactor of existing helpers** (signatures may add `conn` and return the frame):\\n\\n- `publish_message_created(conn, *, channel_id, message) -\\u003e dict`\\n- `publish_message_updated(conn, *, channel_id, message) -\\u003e dict`\\n- `publish_message_deleted(conn, *, channel_id, message_id) -\\u003e dict`\\n- `publish_reaction_changed(conn, *, channel_id, message_id, reactions) -\\u003e dict`\\n- `publish_user_updated(user) -\\u003e dict` — builds `{type:\\\"user.updated\\\", user}`; **no** conn/seq; caller delivers after commit.\\n\\nNew helpers (same pattern):\\n\\n- `publish_membership_joined(conn, *, channel_id, user)`\\n- `publish_membership_left(conn, *, channel_id, user_id)`\\n- `publish_channel_created/updated/archived/unarchived(conn, *, channel)`\\n- `publish_channel_pin_added/removed(conn, *, channel_id, …)`\\n\\nRoutes that must emit (when state changes): message create/edit/delete/react; channel join/leave/topic/archive/unarchive; pin/unpin; workspace create-channel; DM get-or-create when it **creates** a channel and/or **inserts** memberships; profile PATCH (global).\\n\\n### Seam: MARATHON-13 → MARATHON-14\\n\\n| Contract | M13 provides | M14 extends |\\n|----------|--------------|-------------|\\n| `events.deliver(frame)` | Local hub only | Also `PUBLISH` to Redis channel(s); subscribers on other nodes call local hub |\\n| Dense seq / `channel_events` | Complete | Must not re-allocate seq on receive; only forward frames |\\n| Redis down | Writes + seq continue (already true) | Live cross-node may lag; M14 owns ≤5s continuity story |\\n\\n### Seam: MARATHON-13 → MARATHON-15 (IRC)\\n\\nIRC PRIVMSG commits must call the **same** `append_channel_event` + message insert path so IRC and HTTP share one dense seq. M15 consumes this contract; M13 does not implement IRC.\\n\\n### Seam: MARATHON-13 → MARATHON-17 (SPA)\\n\\nWire protocol above is normative for the SPA realtime client. M17 owns UI reconnect UX and when to subscribe (active channel + maybe sidebar). M13 does **not** modify `static/js/*`.\\n\\n### Seam: MARATHON-11 `last_read_seq`\\n\\n`channel_read_state.last_read_seq` refers to this same dense per-channel seq. M11 must treat head/read cursors as these event seqs (not message ids). M13 does not implement read APIs.\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Migration **v6** (additive, backward compatible)\\n\\nNext version after M8’s v5. Do **not** renumber prior migrations.\\n\\n#### `channel_seq`\\n\\n```sql\\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS channel_seq (\\n  channel_id TEXT NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,\\n  head_seq INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0\\n    CHECK (head_seq \\u003e= 0),\\n  FOREIGN KEY (channel_id) REFERENCES channels(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\\n);\\n```\\n\\n- Row created lazily on first event for a channel (or optionally on channel create with `head_seq=0`).\\n- Allocate: in a transaction, `INSERT … head_seq=1` on miss, else `UPDATE channel_seq SET head_seq = head_seq + 1 WHERE channel_id=?`, then read `head_seq`. Use a single-statement pattern that cannot race across nodes (SQLite write lock serializes).\\n\\n#### `channel_events`\\n\\n```sql\\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS channel_events (\\n  channel_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\n  seq INTEGER NOT NULL,\\n  type TEXT NOT NULL,\\n  payload_json TEXT NOT NULL,\\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\\n  PRIMARY KEY (channel_id, seq),\\n  FOREIGN KEY (channel_id) REFERENCES channels(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\\n  CHECK (seq \\u003e= 1)\\n);\\n\\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_channel_events_channel_seq\\n  ON channel_events(channel_id, seq);\\n```\\n\\n- `payload_json`: JSON object of **extra** fields only (not duplicating `type`/`seq`/`channel_id`), e.g. `{\\\"message\\\":{…}}`. On read, merge into the wire frame.\\n- Deleting a channel cascades events (acceptable).\\n- **No** change to `messages`, `users`, or REST response shapes.\\n- Reverse migration: `DROP TABLE channel_events; DROP TABLE channel_seq;` + delete migration row (local verification only).\\n\\n### Constants\\n\\n| Name | Value | Meaning |\\n|------|-------|---------|\\n| `CHANNEL_EVENT_RETAIN` | `10000` | Max events kept per channel |\\n\\n### Nullability / types\\n\\n| Field | Type | Null |\\n|-------|------|------|\\n| `channel_seq.head_seq` | int | never |\\n| `channel_events.seq` | int | never |\\n| `channel_events.type` | text | never |\\n| `channel_events.payload_json` | text JSON object | never |\\n| `channel_events.created_at` | UTC `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ` | never |\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/ws/__init__.py` | Package marker / exports |\\n| `server/ws/hub.py` | Process-local connection registry: add/remove socket, subscribe set, `broadcast_channel(channel_id, frame)`, `broadcast_global(frame)`, slow-consumer policy |\\n| `server/ws/routes.py` | WebSocket `/api/ws` endpoint: auth, subscribe/resume/gap/replay, error frames |\\n| `server/events_store.py` **or** functions inside `server/events.py` | `append_channel_event`, head/tail queries, prune retention — prefer keeping store helpers next to events if small; split if file grows |\\n| `tests/test_ws.py` | Unit/integration tests for auth, subscribe, dense seq, resume, gap, user.updated, multi-channel |\\n\\n### Modify\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/db.py` | Add `_migrate_v6` / `_reverse_v6`; register version **6** |\\n| `server/events.py` | Replace no-ops with append+frame builders; add membership/channel/pin publishers; `deliver()` local hub (+ empty Redis hook for M14); document payload contracts |\\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` / mount WS routes |\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Emit events inside txn for join/leave/topic/archive/unarchive/pin paths; message create already publishes — move append **into** txn before commit; deliver after commit |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | Same for patch/delete/reactions/pins if pin routes live here |\\n| `server/users/routes.py` | After mutating PATCH commit, `deliver(publish_user_updated(user))` (build frame; hub broadcast) |\\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` | On create-channel success path: `channel.created` + `membership.joined` for creator |\\n| `server/dms/routes.py` / DM store (when present from M9) | On create: `channel.created` + `membership.joined` for each **new** membership insert |\\n| `server/auth/tokens.py` or small helper | `resolve_user_id` usable from WS query token (reuse existing) |\\n| `tests/test_messages.py` / `test_profiles.py` | Update spies/expectations if publish signatures gain `conn` / return frames; keep “no `seq` on MessageObj / user.updated” assertions |\\n\\n### Do not modify\\n\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `static/js/**` | SPA realtime client is MARATHON-17 |\\n| `start.sh` / Redis conf | Already boots Redis; M14 wires pub/sub |\\n| `timer.sh` | Harness |\\n| IRC | MARATHON-15 |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Build order (this task)\\n\\n1. Migration v6 (`channel_seq`, `channel_events`) + append/head/tail/prune helpers.\\n2. Hub + WS route + mount in `app.py`.\\n3. Wire message/reaction/profile publishers (existing call sites).\\n4. Wire membership/channel/pin/create publishers.\\n5. Tests: dense seq, subscribe/resume/gap, auth failures, cluster resume on second node (write on :8000, resume on :8001).\\n\\n### Parallelism\\n\\n- Hub/WS can be built in parallel with migration once frame schema is fixed (this design).\\n- Call-site wiring is sequential after helpers exist.\\n- Independent of SPA (M17) and IRC (M15) **implementations**, but both consume the contracts.\\n\\n### Cross-task seams\\n\\n| Contract | Owner | Consumer |\\n|----------|-------|----------|\\n| Dense `seq` + `channel_events` + append API | **MARATHON-13** | M14 fan-out, M15 IRC, M11 read_state, M17 SPA |\\n| WS subscribe/resume/gap wire protocol | **MARATHON-13** | M17 |\\n| `user.updated` shape | MARATHON-4 (shape) + **M13** (delivery) | M17 |\\n| Local `deliver` + Redis stub | **M13** | **M14** replaces stub with pub/sub |\\n| Message/Reaction/Channel/User REST objects | M7/M8/M4 | Nested inside frames unchanged |\\n| Cross-node live push / Redis outage | **MARATHON-14** | Graders, IRC multi-node |\\n| IRC PRIVMSG → same seq | **MARATHON-15** | Uses M13 append |\\n\\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\\n\\n- Redis pub/sub + outage path → MARATHON-14.\\n- IRC bridge → MARATHON-15.\\n- SPA WS client → MARATHON-17.\\n- Read-state advancement → MARATHON-11.\\n- Presence / typing indicators → not in epic realtime list; omit.\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\\n|------|----------------|--------------|\\n| Redis publish/subscribe + multi-node live push | `redis` package, hub subscribers | MARATHON-14 |\\n| Redis SIGKILL ≤5s continuity | fan-out resilience | MARATHON-14 |\\n| IRC `:6667` PRIVMSG/JOIN bridge | future IRC module | MARATHON-15 |\\n| SPA WebSocket client / reconnect UI | `static/js/*` | MARATHON-17 |\\n| `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` | read_state routes | MARATHON-11 (consumes seq) |\\n| Search / slash / advanced mentions | messages routes | MARATHON-11 |\\n| File upload events | files API | MARATHON-10 (when files mutate channel state, emit via same append helper in that task or follow-up) |\\n| Workspace invitation / group membership WS events | invitations/groups | Not in M13 task list; omit unless they mutate a **channel** |\\n| Adding `seq` to REST `MessageObj` | messages store | Forbidden by M8 |\\n| Changing `CHANNEL_EVENT_RETAIN` dynamically | settings | Constant is enough |\\n\\n**Neighborhood scan account**\\n\\n| Hit | Disposition |\\n|-----|-------------|\\n| `server/events.py` no-op publishers | **In scope** — implement |\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` `publish_message_created` after commit | **In scope** — move append into txn; deliver after |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` publish_* | **In scope** |\\n| `server/users/routes.py` `publish_user_updated` | **In scope** — deliver globally |\\n| `server/db.py` `last_read_seq` column | **Unchanged** — semantic alignment documented for M11 |\\n| `server/channels/store.py` read_state embed | **Out of scope** — M11 |\\n| `tests/test_profiles.py` / `test_messages.py` “no seq” / publish spies | **In scope** — adjust to new signatures; keep no-seq-on-REST |\\n| `static/js/api.js` fetch-only client | **Out of scope** — M17 |\\n| `requirements.txt` `redis` already present | **Out of scope** for logic; M14 uses it |\\n| No existing `/api/ws` | Greenfield WS module |\\n| MARATHON-7/8/9 notes reserving WS for M13/14 | Honored |\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\\n|-----------|-------------------|\\n| WS without `token` | Reject 401 / close 4401; no frames |\\n| Invalid token | Same |\\n| Subscribe unknown channel id | `error` `not_found` |\\n| Subscribe private channel as non-member | `error` `forbidden` (workspace member) or `not_found` (stranger) — match REST |\\n| Subscribe public as non-workspace-member | `error` `not_found` |\\n| Double subscribe | Second `subscribed` ack; still one subscription entry |\\n| Resume with `since_seq == head` | `resumed` only; no event frames |\\n| Resume with `since_seq == head - 1` | One event then `resumed` |\\n| Resume when pruned (`since_seq \\u003c tail`) | `resume.gap` with `tail_seq`/`head_seq`; no partial replay |\\n| Empty channel (`head=0`) resume | `resumed` with `head_seq:0` |\\n| Mutation rolls back after append attempted | Entire txn rolls back including seq bump — **no** gap (append must share txn) |\\n| `deliver` raises / hub error | Log; **must not** fail the HTTP response after commit |\\n| Client sends non-JSON | `error` `validation_error` |\\n| Client sends binary | Ignore |\\n| Slow client | Close connection when outbound buffer exceeds cap |\\n| Channel deleted while subscribed | Stop delivering; optional `error` `not_found` on next resume; cascade deletes event rows |\\n| Concurrent writes two nodes | SQLite serializes; seq remains dense |\\n| Idempotent join | HTTP 200; **no** event |\\n| Soft-deleted message react | HTTP 409; **no** event |\\n| Archived channel message post | HTTP 423; **no** event |\\n| Profile PATCH no-op | No `user.updated` |\\n| Token revoked mid-connection | Best-effort: next messages may continue until disconnect; optional periodic re-resolve — **not required**; do not force complexity. New connections must fail auth. |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `ws://127.0.0.1:8000/api/ws?token=\\u003cvalid\\u003e` upgrades successfully; invalid/missing token does **not** yield an authenticated session.\\n2. After `subscribe` to a channel the caller can read, server replies `subscribed` with correct `head_seq`.\\n3. Posting a message (REST) on the **same node** as the WS connection delivers exactly one `message.created` frame with `seq == previous_head + 1`, matching nested `MessageObj` keys (no `seq` inside `message`).\\n4. A thread reply also emits `message.created` (with `parent_id` set), consuming the next dense seq.\\n5. Edit / delete / reaction emit `message.updated` / `message.deleted` / `reaction.changed` with dense seq and required fields.\\n6. Join/leave that change membership emit `membership.joined` / `membership.left`; idempotent join/leave emit **nothing**.\\n7. Topic/archive/unarchive/pin mutations emit the corresponding `channel.*` frames only on actual change.\\n8. N durable events in one channel produce seqs `1…N` with **no gaps/duplicates** when read from `channel_events` or via resume.\\n9. `resume` with `since_seq = k` (retained) replays `k+1…head` in order then `resumed`.\\n10. After pruning (or with `since_seq` below tail), server sends `resume.gap` and does **not** send a partial replay.\\n11. `PATCH /api/users/me` that changes a field delivers `{type:\\\"user.updated\\\", user}` to the WS client **without** `channel_id`/`seq`.\\n12. Write message on `:8000`, open WS on `:8001`, `resume` with `since_seq=0` → receives the event(s) from SQLite (cross-node **catch-up** works without M14).\\n13. **Negative:** REST `MessageObj` / `UserObj` responses still must **not** include `seq`.\\n14. **Negative:** must **not** require Redis for subscribe/resume/seq allocation (Redis may be unused).\\n15. **Negative:** must **not** implement Redis fan-out or IRC in this task.\\n16. Unauthorized subscribe returns an `error` frame and does **not** attach the subscription.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Automated (`tests/test_ws.py` + adjustments)\\n\\n- Auth reject paths (no token, bad token).\\n- Subscribe happy path + forbidden/not_found.\\n- Dense seq: create 3 messages → seqs 1,2,3; resume from 1 → events 2,3 + resumed.\\n- Gap: insert \\u003e`CHANNEL_EVENT_RETAIN` events (or temporarily lower retain in test) → resume from 0 → `resume.gap`.\\n- Reaction / delete / membership / channel.updated smoke.\\n- `user.updated` global delivery.\\n- Cross-node resume: two `create_app` sharing temp sqlite (pattern from auth cluster tests) — write via app A, resume via WS on app B.\\n- Keep `tests/test_messages.py` assertion: `\\\"seq\\\" not in msg`.\\n- Keep profiles test: published user.updated has no seq/channel_id.\\n\\n### Manual / cluster\\n\\n1. Boot `./start.sh`.\\n2. Register/login; create workspace/channel; open websocat/wscat to `:8000/api/ws?token=…`.\\n3. `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"subscribe\\\",\\\"channel_id\\\":\\\"…\\\"}` → note `head_seq`.\\n4. POST a message via curl; observe `message.created` with `seq`.\\n5. Kill WS; reconnect to `:8001`; `resume` with last seq → catch-up.\\n6. PATCH profile; observe `user.updated` on an open socket.\\n\\n### Out of test scope here\\n\\n- Redis down behavior (M14).\\n- IRC parity (M15).\\n- SPA selectors (M17).\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"Design complete for WS subscribe/resume + dense channel seq. Key decisions: SQLite channel_seq/channel_events (v6) as SoT; seq allocated in same txn as mutation; /api/ws?token=; subscribe=live only, resume=replay or resume.gap; user.updated global no seq; Redis fan-out deferred to MARATHON-14 (local hub + catch-up on any node via resume). Label remains backend for implementer after architect approval.\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:29.968254993Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-23T01:31:46.235451662Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"ws://host/api/ws?token= bearer. Client: subscribe, resume with since_seq. Server: subscribed/resumed with head_seq; resume.gap if since_seq older than retained tail. Durable per-channel frames {type, seq, channel_id, ...} for message/reply/reaction/membership/channel mutations. seq dense per-channel (+1 per durable event, no gaps/duplicates). Profile updates: {type:user.updated,user} globally without channel_id/seq. Same seq visible across all HTTP nodes (fan-out task will complete cross-node).\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-14\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-13\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Cross-node fan-out and Redis-outage resilience\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:29.991315274Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-15\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-13\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"IRC gateway on :6667 with bidirectional bridge\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:47.161Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 57,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-13\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"DESIGN-AUTO-APPROVED pass=29\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T01:31:46.291233893Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n/work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1\ntotal 40\ndrwxr-xr-x.  9 root root 4096 Aug 23 01:32 .\ndrwxr-xr-x.  6 root root   93 Aug 22 22:15 ..\n-rw-------.  1 root root  265 Aug 23 01:32 .agent.lock\n-rw-------.  1 root root    0 Aug 22 22:23 .agent.lock.flock\n-rw-r--r--.  1 root root   42 Aug 22 22:15 .git\n-rw-r--r--.  1 root root  229 Aug 22 22:24 .gitignore\ndrwx------.  3 root root   70 Aug 22 22:25 .pytest_cache\ndrwx------.  5 root root  101 Aug 22 22:27 .venv\ndrwx------.  5 root root   64 Aug 23 01:16 data\ndrwxr-xr-x.  2 root root   33 Aug 22 22:15 loom-prompts\n-rw-------.  1 root root  119 Aug 22 22:23 requirements.txt\ndrwx------. 11 root root 4096 Aug 23 01:00 server\n-rwx------.  1 root root 4973 Aug 22 22:27 start.sh\ndrwx------.  4 root root   45 Aug 23 01:15 static\ndrwx------.  3 root root 4096 Aug 23 01:15 tests\n-rwxr-xr-x.  1 root root  558 Aug 22 22:15 timer.sh\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T01:32:15.861Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":377,"interleavedOutput":"Already up to date.\ntime=2026-08-23T01:32:15.861Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-13\",\n  \"title\": \"WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"priority\": 0,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"assignee\": \"backend-dev-1\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"backend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-13 — WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task adds the real-time seam for Huddle: an authenticated WebSocket at `GET /api/ws?token=…`, client `subscribe` / `resume` control frames, and a **dense per-channel `seq`** assigned in shared SQLite so every durable channel mutation (messages including thread replies, reactions, membership, channel mutations, pins) gets a gap-free monotonic frame `{type, seq, channel_id, …}`. Profile changes keep the existing channel-less `user.updated` shape (no `seq`). Same `seq` / event rows are visible from every HTTP node via the shared DB; **live cross-node push** remains MARATHON-14 (this task delivers live frames to connections on the writing node and makes catch-up via `resume` work on any node).\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Seq SoT | **Shared SQLite** counters + durable `channel_events` log (not Redis). Allocation is in the **same transaction** as the HTTP mutation so rollbacks never burn a seq. |\\n| Dense rule | Per `channel_id`, `seq` starts at **0** (empty) and first durable event is **1**, then `+1` per committed durable event. No gaps, no duplicates, no reuse. |\\n| WS transport | FastAPI/Starlette WebSocket on **`/api/ws`**, auth via query `token` (raw bearer, same value as `Authorization: Bearer`). |\\n| Control protocol | Client JSON: `subscribe`, `resume` (with `since_seq`). Server JSON: `subscribed`, `resumed`, `resume.gap`, plus durable/live event frames and `user.updated`. |\\n| History vs live | `subscribe` = watch from **now** (ack `head_seq`, no backlog). `resume` = authorize + **replay** `(since_seq+1)…head` then live, or `resume.gap` if `since_seq` is older than the retained tail. Channel history UI still uses REST (MARATHON-8). |\\n| Retention | Keep the last **`CHANNEL_EVENT_RETAIN = 10_000`** events per channel (constant in code). After append, prune `seq \\u003c head_seq - RETAIN + 1`. Tail = minimum retained `seq` (or `1` if none pruned yet / empty head). |\\n| Local delivery | Process-local **connection hub** on each node. `emit` records to SQLite; **after commit** `deliver(frame)` fans to local WS subscribers. Redis publish is a **no-op stub hook** owned by MARATHON-14. |\\n| Cross-node live | **Out of scope** (MARATHON-14). Reconnect-to-other-node **replay** works in this task because resume reads SQLite. |\\n| REST objects | **Do not** add `seq` to `MessageObj` / `ChannelObj` / `UserObj` (MARATHON-8/4 locks). |\\n| Thread replies | Same frame type `message.created`; “reply” is `message.parent_id != null` inside the nested `MessageObj` (no separate `reply.*` type). |\\n| Publish call sites | Refactor existing post-commit `publish_*` so **seq append happens inside the open write transaction**; hub deliver stays post-commit and must not raise. |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- Epic + MARATHON-2 forbid Redis as SoT (Redis `SIGKILL` must not break dense seq). Shared SQLite is already the cluster SoT.\\n- MARATHON-8/4 already froze event *shapes* and “seq on WS frames only”; this task completes transport + numbering without reopening REST contracts.\\n- Separating local hub (M13) from Redis fan-out (M14) lets IRC/SPA resume against any node immediately while M14 finishes cluster push and outage behavior.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| Redis `INCR` for seq | Breaks dense continuity during Redis outage (epic / M14) |\\n| Seq on `MessageObj` | Explicitly rejected in MARATHON-8 |\\n| Only in-memory events (no `channel_events`) | Cannot resume after reconnect / other node; violates epic replay |\\n| Separate `reply.*` frame types | Task wording lists “reply” as a durable class; existing hooks + MessageObj already encode replies via `parent_id` |\\n| Cookie/`Authorization` header-only WS auth | Browsers cannot set arbitrary WS headers; task specifies `?token=` |\\n| Implement Redis pub/sub in this task | Owned by MARATHON-14; stub only |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\nRetention is finite (`10_000` events/channel). Clients that disconnect longer than the retained window get `resume.gap` and must reload via REST — acceptable for the marathon cluster and keeps SQLite bounded. Live multi-node push waits for M14; until then a client subscribed only on node B will not see live frames for writes on node A until it `resume`s (or reconnects).\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\n- **MARATHON-2:** SQLite SoT; Redis ephemeral; `HUDDLE_REDIS_URL` present but unused for durability here.\\n- **MARATHON-3:** Bearer opaque tokens in SQLite; UUID4 ids; `{error:{code,message}}` for HTTP (WS uses JSON control/error frames, not HTTP envelopes after upgrade).\\n- **MARATHON-4:** `user.updated` = `{type,user}` with **no** `channel_id`/`seq`; `UserObj` keys unchanged.\\n- **MARATHON-7/8:** Channel read/write authz matrices; `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` / `ChannelObj` key sets; soft-delete semantics; archived → HTTP 423 (no WS event for rejected writes).\\n- **MARATHON-8:** No-op publish hooks become real emitters; docstring payload shapes stay the source of truth and gain `seq` where applicable.\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Shared: durable channel frame envelope\\n\\nEvery durable per-channel frame **must** include:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"\\u003cevent-type\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"seq\\\": 42,\\n  \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid\\u003e\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n| Field | Rules |\\n|-------|--------|\\n| `type` | string; one of the durable types below |\\n| `seq` | integer ≥ 1; dense per `channel_id` |\\n| `channel_id` | string; never null on durable frames |\\n| Extra fields | Per type; nested REST objects keep **exact** REST key sets (no `seq` inside nested objects) |\\n\\n**Non-durable / global:**\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"user.updated\\\", \\\"user\\\": { /* UserObj */ } }\\n```\\n\\nNo `channel_id`, no `seq`.\\n\\n### Durable event types (normative)\\n\\n| `type` | Extra fields | Emitted when (actual state change only) |\\n|--------|--------------|------------------------------------------|\\n| `message.created` | `message`: `MessageObj` | Successful message create (top-level or reply) |\\n| `message.updated` | `message`: `MessageObj` | Successful edit |\\n| `message.deleted` | `message_id`: string | Successful soft-delete |\\n| `reaction.changed` | `message_id`, `reactions`: `ReactionObj[]` | Successful add/remove reaction (full aggregate, same as REST) |\\n| `membership.joined` | `user`: `UserObj` | Channel membership row **inserted** (join, create-channel creator, DM ensure-membership that inserts) |\\n| `membership.left` | `user_id`: string | Channel membership row **deleted** (leave) |\\n| `channel.created` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Channel row created (workspace create-channel, DM create) |\\n| `channel.updated` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Topic PATCH that changes stored topic |\\n| `channel.archived` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Archive transition false→true |\\n| `channel.unarchived` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Unarchive true→false |\\n| `channel.pin_added` | `message_id`, `pinned_by`, `pinned_at` | New pin row inserted (not idempotent no-op) |\\n| `channel.pin_removed` | `message_id` | Pin row deleted (not idempotent no-op) |\\n\\nIdempotent HTTP no-ops (**must not** allocate seq / **must not** emit): join when already member; leave when not member; reaction already present/absent; pin already pinned; archive when already archived; topic PATCH with identical topic; profile PATCH with no field changes.\\n\\n### Seam: Client ↔ WebSocket `GET /api/ws?token=\\u003craw-bearer\\u003e`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client (SPA M17 / tools)** | Open `ws://127.0.0.1:800x/api/ws?token=\\u003ctoken\\u003e` (or `wss` if ever TLS). On open, `subscribe` each active channel; store last `seq` per channel; on reconnect `resume` with `since_seq`. While connecting/reconnecting: keep last REST snapshot; show reconnecting affordance (M17). Do not invent REST `seq`. |\\n| **Server** | Validate `token` **before** treating the socket as authenticated; maintain per-connection subscription set; enforce channel read authz on subscribe/resume; deliver frames; never crash the process on client disconnect. |\\n\\n**Handshake / auth**\\n\\n- Missing/empty/whitespace `token`, unknown token, or deleted user → **reject** the WebSocket with HTTP **401** during upgrade when the framework allows; otherwise `accept` then immediately close with code **4401** and reason `unauthorized`. Do not send application frames.\\n- Query param name is exactly **`token`** (not `access_token`). Extra query params ignored.\\n- Same token must work on any node (shared `auth_tokens` — already true).\\n\\n**Wire encoding:** one JSON object per WebSocket text message. Binary frames ignored (no error). Unknown client `type` → server sends:\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"error\\\", \\\"code\\\": \\\"validation_error\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"unknown type\\\" }\\n```\\n\\nand leaves subscriptions unchanged.\\n\\n#### Client → server: `subscribe`\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"subscribe\\\", \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid\\u003e\\\" }\\n```\\n\\n| Rule | Behavior |\\n|------|----------|\\n| Authz | Same as channel **message read** (MARATHON-8 `require_channel_message_read` / pin list matrix). Fail → `{type:\\\"error\\\", code:\\\"forbidden\\\"|\\\"not_found\\\", message}` — **do not** add subscription. Use `not_found` vs `forbidden` exactly as REST would for that channel. |\\n| Success | Add `channel_id` to connection set (idempotent if already subscribed). Reply **`subscribed`**. **No** historical replay. |\\n| `head_seq` | Current dense head for that channel (`0` if no events yet). |\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"subscribed\\\", \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid\\u003e\\\", \\\"head_seq\\\": 0 }\\n```\\n\\n#### Client → server: `resume`\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"resume\\\", \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid\\u003e\\\", \\\"since_seq\\\": 10 }\\n```\\n\\n| Rule | Behavior |\\n|------|----------|\\n| `since_seq` | Required integer; must be ≥ 0. Non-int / missing / negative → `error` `validation_error`. |\\n| Authz | Same as subscribe. |\\n| Subscription | On success path (including gap), connection **is** subscribed to `channel_id` (resume implies subscribe). |\\n| Let `head` = current head; `tail` = minimum retained seq for channel (`null` if `head==0`). |\\n| `head == 0` | Reply `{type:\\\"resumed\\\", channel_id, head_seq:0}` with no event frames. |\\n| `since_seq \\u003e head` | `{type:\\\"error\\\", code:\\\"validation_error\\\", message:\\\"since_seq ahead of head\\\"}`; **do not** change subscription if not already subscribed; if already subscribed, leave it. |\\n| `since_seq \\u003c tail` (retained) | Send **`resume.gap`** then **do not** replay; client must REST-reload. Still subscribed. |\\n| `tail ≤ since_seq ≤ head` | Send each stored event with `seq` in `(since_seq, head]` in ascending `seq` order, then **`resumed`**. |\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"resume.gap\\\", \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid\\u003e\\\", \\\"head_seq\\\": 50, \\\"tail_seq\\\": 20 }\\n```\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"type\\\": \\\"resumed\\\", \\\"channel_id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid\\u003e\\\", \\\"head_seq\\\": 50 }\\n```\\n\\n**Ordering on resume:** gap **or** replay frames, then `resumed`. Never interleave live frames for that channel between replay and `resumed` (buffer live until resume completes).\\n\\n#### Server → client: live delivery\\n\\n- After a connection is subscribed to `channel_id`, deliver every new durable frame for that channel (local hub).\\n- Deliver `user.updated` to **every** authenticated connection on the node (no subscribe required).\\n- Delivery after HTTP commit; at-most-once for a given connection under normal operation; clients use `seq` to detect gaps (reconnect + resume).\\n\\n#### Client slow / fail\\n\\n| Situation | Client | Server |\\n|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| WS connecting | Keep REST UI; disable optimistic “live only” assumptions | N/A |\\n| Subscribe error | Show channel unavailable; retry subscribe | Send `error` frame |\\n| `resume.gap` | Re-fetch channel history via REST; set local cursor to `head_seq`; continue live | Still subscribed |\\n| Socket drop | Reconnect with backoff; `resume` all channels with last seen seq | Drop connection state |\\n| Server backlog / slow client | May disconnect slow consumer | Prefer close rather than unbounded buffers (cap ~1000 pending frames then close 1008/1013) |\\n\\n### Seam: Backend mutation routes ↔ event core\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **HTTP route / store (existing modules)** | Inside the write transaction, after the durable row change succeeds, call `events.append_channel_event(conn, …)` (or typed helpers that wrap it). On idempotent no-op, skip. After **successful commit**, call `events.deliver(frame)` (and for profiles `deliver` of `user.updated`). |\\n| **`server/events.py` (+ hub)** | Allocate seq, insert log row, return frame; post-commit deliver to local subscribers; never raise from `deliver` after commit. |\\n\\n**Refactor of existing helpers** (signatures may add `conn` and return the frame):\\n\\n- `publish_message_created(conn, *, channel_id, message) -\\u003e dict`\\n- `publish_message_updated(conn, *, channel_id, message) -\\u003e dict`\\n- `publish_message_deleted(conn, *, channel_id, message_id) -\\u003e dict`\\n- `publish_reaction_changed(conn, *, channel_id, message_id, reactions) -\\u003e dict`\\n- `publish_user_updated(user) -\\u003e dict` — builds `{type:\\\"user.updated\\\", user}`; **no** conn/seq; caller delivers after commit.\\n\\nNew helpers (same pattern):\\n\\n- `publish_membership_joined(conn, *, channel_id, user)`\\n- `publish_membership_left(conn, *, channel_id, user_id)`\\n- `publish_channel_created/updated/archived/unarchived(conn, *, channel)`\\n- `publish_channel_pin_added/removed(conn, *, channel_id, …)`\\n\\nRoutes that must emit (when state changes): message create/edit/delete/react; channel join/leave/topic/archive/unarchive; pin/unpin; workspace create-channel; DM get-or-create when it **creates** a channel and/or **inserts** memberships; profile PATCH (global).\\n\\n### Seam: MARATHON-13 → MARATHON-14\\n\\n| Contract | M13 provides | M14 extends |\\n|----------|--------------|-------------|\\n| `events.deliver(frame)` | Local hub only | Also `PUBLISH` to Redis channel(s); subscribers on other nodes call local hub |\\n| Dense seq / `channel_events` | Complete | Must not re-allocate seq on receive; only forward frames |\\n| Redis down | Writes + seq continue (already true) | Live cross-node may lag; M14 owns ≤5s continuity story |\\n\\n### Seam: MARATHON-13 → MARATHON-15 (IRC)\\n\\nIRC PRIVMSG commits must call the **same** `append_channel_event` + message insert path so IRC and HTTP share one dense seq. M15 consumes this contract; M13 does not implement IRC.\\n\\n### Seam: MARATHON-13 → MARATHON-17 (SPA)\\n\\nWire protocol above is normative for the SPA realtime client. M17 owns UI reconnect UX and when to subscribe (active channel + maybe sidebar). M13 does **not** modify `static/js/*`.\\n\\n### Seam: MARATHON-11 `last_read_seq`\\n\\n`channel_read_state.last_read_seq` refers to this same dense per-channel seq. M11 must treat head/read cursors as these event seqs (not message ids). M13 does not implement read APIs.\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Migration **v6** (additive, backward compatible)\\n\\nNext version after M8’s v5. Do **not** renumber prior migrations.\\n\\n#### `channel_seq`\\n\\n```sql\\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS channel_seq (\\n  channel_id TEXT NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,\\n  head_seq INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0\\n    CHECK (head_seq \\u003e= 0),\\n  FOREIGN KEY (channel_id) REFERENCES channels(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\\n);\\n```\\n\\n- Row created lazily on first event for a channel (or optionally on channel create with `head_seq=0`).\\n- Allocate: in a transaction, `INSERT … head_seq=1` on miss, else `UPDATE channel_seq SET head_seq = head_seq + 1 WHERE channel_id=?`, then read `head_seq`. Use a single-statement pattern that cannot race across nodes (SQLite write lock serializes).\\n\\n#### `channel_events`\\n\\n```sql\\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS channel_events (\\n  channel_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\n  seq INTEGER NOT NULL,\\n  type TEXT NOT NULL,\\n  payload_json TEXT NOT NULL,\\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\\n  PRIMARY KEY (channel_id, seq),\\n  FOREIGN KEY (channel_id) REFERENCES channels(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\\n  CHECK (seq \\u003e= 1)\\n);\\n\\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_channel_events_channel_seq\\n  ON channel_events(channel_id, seq);\\n```\\n\\n- `payload_json`: JSON object of **extra** fields only (not duplicating `type`/`seq`/`channel_id`), e.g. `{\\\"message\\\":{…}}`. On read, merge into the wire frame.\\n- Deleting a channel cascades events (acceptable).\\n- **No** change to `messages`, `users`, or REST response shapes.\\n- Reverse migration: `DROP TABLE channel_events; DROP TABLE channel_seq;` + delete migration row (local verification only).\\n\\n### Constants\\n\\n| Name | Value | Meaning |\\n|------|-------|---------|\\n| `CHANNEL_EVENT_RETAIN` | `10000` | Max events kept per channel |\\n\\n### Nullability / types\\n\\n| Field | Type | Null |\\n|-------|------|------|\\n| `channel_seq.head_seq` | int | never |\\n| `channel_events.seq` | int | never |\\n| `channel_events.type` | text | never |\\n| `channel_events.payload_json` | text JSON object | never |\\n| `channel_events.created_at` | UTC `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ` | never |\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/ws/__init__.py` | Package marker / exports |\\n| `server/ws/hub.py` | Process-local connection registry: add/remove socket, subscribe set, `broadcast_channel(channel_id, frame)`, `broadcast_global(frame)`, slow-consumer policy |\\n| `server/ws/routes.py` | WebSocket `/api/ws` endpoint: auth, subscribe/resume/gap/replay, error frames |\\n| `server/events_store.py` **or** functions inside `server/events.py` | `append_channel_event`, head/tail queries, prune retention — prefer keeping store helpers next to events if small; split if file grows |\\n| `tests/test_ws.py` | Unit/integration tests for auth, subscribe, dense seq, resume, gap, user.updated, multi-channel |\\n\\n### Modify\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/db.py` | Add `_migrate_v6` / `_reverse_v6`; register version **6** |\\n| `server/events.py` | Replace no-ops with append+frame builders; add membership/channel/pin publishers; `deliver()` local hub (+ empty Redis hook for M14); document payload contracts |\\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` / mount WS routes |\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Emit events inside txn for join/leave/topic/archive/unarchive/pin paths; message create already publishes — move append **into** txn before commit; deliver after commit |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | Same for patch/delete/reactions/pins if pin routes live here |\\n| `server/users/routes.py` | After mutating PATCH commit, `deliver(publish_user_updated(user))` (build frame; hub broadcast) |\\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` | On create-channel success path: `channel.created` + `membership.joined` for creator |\\n| `server/dms/routes.py` / DM store (when present from M9) | On create: `channel.created` + `membership.joined` for each **new** membership insert |\\n| `server/auth/tokens.py` or small helper | `resolve_user_id` usable from WS query token (reuse existing) |\\n| `tests/test_messages.py` / `test_profiles.py` | Update spies/expectations if publish signatures gain `conn` / return frames; keep “no `seq` on MessageObj / user.updated” assertions |\\n\\n### Do not modify\\n\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `static/js/**` | SPA realtime client is MARATHON-17 |\\n| `start.sh` / Redis conf | Already boots Redis; M14 wires pub/sub |\\n| `timer.sh` | Harness |\\n| IRC | MARATHON-15 |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Build order (this task)\\n\\n1. Migration v6 (`channel_seq`, `channel_events`) + append/head/tail/prune helpers.\\n2. Hub + WS route + mount in `app.py`.\\n3. Wire message/reaction/profile publishers (existing call sites).\\n4. Wire membership/channel/pin/create publishers.\\n5. Tests: dense seq, subscribe/resume/gap, auth failures, cluster resume on second node (write on :8000, resume on :8001).\\n\\n### Parallelism\\n\\n- Hub/WS can be built in parallel with migration once frame schema is fixed (this design).\\n- Call-site wiring is sequential after helpers exist.\\n- Independent of SPA (M17) and IRC (M15) **implementations**, but both consume the contracts.\\n\\n### Cross-task seams\\n\\n| Contract | Owner | Consumer |\\n|----------|-------|----------|\\n| Dense `seq` + `channel_events` + append API | **MARATHON-13** | M14 fan-out, M15 IRC, M11 read_state, M17 SPA |\\n| WS subscribe/resume/gap wire protocol | **MARATHON-13** | M17 |\\n| `user.updated` shape | MARATHON-4 (shape) + **M13** (delivery) | M17 |\\n| Local `deliver` + Redis stub | **M13** | **M14** replaces stub with pub/sub |\\n| Message/Reaction/Channel/User REST objects | M7/M8/M4 | Nested inside frames unchanged |\\n| Cross-node live push / Redis outage | **MARATHON-14** | Graders, IRC multi-node |\\n| IRC PRIVMSG → same seq | **MARATHON-15** | Uses M13 append |\\n\\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\\n\\n- Redis pub/sub + outage path → MARATHON-14.\\n- IRC bridge → MARATHON-15.\\n- SPA WS client → MARATHON-17.\\n- Read-state advancement → MARATHON-11.\\n- Presence / typing indicators → not in epic realtime list; omit.\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\\n|------|----------------|--------------|\\n| Redis publish/subscribe + multi-node live push | `redis` package, hub subscribers | MARATHON-14 |\\n| Redis SIGKILL ≤5s continuity | fan-out resilience | MARATHON-14 |\\n| IRC `:6667` PRIVMSG/JOIN bridge | future IRC module | MARATHON-15 |\\n| SPA WebSocket client / reconnect UI | `static/js/*` | MARATHON-17 |\\n| `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` | read_state routes | MARATHON-11 (consumes seq) |\\n| Search / slash / advanced mentions | messages routes | MARATHON-11 |\\n| File upload events | files API | MARATHON-10 (when files mutate channel state, emit via same append helper in that task or follow-up) |\\n| Workspace invitation / group membership WS events | invitations/groups | Not in M13 task list; omit unless they mutate a **channel** |\\n| Adding `seq` to REST `MessageObj` | messages store | Forbidden by M8 |\\n| Changing `CHANNEL_EVENT_RETAIN` dynamically | settings | Constant is enough |\\n\\n**Neighborhood scan account**\\n\\n| Hit | Disposition |\\n|-----|-------------|\\n| `server/events.py` no-op publishers | **In scope** — implement |\\n| `server/channels/routes.py` `publish_message_created` after commit | **In scope** — move append into txn; deliver after |\\n| `server/messages/routes.py` publish_* | **In scope** |\\n| `server/users/routes.py` `publish_user_updated` | **In scope** — deliver globally |\\n| `server/db.py` `last_read_seq` column | **Unchanged** — semantic alignment documented for M11 |\\n| `server/channels/store.py` read_state embed | **Out of scope** — M11 |\\n| `tests/test_profiles.py` / `test_messages.py` “no seq” / publish spies | **In scope** — adjust to new signatures; keep no-seq-on-REST |\\n| `static/js/api.js` fetch-only client | **Out of scope** — M17 |\\n| `requirements.txt` `redis` already present | **Out of scope** for logic; M14 uses it |\\n| No existing `/api/ws` | Greenfield WS module |\\n| MARATHON-7/8/9 notes reserving WS for M13/14 | Honored |\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\\n|-----------|-------------------|\\n| WS without `token` | Reject 401 / close 4401; no frames |\\n| Invalid token | Same |\\n| Subscribe unknown channel id | `error` `not_found` |\\n| Subscribe private channel as non-member | `error` `forbidden` (workspace member) or `not_found` (stranger) — match REST |\\n| Subscribe public as non-workspace-member | `error` `not_found` |\\n| Double subscribe | Second `subscribed` ack; still one subscription entry |\\n| Resume with `since_seq == head` | `resumed` only; no event frames |\\n| Resume with `since_seq == head - 1` | One event then `resumed` |\\n| Resume when pruned (`since_seq \\u003c tail`) | `resume.gap` with `tail_seq`/`head_seq`; no partial replay |\\n| Empty channel (`head=0`) resume | `resumed` with `head_seq:0` |\\n| Mutation rolls back after append attempted | Entire txn rolls back including seq bump — **no** gap (append must share txn) |\\n| `deliver` raises / hub error | Log; **must not** fail the HTTP response after commit |\\n| Client sends non-JSON | `error` `validation_error` |\\n| Client sends binary | Ignore |\\n| Slow client | Close connection when outbound buffer exceeds cap |\\n| Channel deleted while subscribed | Stop delivering; optional `error` `not_found` on next resume; cascade deletes event rows |\\n| Concurrent writes two nodes | SQLite serializes; seq remains dense |\\n| Idempotent join | HTTP 200; **no** event |\\n| Soft-deleted message react | HTTP 409; **no** event |\\n| Archived channel message post | HTTP 423; **no** event |\\n| Profile PATCH no-op | No `user.updated` |\\n| Token revoked mid-connection | Best-effort: next messages may continue until disconnect; optional periodic re-resolve — **not required**; do not force complexity. New connections must fail auth. |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `ws://127.0.0.1:8000/api/ws?token=\\u003cvalid\\u003e` upgrades successfully; invalid/missing token does **not** yield an authenticated session.\\n2. After `subscribe` to a channel the caller can read, server replies `subscribed` with correct `head_seq`.\\n3. Posting a message (REST) on the **same node** as the WS connection delivers exactly one `message.created` frame with `seq == previous_head + 1`, matching nested `MessageObj` keys (no `seq` inside `message`).\\n4. A thread reply also emits `message.created` (with `parent_id` set), consuming the next dense seq.\\n5. Edit / delete / reaction emit `message.updated` / `message.deleted` / `reaction.changed` with dense seq and required fields.\\n6. Join/leave that change membership emit `membership.joined` / `membership.left`; idempotent join/leave emit **nothing**.\\n7. Topic/archive/unarchive/pin mutations emit the corresponding `channel.*` frames only on actual change.\\n8. N durable events in one channel produce seqs `1…N` with **no gaps/duplicates** when read from `channel_events` or via resume.\\n9. `resume` with `since_seq = k` (retained) replays `k+1…head` in order then `resumed`.\\n10. After pruning (or with `since_seq` below tail), server sends `resume.gap` and does **not** send a partial replay.\\n11. `PATCH /api/users/me` that changes a field delivers `{type:\\\"user.updated\\\", user}` to the WS client **without** `channel_id`/`seq`.\\n12. Write message on `:8000`, open WS on `:8001`, `resume` with `since_seq=0` → receives the event(s) from SQLite (cross-node **catch-up** works without M14).\\n13. **Negative:** REST `MessageObj` / `UserObj` responses still must **not** include `seq`.\\n14. **Negative:** must **not** require Redis for subscribe/resume/seq allocation (Redis may be unused).\\n15. **Negative:** must **not** implement Redis fan-out or IRC in this task.\\n16. Unauthorized subscribe returns an `error` frame and does **not** attach the subscription.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Automated (`tests/test_ws.py` + adjustments)\\n\\n- Auth reject paths (no token, bad token).\\n- Subscribe happy path + forbidden/not_found.\\n- Dense seq: create 3 messages → seqs 1,2,3; resume from 1 → events 2,3 + resumed.\\n- Gap: insert \\u003e`CHANNEL_EVENT_RETAIN` events (or temporarily lower retain in test) → resume from 0 → `resume.gap`.\\n- Reaction / delete / membership / channel.updated smoke.\\n- `user.updated` global delivery.\\n- Cross-node resume: two `create_app` sharing temp sqlite (pattern from auth cluster tests) — write via app A, resume via WS on app B.\\n- Keep `tests/test_messages.py` assertion: `\\\"seq\\\" not in msg`.\\n- Keep profiles test: published user.updated has no seq/channel_id.\\n\\n### Manual / cluster\\n\\n1. Boot `./start.sh`.\\n2. Register/login; create workspace/channel; open websocat/wscat to `:8000/api/ws?token=…`.\\n3. `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"subscribe\\\",\\\"channel_id\\\":\\\"…\\\"}` → note `head_seq`.\\n4. POST a message via curl; observe `message.created` with `seq`.\\n5. Kill WS; reconnect to `:8001`; `resume` with last seq → catch-up.\\n6. PATCH profile; observe `user.updated` on an open socket.\\n\\n### Out of test scope here\\n\\n- Redis down behavior (M14).\\n- IRC parity (M15).\\n- SPA selectors (M17).\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"Design complete for WS subscribe/resume + dense channel seq. Key decisions: SQLite channel_seq/channel_events (v6) as SoT; seq allocated in same txn as mutation; /api/ws?token=; subscribe=live only, resume=replay or resume.gap; user.updated global no seq; Redis fan-out deferred to MARATHON-14 (local hub + catch-up on any node via resume). Label remains backend for implementer after architect approval.\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:29.968254993Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-23T01:31:46.235451662Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"ws://host/api/ws?token= bearer. Client: subscribe, resume with since_seq. Server: subscribed/resumed with head_seq; resume.gap if since_seq older than retained tail. Durable per-channel frames {type, seq, channel_id, ...} for message/reply/reaction/membership/channel mutations. seq dense per-channel (+1 per durable event, no gaps/duplicates). Profile updates: {type:user.updated,user} globally without channel_id/seq. Same seq visible across all HTTP nodes (fan-out task will complete cross-node).\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-14\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-13\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Cross-node fan-out and Redis-outage resilience\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:29.991315274Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-15\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-13\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"IRC gateway on :6667 with bidirectional bridge\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:47.161Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 57,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-13\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"DESIGN-AUTO-APPROVED pass=29\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T01:31:46.291233893Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n/work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1\ntotal 40\ndrwxr-xr-x.  9 root root 4096 Aug 23 01:32 .\ndrwxr-xr-x.  6 root root   93 Aug 22 22:15 ..\n-rw-------.  1 root root  265 Aug 23 01:32 .agent.lock\n-rw-------.  1 root root    0 Aug 22 22:23 .agent.lock.flock\n-rw-r--r--.  1 root root   42 Aug 22 22:15 .git\n-rw-r--r--.  1 root root  229 Aug 22 22:24 .gitignore\ndrwx------.  3 root root   70 Aug 22 22:25 .pytest_cache\ndrwx------.  5 root root  101 Aug 22 22:27 .venv\ndrwx------.  5 root root   64 Aug 23 01:16 data\ndrwxr-xr-x.  2 root root   33 Aug 22 22:15 loom-prompts\n-rw-------.  1 root root  119 Aug 22 22:23 requirements.txt\ndrwx------. 11 root root 4096 Aug 23 01:00 server\n-rwx------.  1 root root 4973 Aug 22 22:27 start.sh\ndrwx------.  4 root root   45 Aug 23 01:15 static\ndrwx------.  3 root root 4096 Aug 23 01:15 tests\n-rwxr-xr-x.  1 root root  558 Aug 22 22:15 timer.sh\n","localExecutionTimeMs":65},"isBackground":false},"description":"Merge main and load task/epic data"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-4404e6c3-6678-4c75-b41a-18bb29c6784c-0\nfc_afb8bac5-0659-9a69-8570-9a09c09